4, "end": 638.52, "text": " for massive binary blobs so fliction uses this friction to teach the concept of the manifest okay explain", "tokens": [50977, 337, 5994, 17434, 1749, 929, 370, 932, 4105, 4960, 341, 17710, 281, 2924, 264, 3410, 295, 264, 10067, 1392, 2903, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04626204208894209, "compression_ratio": 1.6586345381526104, "no_speech_prob": 3.3571975494722794e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 61900, "start": 638.52, "end": 645.08, "text": " the manifest instead of committing the seven gigabyte model itself you commit a cryptographic hash of the", "tokens": [51341, 264, 10067, 2602, 295, 26659, 264, 3407, 8741, 34529, 2316, 2564, 291, 5599, 257, 9844, 12295, 22019, 295, 264, 51669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04626204208894209, "compression_ratio": 1.6586345381526104, "no_speech_prob": 3.3571975494722794e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 64508, "start": 645.08, "end": 651.8000000000001, "text": " model and the exact script required to download it from a remote blob store you separate the identity", "tokens": [50365, 2316, 293, 264, 1900, 5755, 4739, 281, 5484, 309, 490, 257, 8607, 46115, 3531, 291, 4994, 264, 6575, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06033994450288661, "compression_ratio": 1.7679324894514767, "no_speech_prob": 3.978372752760917e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 64508, "start": 651.8000000000001, "end": 657.48, "text": " of the asset from the actual bytes of the asset so you record the recipe not the meal itself exactly", "tokens": [50701, 295, 264, 11999, 490, 264, 3539, 36088, 295, 264, 11999, 370, 291, 2136, 264, 6782, 406, 264, 6791, 2564, 2293, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06033994450288661, "compression_ratio": 1.7679324894514767, "no_speech_prob": 3.978372752760917e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 64508, "start": 657.48, "end": 663.32, "text": " but to really understand why git fails with massive binary files volume 2 takes you underneath the hood", "tokens": [50985, 457, 281, 534, 1223, 9