 "start": 795.8000000000001, "end": 802.04, "text": " before it the author's name and the commit message so a commit points to a tree a tree points to blobs", "tokens": [51481, 949, 309, 264, 3793, 311, 1315, 293, 264, 5599, 3636, 370, 257, 5599, 2793, 281, 257, 4230, 257, 4230, 2793, 281, 1749, 929, 51793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04212179103819262, "compression_ratio": 1.9575289575289576, "no_speech_prob": 1.935183350371128e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 80204, "start": 802.04, "end": 806.8399999999999, "text": " and blobs hold the data this explains why fliction makes the student do something that just sounds", "tokens": [50365, 293, 1749, 929, 1797, 264, 1412, 341, 13948, 983, 932, 4105, 1669, 264, 3107, 360, 746, 300, 445, 3263, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061013189951578777, "compression_ratio": 1.9450980392156862, "no_speech_prob": 2.218682052315679e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 80204, "start": 806.8399999999999, "end": 811.48, "text": " like absolute torture oh you mean the hand constructed commit yes there's an exercise", "tokens": [50605, 411, 8236, 20711, 1954, 291, 914, 264, 1011, 17083, 5599, 2086, 456, 311, 364, 5380, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061013189951578777, "compression_ratio": 1.9450980392156862, "no_speech_prob": 2.218682052315679e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 80204, "start": 811.48, "end": 817.4, "text": " where you have to construct the commit entirely by hand you never get add or git commit right you use", "tokens": [50837, 689, 291, 362, 281, 7690, 264, 5599, 7696, 538, 1011, 291, 1128, 483, 909, 420, 18331, 5599, 558, 291, 764, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061013189951578777, "compression_ratio": 1.9450980392156862, "no_speech_prob": 2.218682052315679e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 80204, "start": 817.4, "end": 824.1999999999999, "text": " git hash object to manually write the blob to the database then you use git update index and git write", "tokens": [51133, 18331, 22019, 2657, 281, 1694