3, "no_speech_prob": 3.0667465095168822e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 83076, "start": 847.48, "end": 853.72, "text": " incredibly rigid content addressable database a branch isn't a folder containing a copy of your project", "tokens": [51201, 6252, 22195, 2701, 2985, 712, 8149, 257, 9819, 1943, 380, 257, 10820, 19273, 257, 5055, 295, 428, 1716, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04993683792823969, "compression_ratio": 1.6804979253112033, "no_speech_prob": 3.0667465095168822e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 85372, "start": 853.72, "end": 860.84, "text": " no a branch is literally just a tiny text file sitting your dot git slash refs directory containing", "tokens": [50365, 572, 257, 9819, 307, 3736, 445, 257, 5870, 2487, 3991, 3798, 428, 5893, 18331, 17330, 1895, 82, 21120, 19273, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04637258743571344, "compression_ratio": 1.8689138576779025, "no_speech_prob": 2.352908232833295e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 85372, "start": 860.84, "end": 865.4, "text": " a 40 character screen that points to a commit it fundamentally changes how you view operations", "tokens": [50721, 257, 3356, 2517, 2568, 300, 2793, 281, 257, 5599, 309, 17879, 2962, 577, 291, 1910, 7705, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04637258743571344, "compression_ratio": 1.8689138576779025, "no_speech_prob": 2.352908232833295e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 85372, "start": 866.0400000000001, "end": 871.1600000000001, "text": " checking out a branch isn't switching folders it's telling git look at the commit this branch points to", "tokens": [50981, 8568, 484, 257, 9819, 1943, 380, 16493, 31082, 309, 311, 3585, 18331, 574, 412, 264, 5599, 341, 9819, 2793, 281, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04637258743571344, "compression_ratio": 1.8689138576779025, "no_speech_prob": 2.352908232833295e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 85372, "start": 871.1600000000001, "end": 876.2, "text": " look at the tree that commit points to look at the blobs that tree points to and inflate those blobs", "tokens": [51237, 574, 412, 264, 4230, 300, 5599, 2793, 281, 574, 412, 264, 1749, 929, 300, 4230, 2793, 281, 293, 9922, 473, 729, 1749, 929, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04637258743571344, "compression_ratio": 1.8689138576779025, "no_speech_prob": 2.352908232833295e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 85372, "start": 876.2, "end": 882.44, "text": " into my working directory and once you grasp that mechanical reality moving into section two of the", "tokens": [51489, 666, 452, 1364, 21120, 293, 1564, 291, 21743, 300, 12070, 4103, 2684, 666, 3541, 732, 295, 264, 51801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.04637258743571344, "compression_ratio": 1.8689138576779025, "no_speech_prob": 2.352908232833295e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 88244, "start": 882.44, "end": 888.2, "text": " curriculum which is volumes three and four it feels entirely different because if git is just a chain", "tokens": [50365, 14302, 597, 307, 22219, 1045, 293, 1451, 309, 3417, 7696, 819, 570, 498, 18331, 307, 445, 257, 5021, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03866912657956043, "compression_ratio": 1.6721311475409837, "no_speech_prob": 2.6861082802476233e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 88244, "start": 888.2, "end": 893.5600000000001, "text": " of cryptographic objects pointing to one another you suddenly realize those chains can split they can", "tokens": [50653, 295, 9844, 12295, 6565, 12166, 281, 472, 1071, 291, 5800, 4325, 729, 12626, 393, 7472, 436, 393, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03866912657956043, "compression_ratio": 1.6721311475409837, "no_speech_prob": 2.6861082802476233e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 88244, "start": 893.5600000000001, "end": 899.4000000000001, "text": " weave together and they can break the graph is no longer a timeline it becomes a geometric space", "tokens": [50921, 29145, 1214, 293, 436, 393, 1821, 264, 4295, 307, 572, 2854, 257, 12933, 309, 3643, 257, 33246, 1901, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03866912657956043, "compression_ratio": 1.6721311475409837, "no_speech_prob": 2.6861082802476233e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 88244, "start": 900.2, "end": 907.24, "text": " volume three is actually aptly named the geometry of git we shipped applications again here right now we're", "tokens": [51253, 5523, 1045, 307, 767, 29427, 356, 4926, 264, 18426, 295, 18331, 321, 25312, 5821, 797, 510, 558, 586, 321, 434, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03866912657956043, "compression_ratio": 1.6721311475409837, "no_speech_prob": 2.6861082802476233e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 90724, "start": 907.24, "end": 913.48, "text": " managing an alama and granite research assistant basically a local ai text summarizer the student's", "tokens": [50365, 11642, 364, 419, 2404, 293, 9370, 642, 2132, 10994, 1936, 257, 2654, 9783, 2487, 14611, 6545, 264, 3107, 311, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03467625379562378, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 3.6299585299409687e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 90724, "start": 913.48, "end": 919.48, "text": " task is to test out radically different summarization strategies yeah so one branch might use fixed chunking", "tokens": [50677, 5633, 307, 281, 1500, 484, 35508, 819, 14611, 2144, 9029, 1338, 370, 472, 9819, 1062, 764, 6806, 16635, 278, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03467625379562378, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 3.6299585299409687e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 90724, "start": 919.48, "end": 925.16, "text": " cutting the text every 500 words another branch uses semantic sectioning analyzing paragraph breaks", "tokens": [50977, 6492, 264, 2487, 633, 5923, 2283, 1071, 9819, 4960, 47982, 3541, 278, 23663, 18865, 9857, 51261], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03467625379562378, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 3.6299585299409687e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 90724, "start": 925.16, "end": 930.28, "text": " and branches are no longer introduced the way we were all taught as like a copy of your workspace right", "tokens": [51261, 293, 14770, 366, 572, 2854, 7268, 264, 636, 321, 645, 439, 5928, 382, 411, 257, 5055, 295, 428, 32706, 558, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03467625379562378, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 3.6299585299409687e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 90724, "start": 930.28, "end": 935.08, "text": " they're introduced as literal historical representations of genuine competing hypotheses", "tokens": [51517, 436, 434, 7268, 382, 20411, 8584, 33358, 295, 16699, 15439, 49969, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03467625379562378, "compression_ratio": 1.6925675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 3.6299585299409687e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 93508, "start": 935.08, "end": 941.32, "text": " i am trying an idea in this geometric space and you are trying a completely different idea in a parallel space", "tokens": [50365, 741, 669, 1382, 364, 1558, 294, 341, 33246, 1901, 293, 291, 366, 1382, 257, 2584, 819, 1558, 294, 257, 8952, 1901, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13473518773129112, "compression_ratio": 1.7950819672131149, "no_speech_prob": 2.9163334074044922e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 93508, "start": 941.32, "end": 948.5200000000001, "text": " and this requires understanding ancestry as a mathematical relation if we view the repository as a directed", "tokens": [50677, 293, 341, 7029, 3701, 44729, 382, 257, 18894, 9721, 498, 321, 1910, 264, 25841, 382, 257, 12898, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13473518773129112, "compression_ratio": 1.7950819672131149, "no_speech_prob": 2.9163334074044922e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 93508, "start": 948.5200000000001, "end": 957.4000000000001, "text": " auslick graph a dag ancestry is strict if commit a is an ancestor of commit b it means there is an unbroken", "tokens": [51037, 3437, 75, 618, 4295, 257, 15460, 44729, 307, 10910, 498, 5599, 257, 307, 364, 40032, 295, 5599, 272, 309, 1355, 456, 307, 364, 517, 37947, 51481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13473518773129112, "compression_ratio": 1.7950819672131149, "no_speech_prob": 2.9163334074044922e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 93508, "start": 957.4000000000001, "end": 964.44, "text": " chain of parent pointers from b back to a therefore b contains the entire history of a exactly so when you want", "tokens": [51481, 5021, 295, 2596, 44548, 490, 272, 646, 281, 257, 4412, 272, 8306, 264, 2302, 2503, 295, 257, 2293, 370, 562, 291, 528, 51833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13473518773129112, "compression_ratio": 1.7950819672131149, "no_speech_prob": 2.9163334074044922e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 96444, "start": 964.44, "end": 970.12, "text": " to combine two competing hypotheses git has to calculate the geometry between them which brings up the", "tokens": [50365, 281, 10432, 732, 15439, 49969, 18331, 575, 281, 8873, 264, 18426, 1296, 552, 597, 5607, 493, 264, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.02603249460737282, "compression_ratio": 1.8216783216783217, "no_speech_prob": 2.2317315096637147e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 96444, "start": 970.12, "end": 974.6, "text": " concept of the merge base which i feel like nobody ever talks about yeah but it's literally the engine", "tokens": [50649, 3410, 295, 264, 22183, 3096, 597, 741, 841, 411, 5079, 1562, 6686, 466, 1338, 457, 309, 311, 3736, 264, 2848, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.02603249460737282, "compression_ratio": 1.8216783216783217, "no_speech_prob": 2.2317315096637147e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 96444, "start": 974.6, "end": 981.8000000000001, "text": " that runs every collaboration it is arguably the most important calculation git performs if you have your", "tokens": [50873, 300, 6676, 633, 9363, 309, 307, 26771, 264, 881, 1021, 17108, 18331, 26213, 498, 291, 362, 428, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.02603249460737282, "compression_ratio": 1.8216783216783217, "no_speech_prob": 2.2317315096637147e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 96444, "start": 981.8000000000001, "end": 986.6, "text": " feature branch and i have the main branch and we want to merge git doesn't just smash the files together", "tokens": [51233, 4111, 9819, 293, 741, 362, 264, 2135, 9819, 293, 321, 528, 281, 22183, 18331, 1177, 380, 445, 17960, 264, 7098, 1214, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.02603249460737282, "compression_ratio": 1.8216783216783217, "no_speech_prob": 2.2317315096637147e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 96444, "start": 986.6, "end": 992.12, "text": " no it traverses the graph backward from your branch and backward from my branch until it finds the exact", "tokens": [51473, 572, 309, 23149, 279, 264, 4295, 23897, 490, 428, 9819, 293, 23897, 490, 452, 9819, 1826, 309, 10704, 264, 1900, 51749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.02603249460737282, "compression_ratio": 1.8216783216783217, "no_speech_prob": 2.2317315096637147e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 99212, "start": 992.12, "end": 997.64, "text": " commit where our histories diverged that is the lowest common ancestor the merge base so git does a", "tokens": [50365, 5599, 689, 527, 30631, 18558, 3004, 300, 307, 264, 12437, 2689, 40032, 264, 22183, 3096, 370, 18331, 775, 257, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03904474921848463, "compression_ratio": 2.004, "no_speech_prob": 2.494912479736322e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 99212, "start": 997.64, "end": 1001.88, "text": " three-way merge it looks at the merge base it looks at your branch and it looks at my branch", "tokens": [50641, 1045, 12, 676, 22183, 309, 1542, 412, 264, 22183, 3096, 309, 1542, 412, 428, 9819, 293, 309, 1542, 412, 452, 9819, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03904474921848463, "compression_ratio": 2.004, "no_speech_prob": 2.494912479736322e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 99212, "start": 1001.88, "end": 1008.2, "text": " so if a file was untouched on my branch but you changed it on yours git knows it can safely apply", "tokens": [50853, 370, 498, 257, 3991, 390, 1701, 36740, 322, 452, 9819, 457, 291, 3105, 309, 322, 6342, 18331, 3255, 309, 393, 11750, 3079, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03904474921848463, "compression_ratio": 2.004, "no_speech_prob": 2.494912479736322e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 99212, "start": 1008.2, "end": 1013.5600000000001, "text": " your change because it compares it to that merge base right but what if our branches never diverged in the", "tokens": [51169, 428, 1319, 570, 309, 38334, 309, 281, 300, 22183, 3096, 558, 457, 437, 498, 527, 14770, 1128, 18558, 3004, 294, 264, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03904474921848463, "compression_ratio": 2.004, "no_speech_prob": 2.494912479736322e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 99212, "start": 1013.5600000000001, "end": 1019.32, "text": " first place what if i branched off main made three commits and nobody else touched main in the meantime", "tokens": [51437, 700, 1081, 437, 498, 741, 9819, 292, 766, 2135, 1027, 1045, 48311, 293, 5079, 1646, 9828, 2135, 294, 264, 14991, 51725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03904474921848463, "compression_ratio": 2.004, "no_speech_prob": 2.494912479736322e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 101932, "start": 1019.32, "end": 1025.56, "text": " oh then when i go to merge git calculates the merge base and realizes the merge base is the current", "tokens": [50365, 1954, 550, 562, 741, 352, 281, 22183, 18331, 4322, 1024, 264, 22183, 3096, 293, 29316, 264, 22183, 3096, 307, 264, 2190, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03664078712463379, "compression_ratio": 1.7991071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 3.0391938965479426e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 101932, "start": 1026.28, "end": 1032.68, "text": " tip of main in that case no three-way merge is needed at all git just performs a fast forward it", "tokens": [50713, 4125, 295, 2135, 294, 300, 1389, 572, 1045, 12, 676, 22183, 307, 2978, 412, 439, 18331, 445, 26213, 257, 2370, 2128, 309, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03664078712463379, "compression_ratio": 1.7991071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 3.0391938965479426e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 101932, "start": 1032.68, "end": 1037.64, "text": " literally just takes the main branch pointer and slides it up the graph to point to your new commit", "tokens": [51033, 3736, 445, 2516, 264, 2135, 9819, 23918, 293, 9788, 309, 493, 264, 4295, 281, 935, 281, 428, 777, 5599, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03664078712463379, "compression_ratio": 1.7991071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 3.0391938965479426e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 101932, "start": 1037.64, "end": 1044.52, "text": " the geometry is perfectly linear flexion forces the student to trace these geometries visually which helps", "tokens": [51281, 264, 18426, 307, 6239, 8213, 5896, 313, 5874, 264, 3107, 281, 13508, 613, 12956, 2244, 19622, 597, 3665, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03664078712463379, "compression_ratio": 1.7991071428571428, "no_speech_prob": 3.0391938965479426e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 104452, "start": 1044.52, "end": 1050.92, "text": " so much and then the curriculum introduces the octopus merge which sounds like a cryptid but is", "tokens": [50365, 370, 709, 293, 550, 264, 14302, 31472, 264, 27962, 22183, 597, 3263, 411, 257, 9844, 327, 457, 307, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.027880904766229484, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7685207681986115e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 104452, "start": 1050.92, "end": 1055.72, "text": " actually a fundamental feature yeah an octopus merge is just merging more than two branches at the exact", "tokens": [50685, 767, 257, 8088, 4111, 1338, 364, 27962, 22183, 307, 445, 44559, 544, 813, 732, 14770, 412, 264, 1900, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.027880904766229484, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7685207681986115e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 104452, "start": 1055.72, "end": 1060.76, "text": " same time instead of a commit having two parents it might have three or four or eight it's tying", "tokens": [50925, 912, 565, 2602, 295, 257, 5599, 1419, 732, 3152, 309, 1062, 362, 1045, 420, 1451, 420, 3180, 309, 311, 32405, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.027880904766229484, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7685207681986115e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 104452, "start": 1060.76, "end": 1067.16, "text": " multiple independent hypotheses into a single knot but talking about tying knots brings up like the most", "tokens": [51177, 3866, 6695, 49969, 666, 257, 2167, 16966, 457, 1417, 466, 32405, 27426, 5607, 493, 411, 264, 881, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.027880904766229484, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7685207681986115e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 104452, "start": 1067.16, "end": 1072.36, "text": " hotly debated topic in software engineering you go on reddit you go on hacker news and people", "tokens": [51497, 2368, 356, 42212, 4829, 294, 4722, 7043, 291, 352, 322, 2182, 17975, 291, 352, 322, 38155, 2583, 293, 561, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.027880904766229484, "compression_ratio": 1.7464788732394365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7685207681986115e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 107236, "start": 1072.36, "end": 1080.9199999999998, "text": " treat the merge versus rebase debate like a literal religious war oh absolutely and the intensity of", "tokens": [50365, 2387, 264, 22183, 5717, 12970, 651, 7958, 411, 257, 20411, 7185, 1516, 1954, 3122, 293, 264, 13749, 295, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0679012094990591, "compression_ratio": 1.726530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 2.227362608589467e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 107236, "start": 1080.9199999999998, "end": 1086.6799999999998, "text": " that debate stems from a misunderstanding of what a rebase actually is people argue about it as if it's a", "tokens": [50793, 300, 7958, 27600, 490, 257, 29227, 295, 437, 257, 12970, 651, 767, 307, 561, 9695, 466, 309, 382, 498, 309, 311, 257, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0679012094990591, "compression_ratio": 1.726530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 2.227362608589467e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 107236, "start": 1086.6799999999998, "end": 1093.08, "text": " moral question you know like should we preserve the messy truth of history or should we present a clean", "tokens": [51081, 9723, 1168, 291, 458, 411, 820, 321, 15665, 264, 16191, 3494, 295, 2503, 420, 820, 321, 1974, 257, 2541, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0679012094990591, "compression_ratio": 1.726530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 2.227362608589467e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 107236, "start": 1093.08, "end": 1099.9599999999998, "text": " linear narrative but flick chain neutralizes the religious war by framing it purely geometrically exactly so how", "tokens": [51401, 8213, 9977, 457, 22774, 5021, 10598, 5660, 264, 7185, 1516, 538, 28971, 309, 17491, 12956, 81, 984, 2293, 370, 577, 51745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0679012094990591, "compression_ratio": 1.726530612244898, "no_speech_prob": 2.227362608589467e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 109996, "start": 1099.96, "end": 1105.24, "text": " does a rebase actually work geometrically if a merge creates a new knot tying two branches together", "tokens": [50365, 775, 257, 12970, 651, 767, 589, 12956, 81, 984, 498, 257, 22183, 7829, 257, 777, 16966, 32405, 732, 14770, 1214, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07152923784757916, "compression_ratio": 1.7986111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251533077389697e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 109996, "start": 1105.24, "end": 1111.56, "text": " what does a rebase do rebase reconstructs history based on a hypothetical question let's say you", "tokens": [50629, 437, 775, 257, 12970, 651, 360, 12970, 651, 31499, 82, 2503, 2361, 322, 257, 33053, 1168, 718, 311, 584, 291, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07152923784757916, "compression_ratio": 1.7986111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251533077389697e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 109996, "start": 1111.56, "end": 1116.92, "