atically, enforcing contextual integrity. We watched a Perl script brilliantly satirize the dangerous, highly consequential gap between procedural determinism and actual justified legitimacy. And we explored how a Rust program separates an immutable, append-only documentary history from the highly selective, narrowly defined, operative reality we actually experience. It provides us with a totally new, highly rigorous vocabulary for analyzing the digital infrastructure around us. The next time you interact with a corporate workflow tool that grays out the submit button, or a banking app that denies a transfer, or a social media platform that silently quarantines a post, you can dissect the interaction. You can ask yourself, which specific mathematical boundary did I just hit? Was it an ingress failure where my signal was never even recognized? Or was my proposal formally recorded, judged against a hidden policy bundle, and denied continuation? And crucially, where does that system keep the documentary record of that refusal? Exactly. It completely changes how you see the invisible walls of the internet. And before we wrap up this deep dive, I want to leave you with one final, slightly chilling thought to mull over. Oh, here we go. It's an extrapolation that builds directly on Fluxian's architecture, but points toward our immediate future. We've established today, mathematically and conceptually, that rejected proposals remain incredibly valuable as structural evidence. The graveyard of refusals maps the exact boundaries of what a system considers an acceptable reality. The refusals define the perimeter of the continuation space. Right. So, if our modern, hyper-skilled software systems are unconditionally recording every single rejected proposal, every malformed request, every denied loan application, every quarantined message, every behavioral outlier that the system flagged and stopped. They are building an unimaginably massive archive of failed continuations. Okay. I see where you're going with this. How long until massive AI systems start looking at that documentary history of refusals, not just as static audit evidence, but as primary high-value training data? It fundamentally shifts the training paradigm. Instead of learning how to mimic successful outputs, a model trained on the documentary history of refusals learns the exact contour of institutional boundaries. It learns exactly what the system fears, what it rejects, and how it defines an invalid reality. Exactly. And what happens when a machine learning model, trained on billions of meticulous rejections, begins to autonomously update the policy bundles? What happens when it uses that massive graveyard of failed continuations to redefine the rules of the ingress operator itself? When the machine learns more from our refusals than our successes, who is really setting the boundaries of the continuation space? When the AI decides what even constitutes a well-formed proposal, it gains the power to decide what parts of human behavior are allowed to exist in the digital record at all. It's the ultimate centralization of the ingress operator. The system wouldn't just be governing the operative reality, it would be preemptively defining the limits of existence. Think about all those things your computer almost did, those denied requests, those blocked actions, those silent refusals. They aren't gone. They are sitting in the documentary history, mapping the edges of our reality, just waiting in the margins. Until next time, thanks for taking the deep dive with us.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 4.72, "text": " Have you ever thought about what happens to all the things your computer, you know, almost did?", "tokens": [50365, 3560, 291, 1562, 1194, 466, 437, 2314, 281, 439, 264, 721, 428, 3820, 11, 291, 458, 11, 1920, 630, 30, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434025891059268, "compression_ratio": 1.5800711743772242, "no_speech_prob": 9.21532706914252e-13}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 4.84, "end": 6.5600000000000005, "text": " Oh, that is such a good question.", "tokens": [50607, 876, 11, 300, 307, 1270, 257, 665, 1168, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434025891059268, "compression_ratio": 1.5800711743772242, "no_speech_prob": 9.21532706914252e-13}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 6.9, "end": 10.620000000000001, "text": " Right. Because we spend so much time analyzing execution.", "tokens": [50710, 1779, 13, 1436, 321, 3496, 370, 709, 565, 23663, 15058, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434025891059268, "compression_ratio": 1.5800711743772242, "no_speech_prob": 9.21532706914252e-13}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 11.14, "end": 13.200000000000001, "text": " We completely obsess over the output.", "tokens": [50922, 492, 2584, 35803, 670, 264, 5598, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434025891059268, "compression_ratio": 1.5800711743772242, "no_speech_prob": 9.21532706914252e-13}, {"id": 4, "seek": 0, "start": 13.36, "end": 15.44, "text": " Yeah, the rendered page, the database query.", "tokens": [51033, 865, 11, 264, 28748, 3028, 11, 264, 8149, 14581, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434025891059268, "compression_ratio": 1.5800711743772242, "no_speech_prob": 9.21532706914252e-13}, {"id": 5, "seek": 0, "start": 15.66, "end": 17.18, "text": " Exactly, the final compiled binary.", "tokens": [51148, 7587, 11, 264, 2572, 36548, 17434, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434025891059268, "compression_ratio": 1.5800711743772242, "no_speech_prob": 9.21532706914252e-13}, {"id": 6, "seek": 0, "start": 17.72, "end": 21.02, "text": " But if you actually look at the lifecycle of any complex system,", "tokens": [51251, 583, 498, 291, 767, 574, 412, 264, 45722, 295, 604, 3997, 1185, 11, 51416], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434025891059268, "compression_ratio": 1.5800711743772242, "no_speech_prob": 9.21532706914252e-13}, {"id": 7, "seek": 0, "start": 21.34, "end": 26.22, "text": " execution is just this tiny, tiny fraction of its reality.", "tokens": [51432, 15058, 307, 445, 341, 5870, 11, 5870, 14135, 295, 1080, 4103, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434025891059268, "compression_ratio": 1.5800711743772242, "no_speech_prob": 9.21532706914252e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 0, "start": 26.36, "end": 27.14, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51683, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1434025891059268, "compression_ratio": 1.5800711743772242, "no_speech_prob": 9.21532706914252e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 2714, "start": 27.14, "end": 29.900000000000002, "text": " Every blocked pop-up, every dropped network packet,", "tokens": [50365, 2048, 15470, 1665, 12, 1010, 11, 633, 8119, 3209, 20300, 11, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552773369683158, "compression_ratio": 1.57439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 6.794957933993484e-13}, {"id": 10, "seek": 2714, "start": 30.380000000000003, "end": 34.38, "text": " every API request that gets rejected because of some, like, malformed header,", "tokens": [50527, 633, 9362, 5308, 300, 2170, 15749, 570, 295, 512, 11, 411, 11, 2806, 22892, 23117, 11, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552773369683158, "compression_ratio": 1.57439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 6.794957933993484e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 2714, "start": 35.54, "end": 36.64, "text": " these aren't just errors.", "tokens": [50785, 613, 3212, 380, 445, 13603, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552773369683158, "compression_ratio": 1.57439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 6.794957933993484e-13}, {"id": 12, "seek": 2714, "start": 36.88, "end": 37.6, "text": " No, they're not.", "tokens": [50852, 883, 11, 436, 434, 406, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552773369683158, "compression_ratio": 1.57439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 6.794957933993484e-13}, {"id": 13, "seek": 2714, "start": 37.72, "end": 43.36, "text": " They are proposed happenings that the system actively decided to quarantine or just straight-up destroy.", "tokens": [50894, 814, 366, 10348, 1051, 1109, 300, 264, 1185, 13022, 3047, 281, 18138, 420, 445, 2997, 12, 1010, 5293, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552773369683158, "compression_ratio": 1.57439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 6.794957933993484e-13}, {"id": 14, "seek": 2714, "start": 43.64, "end": 43.88, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51190, 865, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552773369683158, "compression_ratio": 1.57439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 6.794957933993484e-13}, {"id": 15, "seek": 2714, "start": 44.28, "end": 49.24, "text": " And when we look at software strictly as this engine of doing, we miss its primary function.", "tokens": [51222, 400, 562, 321, 574, 412, 4722, 20792, 382, 341, 2848, 295, 884, 11, 321, 1713, 1080, 6194, 2445, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552773369683158, "compression_ratio": 1.57439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 6.794957933993484e-13}, {"id": 16, "seek": 2714, "start": 49.72, "end": 51.92, "text": " Software is fundamentally a gatekeeper.", "tokens": [51494, 27428, 307, 17879, 257, 8539, 23083, 13, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552773369683158, "compression_ratio": 1.57439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 6.794957933993484e-13}, {"id": 17, "seek": 2714, "start": 52.120000000000005, "end": 53.78, "text": " It is a gatekeeper. That's exactly it.", "tokens": [51614, 467, 307, 257, 8539, 23083, 13, 663, 311, 2293, 309, 13, 51697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14552773369683158, "compression_ratio": 1.57439446366782, "no_speech_prob": 6.794957933993484e-13}, {"id": 18, "seek": 5378, "start": 53.78, "end": 61.34, "text": " It spends the vast majority of its computational energy just deciding which proposed realities are allowed to cross the threshold into actual reality.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 25620, 264, 8369, 6286, 295, 1080, 28270, 2281, 445, 17990, 597, 10348, 27785, 366, 4350, 281, 3278, 264, 14678, 666, 3539, 4103, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284280518690745, "compression_ratio": 1.462962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.335457677602292e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 5378, "start": 61.34, "end": 67.32000000000001, "text": " And that concept, it forces a total reorientation of how we view digital architecture.", "tokens": [50743, 400, 300, 3410, 11, 309, 5874, 257, 3217, 319, 19521, 399, 295, 577, 321, 1910, 4562, 9482, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284280518690745, "compression_ratio": 1.462962962962963, "no_speech_prob": 1.335457677602292e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 6732, "start": 67.32, "end": 71.0, "text": " I mean, the successful outputs are just the survivors.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 264, 4406, 23930, 366, 445, 264, 18369, 13, 50549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261509043829781, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.626073949968776e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 6732, "start": 71.22, "end": 72.0, "text": " The survivors, yeah.", "tokens": [50560, 440, 18369, 11, 1338, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261509043829781, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.626073949968776e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 6732, "start": 72.19999999999999, "end": 77.22, "text": " If you want to understand the true shape and governance of a system, you have to look at its refusals.", "tokens": [50609, 759, 291, 528, 281, 1223, 264, 2074, 3909, 293, 17449, 295, 257, 1185, 11, 291, 362, 281, 574, 412, 1080, 1895, 301, 1124, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261509043829781, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.626073949968776e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 6732, "start": 77.61999999999999, "end": 84.63999999999999, "text": " The boundaries of any digital environment are defined entirely by that invisible scaffolding of failed attempts.", "tokens": [50880, 440, 13180, 295, 604, 4562, 2823, 366, 7642, 7696, 538, 300, 14603, 44094, 278, 295, 7612, 15257, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261509043829781, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.626073949968776e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 6732, "start": 84.78, "end": 89.85999999999999, "text": " But because those refusals rarely generate a user-facing event, we just treat them as ephemeral.", "tokens": [51238, 583, 570, 729, 1895, 301, 1124, 13752, 8460, 257, 4195, 12, 44046, 2280, 11, 321, 445, 2387, 552, 382, 308, 41245, 2790, 13, 51492], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261509043829781, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.626073949968776e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 6732, "start": 90.13999999999999, "end": 92.52, "text": " Like, we treat them as if they never existed at all.", "tokens": [51506, 1743, 11, 321, 2387, 552, 382, 498, 436, 1128, 13135, 412, 439, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261509043829781, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.626073949968776e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 6732, "start": 92.6, "end": 92.88, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51629, 1779, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12261509043829781, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.626073949968776e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 9288, "start": 92.88, "end": 94.56, "text": " They just vanish into the void.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 445, 43584, 666, 264, 22009, 13, 50449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13145208740234374, "compression_ratio": 1.5527156549520766, "no_speech_prob": 2.1340067300062993e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 9288, "start": 94.75999999999999, "end": 98.64, "text": " And that hidden graveyard of refusals is exactly what we are exploring today.", "tokens": [50459, 400, 300, 7633, 42607, 295, 1895, 301, 1124, 307, 2293, 437, 321, 366, 12736, 965, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13145208740234374, "compression_ratio": 1.5527156549520766, "no_speech_prob": 2.1340067300062993e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 9288, "start": 98.89999999999999, "end": 104.16, "text": " We're doing a deep dive into a frankly brilliant 2026 paper by Flixion.", "tokens": [50666, 492, 434, 884, 257, 2452, 9192, 666, 257, 11939, 10248, 945, 10880, 3035, 538, 3235, 970, 313, 13, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13145208740234374, "compression_ratio": 1.5527156549520766, "no_speech_prob": 2.1340067300062993e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 9288, "start": 104.39999999999999, "end": 105.88, "text": " Oh, this paper is fantastic.", "tokens": [50941, 876, 11, 341, 3035, 307, 5456, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13145208740234374, "compression_ratio": 1.5527156549520766, "no_speech_prob": 2.1340067300062993e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 9288, "start": 106.19999999999999, "end": 106.69999999999999, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51031, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13145208740234374, "compression_ratio": 1.5527156549520766, "no_speech_prob": 2.1340067300062993e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 9288, "start": 106.75999999999999, "end": 110.03999999999999, "text": " It's titled Selective Continuation in Three Small Programs.", "tokens": [51059, 467, 311, 19841, 13638, 488, 14674, 16073, 294, 6244, 15287, 44762, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13145208740234374, "compression_ratio": 1.5527156549520766, "no_speech_prob": 2.1340067300062993e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 9288, "start": 110.5, "end": 112.89999999999999, "text": " Proposal, Record, Admission, and History.", "tokens": [51246, 21944, 329, 304, 11, 27401, 11, 1999, 29797, 11, 293, 12486, 13, 51366], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13145208740234374, "compression_ratio": 1.5527156549520766, "no_speech_prob": 2.1340067300062993e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 9288, "start": 113.28, "end": 122.19999999999999, "text": " And what makes this paper so compelling to me is that Flixion doesn't try to prove these concepts by analyzing some massive, sprawling enterprise architecture.", "tokens": [51385, 400, 437, 1669, 341, 3035, 370, 20050, 281, 385, 307, 300, 3235, 970, 313, 1177, 380, 853, 281, 7081, 613, 10392, 538, 23663, 512, 5994, 11, 22734, 1688, 14132, 9482, 13, 51831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13145208740234374, "compression_ratio": 1.5527156549520766, "no_speech_prob": 2.1340067300062993e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 12220, "start": 122.2, "end": 126.3, "text": " Right, like a global banking ledger or a hyperscale cloud provider.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 411, 257, 4338, 18261, 4684, 1321, 420, 257, 7420, 433, 37088, 4588, 12398, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469640639221784, "compression_ratio": 1.6168582375478928, "no_speech_prob": 1.4210568485828468e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 12220, "start": 126.68, "end": 127.08, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50589, 7587, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469640639221784, "compression_ratio": 1.6168582375478928, "no_speech_prob": 1.4210568485828468e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 12220, "start": 127.58, "end": 138.96, "text": " Instead, the paper walks us through a theoretical progression using three tiny custom-built command line programs, one written in Go, one in Perl, and one in Rust.", "tokens": [50634, 7156, 11, 264, 3035, 12896, 505, 807, 257, 20864, 18733, 1228, 1045, 5870, 2375, 12, 23018, 5622, 1622, 4268, 11, 472, 3720, 294, 1037, 11, 472, 294, 3026, 75, 11, 293, 472, 294, 34952, 13, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469640639221784, "compression_ratio": 1.6168582375478928, "no_speech_prob": 1.4210568485828468e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 12220, "start": 139.36, "end": 145.38, "text": " And, you know, the choice to use small custom programs is an incredibly potent analytical tool here.", "tokens": [51223, 400, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 3922, 281, 764, 1359, 2375, 4268, 307, 364, 6252, 27073, 29579, 2290, 510, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469640639221784, "compression_ratio": 1.6168582375478928, "no_speech_prob": 1.4210568485828468e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 12220, "start": 145.82, "end": 149.24, "text": " Flixion explicitly refers to them as executable witnesses.", "tokens": [51546, 3235, 970, 313, 20803, 14942, 281, 552, 382, 7568, 712, 20217, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469640639221784, "compression_ratio": 1.6168582375478928, "no_speech_prob": 1.4210568485828468e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 12220, "start": 149.78, "end": 150.8, "text": " Executable witnesses.", "tokens": [51744, 17662, 32148, 20217, 13, 51795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1469640639221784, "compression_ratio": 1.6168582375478928, "no_speech_prob": 1.4210568485828468e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 15080, "start": 150.8, "end": 151.8, "text": " I love that phrasing.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 959, 300, 7636, 3349, 13, 50415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731268843015035, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549014762723413e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 15080, "start": 151.9, "end": 162.86, "text": " It's great because when you analyze a massive enterprise application, the core logic is almost always obscured by, like, millions of lines of framework code and load balancers and middleware.", "tokens": [50420, 467, 311, 869, 570, 562, 291, 12477, 257, 5994, 14132, 3861, 11, 264, 4965, 9952, 307, 1920, 1009, 22082, 3831, 538, 11, 411, 11, 6803, 295, 3876, 295, 8388, 3089, 293, 3677, 3119, 4463, 433, 293, 2808, 3039, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731268843015035, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549014762723413e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 15080, "start": 163.04000000000002, "end": 164.84, "text": " You just can't see the forest for the trees.", "tokens": [50977, 509, 445, 393, 380, 536, 264, 6719, 337, 264, 5852, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731268843015035, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549014762723413e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 15080, "start": 165.06, "end": 165.32000000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51078, 1779, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731268843015035, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549014762723413e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 15080, "start": 165.38000000000002, "end": 170.14000000000001, "text": " You can't see the actual decision-making process because it's buried under the sheer weight of dependency management.", "tokens": [51094, 509, 393, 380, 536, 264, 3539, 3537, 12, 12402, 1399, 570, 309, 311, 14101, 833, 264, 23061, 3364, 295, 33621, 4592, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731268843015035, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549014762723413e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 15080, "start": 170.24, "end": 170.38000000000002, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51337, 865, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08731268843015035, "compression_ratio": 1.5748987854251013, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549014762723413e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 17038, "start": 170.38, "end": 174.26, "text": " But a tiny, isolated program, it exposes its assumptions.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 257, 5870, 11, 14621, 1461, 11, 309, 1278, 4201, 1080, 17695, 13, 50559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10660338768592248, "compression_ratio": 1.5139664804469273, "no_speech_prob": 2.019714256951133e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 17038, "start": 174.42, "end": 175.29999999999998, "text": " It lays it all bare.", "tokens": [50567, 467, 32714, 309, 439, 6949, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10660338768592248, "compression_ratio": 1.5139664804469273, "no_speech_prob": 2.019714256951133e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 17038, "start": 175.46, "end": 175.68, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50619, 865, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10660338768592248, "compression_ratio": 1.5139664804469273, "no_speech_prob": 2.019714256951133e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 17038, "start": 175.79999999999998, "end": 186.0, "text": " It allows us to observe the raw, exposed nerves of how a system handles execution, how it constructs institutional judgment, and how it fundamentally manages the continuation of history.", "tokens": [50636, 467, 4045, 505, 281, 11441, 264, 8936, 11, 9495, 23078, 295, 577, 257, 1185, 18722, 15058, 11, 577, 309, 7690, 82, 18391, 12216, 11, 293, 577, 309, 17879, 22489, 264, 29357, 295, 2503, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10660338768592248, "compression_ratio": 1.5139664804469273, "no_speech_prob": 2.019714256951133e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 18600, "start": 186.0, "end": 187.26, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 50428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17291621005896365, "compression_ratio": 1.4689265536723164, "no_speech_prob": 1.988390138304985e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 18600, "start": 187.66, "end": 196.34, "text": " Because before Flixion even introduces the three programs, the paper sets the stage by dismantling a foundational assumption that most of us make about software.", "tokens": [50448, 1436, 949, 3235, 970, 313, 754, 31472, 264, 1045, 4268, 11, 264, 3035, 6352, 264, 3233, 538, 30506, 1688, 257, 32195, 15302, 300, 881, 295, 505, 652, 466, 4722, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17291621005896365, "compression_ratio": 1.4689265536723164, "no_speech_prob": 1.988390138304985e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 18600, "start": 196.72, "end": 198.14, "text": " The equivalency illusion.", "tokens": [50901, 440, 9052, 3020, 18854, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17291621005896365, "compression_ratio": 1.4689265536723164, "no_speech_prob": 1.988390138304985e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 18600, "start": 198.38, "end": 198.62, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50984, 1079, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17291621005896365, "compression_ratio": 1.4689265536723164, "no_speech_prob": 1.988390138304985e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 18600, "start": 198.92, "end": 200.68, "text": " Flixion calls it the equivalency illusion.", "tokens": [51011, 3235, 970, 313, 5498, 309, 264, 9052, 3020, 18854, 13, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17291621005896365, "compression_ratio": 1.4689265536723164, "no_speech_prob": 1.988390138304985e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 20068, "start": 200.68, "end": 212.1, "text": " It's this habit we all have of collapsing completely distinct layers of systemic authority into a single binary concept of just, you know, it works or it doesn't work.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 341, 7164, 321, 439, 362, 295, 45339, 2584, 10644, 7914, 295, 23789, 8281, 666, 257, 2167, 17434, 3410, 295, 445, 11, 291, 458, 11, 309, 1985, 420, 309, 1177, 380, 589, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253442257008654, "compression_ratio": 1.5307692307692307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683221202769884e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 20068, "start": 212.20000000000002, "end": 214.66, "text": " Yeah, we just look for the error code or the success message.", "tokens": [50941, 865, 11, 321, 445, 574, 337, 264, 6713, 3089, 420, 264, 2245, 3636, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253442257008654, "compression_ratio": 1.5307692307692307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683221202769884e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 20068, "start": 214.78, "end": 215.22, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51070, 7587, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253442257008654, "compression_ratio": 1.5307692307692307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683221202769884e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 20068, "start": 216.12, "end": 220.26000000000002, "text": " But Flixion formalizes a central refusal of this idea right at the beginning.", "tokens": [51137, 583, 3235, 970, 313, 9860, 5660, 257, 5777, 48948, 295, 341, 1558, 558, 412, 264, 2863, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253442257008654, "compression_ratio": 1.5307692307692307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683221202769884e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 20068, "start": 220.88, "end": 226.76000000000002, "text": " They draw a hard line between execution, modeling, legitimacy, and authorization.", "tokens": [51375, 814, 2642, 257, 1152, 1622, 1296, 15058, 11, 15983, 11, 41339, 11, 293, 33697, 13, 51669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1253442257008654, "compression_ratio": 1.5307692307692307, "no_speech_prob": 1.8683221202769884e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 22676, "start": 226.76, "end": 236.35999999999999, "text": " It's a necessary dismantling, honestly, because we constantly conflate a program successfully executing a rule with that rule actually being legitimate.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 4818, 30506, 1688, 11, 6095, 11, 570, 321, 6460, 1497, 17593, 257, 1461, 10727, 32368, 257, 4978, 365, 300, 4978, 767, 885, 17956, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14059476178101818, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875354195630687e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 22676, "start": 236.67999999999998, "end": 236.78, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50861, 1779, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14059476178101818, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875354195630687e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 22676, "start": 236.98, "end": 241.0, "text": " But Flixion forces us to separate these layers mathematically and conceptually.", "tokens": [50876, 583, 3235, 970, 313, 5874, 505, 281, 4994, 613, 7914, 44003, 293, 3410, 671, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14059476178101818, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875354195630687e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 22676, "start": 241.17999999999998, "end": 245.66, "text": " Like a program can execute a function with absolute flawless mathematical perfection.", "tokens": [51086, 1743, 257, 1461, 393, 14483, 257, 2445, 365, 8236, 45693, 18894, 19708, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14059476178101818, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875354195630687e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 22676, "start": 246.1, "end": 248.64, "text": " It can be completely reproducible, totally bug-free.", "tokens": [51332, 467, 393, 312, 2584, 11408, 32128, 11, 3879, 7426, 12, 10792, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14059476178101818, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875354195630687e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 22676, "start": 248.76, "end": 252.2, "text": " But the underlying model that the rule is based on might be entirely defective.", "tokens": [51465, 583, 264, 14217, 2316, 300, 264, 4978, 307, 2361, 322, 1062, 312, 7696, 16445, 488, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14059476178101818, "compression_ratio": 1.6654545454545455, "no_speech_prob": 1.6875354195630687e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 25220, "start": 252.2, "end": 252.67999999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1209316002695184, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.34572387955334e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 25220, "start": 253.1, "end": 259.0, "text": " And taking it a step further, even if the execution is flawless and the model is accurate, the rule itself might lack legitimacy.", "tokens": [50410, 400, 1940, 309, 257, 1823, 3052, 11, 754, 498, 264, 15058, 307, 45693, 293, 264, 2316, 307, 8559, 11, 264, 4978, 2564, 1062, 5011, 41339, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1209316002695184, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.34572387955334e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 25220, "start": 259.15999999999997, "end": 260.0, "text": " Meaning what, exactly?", "tokens": [50713, 19948, 437, 11, 2293, 30, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1209316002695184, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.34572387955334e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 25220, "start": 260.24, "end": 265.59999999999997, "text": " Meaning the system simply might not have the jurisdictional authority to enforce that ruling in the first place.", "tokens": [50767, 19948, 264, 1185, 2935, 1062, 406, 362, 264, 19078, 23611, 8281, 281, 24825, 300, 21437, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1209316002695184, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.34572387955334e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 25220, "start": 265.71999999999997, "end": 266.18, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [51041, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1209316002695184, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.34572387955334e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 25220, "start": 266.38, "end": 266.64, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51074, 865, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1209316002695184, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.34572387955334e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 25220, "start": 267.21999999999997, "end": 275.53999999999996, "text": " And finally, even if the rule is legitimate, the resulting actions still might not be authorized to project an effect into the external world.", "tokens": [51116, 400, 2721, 11, 754, 498, 264, 4978, 307, 17956, 11, 264, 16505, 5909, 920, 1062, 406, 312, 28312, 281, 1716, 364, 1802, 666, 264, 8320, 1002, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1209316002695184, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.34572387955334e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 25220, "start": 275.8, "end": 277.84, "text": " I love how Flixion formalizes this.", "tokens": [51545, 286, 959, 577, 3235, 970, 313, 9860, 5660, 341, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1209316002695184, "compression_ratio": 1.6774193548387097, "no_speech_prob": 1.34572387955334e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 27784, "start": 277.84, "end": 286.26, "text": " It takes that vague unease we all feel when a computer system unfairly denies a request, and it gives it rigorous structural teeth.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2516, 300, 24247, 2251, 651, 321, 439, 841, 562, 257, 3820, 1185, 17019, 356, 1441, 530, 257, 5308, 11, 293, 309, 2709, 309, 29882, 15067, 7798, 13, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.083473941736054, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671682701556833e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 27784, "start": 286.34, "end": 287.9, "text": " It gives us a vocabulary for it.", "tokens": [50790, 467, 2709, 505, 257, 19864, 337, 309, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.083473941736054, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671682701556833e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 27784, "start": 287.96, "end": 288.28, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50871, 1779, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.083473941736054, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671682701556833e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 27784, "start": 288.64, "end": 297.52, "text": " So to break apart that conflation, the paper introduces a foundational architecture defining four distinct stages that every action must pass through.", "tokens": [50905, 407, 281, 1821, 4936, 300, 1497, 24278, 11, 264, 3035, 31472, 257, 32195, 9482, 17827, 1451, 10644, 10232, 300, 633, 3069, 1633, 1320, 807, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.083473941736054, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671682701556833e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 27784, "start": 298.05999999999995, "end": 300.82, "text": " Proposal, record, admission, and continuation.", "tokens": [51376, 21944, 329, 304, 11, 2136, 11, 24668, 11, 293, 29357, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.083473941736054, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671682701556833e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 27784, "start": 301.23999999999995, "end": 306.91999999999996, "text": " But, and this is key, before an action can even become a proposal, it has to pass through the ingress operator.", "tokens": [51535, 583, 11, 293, 341, 307, 2141, 11, 949, 364, 3069, 393, 754, 1813, 257, 11494, 11, 309, 575, 281, 1320, 807, 264, 3957, 735, 12973, 13, 51819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.083473941736054, "compression_ratio": 1.6529209621993126, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671682701556833e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 30692, "start": 306.92, "end": 308.88, "text": " Which the paper represents is the letter Q.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 264, 3035, 8855, 307, 264, 5063, 1249, 13, 50463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 30692, "start": 309.08000000000004, "end": 309.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50473, 7587, 13, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 30692, "start": 309.84000000000003, "end": 310.12, "text": " Q.", "tokens": [50511, 1249, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 30692, "start": 310.5, "end": 315.56, "text": " And the ingress operator is the absolute boundary of the system's recognized reality.", "tokens": [50544, 400, 264, 3957, 735, 12973, 307, 264, 8236, 12866, 295, 264, 1185, 311, 9823, 4103, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 30692, "start": 315.62, "end": 316.88, "text": " Okay, so break that down for me.", "tokens": [50800, 1033, 11, 370, 1821, 300, 760, 337, 385, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 30692, "start": 316.94, "end": 318.02000000000004, "text": " What does that actually look like?", "tokens": [50866, 708, 775, 300, 767, 574, 411, 30, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 30692, "start": 318.04, "end": 320.58000000000004, "text": " Let's look at the theoretical spaces Flixion defines here.", "tokens": [50921, 961, 311, 574, 412, 264, 20864, 7673, 3235, 970, 313, 23122, 510, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 30692, "start": 320.94, "end": 325.72, "text": " You have space X, which represents the infinite universe of all offered inputs.", "tokens": [51066, 509, 362, 1901, 1783, 11, 597, 8855, 264, 13785, 6445, 295, 439, 8059, 15743, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 30692, "start": 325.84000000000003, "end": 328.08000000000004, "text": " So that's just, like, everything.", "tokens": [51311, 407, 300, 311, 445, 11, 411, 11, 1203, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 30692, "start": 328.44, "end": 328.88, "text": " Everything.", "tokens": [51441, 5471, 13, 51463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 30692, "start": 329.74, "end": 336.42, "text": " Every possible signal, every burst of static on the wire, every malformed string you could possibly throw at a machine.", "tokens": [51506, 2048, 1944, 6358, 11, 633, 12712, 295, 13437, 322, 264, 6234, 11, 633, 2806, 22892, 6798, 291, 727, 6264, 3507, 412, 257, 3479, 13, 51840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13885563070123846, "compression_ratio": 1.6634304207119741, "no_speech_prob": 2.2360726551623467e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 33642, "start": 336.42, "end": 337.18, "text": " Pure chaos.", "tokens": [50365, 29474, 14158, 13, 50403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17089168324190027, "compression_ratio": 1.4619047619047618, "no_speech_prob": 1.460049746035419e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 33642, "start": 337.26, "end": 337.94, "text": " Pure chaos.", "tokens": [50407, 29474, 14158, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17089168324190027, "compression_ratio": 1.4619047619047618, "no_speech_prob": 1.460049746035419e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 33642, "start": 338.16, "end": 343.3, "text": " Then you have space X, which is a strictly bounded space of finite, well-formed proposals.", "tokens": [50452, 1396, 291, 362, 1901, 1783, 11, 597, 307, 257, 20792, 37498, 1901, 295, 19362, 11, 731, 12, 22892, 20198, 13, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17089168324190027, "compression_ratio": 1.4619047619047618, "no_speech_prob": 1.460049746035419e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 33642, "start": 344.16, "end": 348.64000000000004, "text": " And the ingress operator, Q, is the vital membrane between X and I.", "tokens": [50752, 400, 264, 3957, 735, 12973, 11, 1249, 11, 307, 264, 11707, 19651, 1296, 1783, 293, 286, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17089168324190027, "compression_ratio": 1.4619047619047618, "no_speech_prob": 1.460049746035419e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 33642, "start": 348.78000000000003, "end": 350.14000000000004, "text": " So it's filtering the chaos.", "tokens": [50983, 407, 309, 311, 30822, 264, 14158, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17089168324190027, "compression_ratio": 1.4619047619047618, "no_speech_prob": 1.460049746035419e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 33642, "start": 350.3, "end": 350.46000000000004, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51059, 865, 13, 51067], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17089168324190027, "compression_ratio": 1.4619047619047618, "no_speech_prob": 1.460049746035419e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 33642, "start": 350.58000000000004, "end": 356.64, "text": " Its entire job is framing, size enforcement, syntactic normalization, and authentication.", "tokens": [51073, 6953, 2302, 1691, 307, 28971, 11, 2744, 11475, 11, 23980, 19892, 2710, 2144, 11, 293, 26643, 13, 51376], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17089168324190027, "compression_ratio": 1.4619047619047618, "no_speech_prob": 1.460049746035419e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 35664, "start": 356.64, "end": 363.91999999999996, "text": " And the critical detail here is that if a signal fails at the ingress operator, it doesn't return a rejected proposal.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 4924, 2607, 510, 307, 300, 498, 257, 6358, 18199, 412, 264, 3957, 735, 12973, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 2736, 257, 15749, 11494, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16333218838306182, "compression_ratio": 1.3583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549751156834768e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 35664, "start": 364.24, "end": 365.82, "text": " It returns a null state.", "tokens": [50745, 467, 11247, 257, 18184, 1785, 13, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16333218838306182, "compression_ratio": 1.3583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549751156834768e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 35664, "start": 365.91999999999996, "end": 366.12, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50829, 1779, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16333218838306182, "compression_ratio": 1.3583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549751156834768e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 35664, "start": 366.2, "end": 366.78, "text": " It drops it.", "tokens": [50843, 467, 11438, 309, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16333218838306182, "compression_ratio": 1.3583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549751156834768e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 36678, "start": 366.78, "end": 374.17999999999995, "text": " The paper notes that if a byte stream is rejected because it exceeds a size limit or fails a basic checksum, it simply never entered the system.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 5570, 300, 498, 257, 40846, 4309, 307, 15749, 570, 309, 43305, 257, 2744, 4948, 420, 18199, 257, 3875, 13834, 449, 11, 309, 2935, 1128, 9065, 264, 1185, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11176974197913861, "compression_ratio": 1.4430379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 2.1258736958296165e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 36678, "start": 374.34, "end": 375.84, "text": " It was never real to the system.", "tokens": [50743, 467, 390, 1128, 957, 281, 264, 1185, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11176974197913861, "compression_ratio": 1.4430379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 2.1258736958296165e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 36678, "start": 375.84, "end": 378.28, "text": " So it's like trying to get into an exclusive club.", "tokens": [50818, 407, 309, 311, 411, 1382, 281, 483, 666, 364, 13005, 6482, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11176974197913861, "compression_ratio": 1.4430379746835442, "no_speech_prob": 2.1258736958296165e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 37828, "start": 378.28, "end": 389.78, "text": " If you walk up to the door speaking absolute gibberish or you refuse to show your ID, the bouncer doesn't pull out a formal ledger and write down, you know, user was denied entry for failing to articulate a request.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 1792, 493, 281, 264, 2853, 4124, 8236, 4553, 43189, 420, 291, 16791, 281, 855, 428, 7348, 11, 264, 272, 14296, 1177, 380, 2235, 484, 257, 9860, 4684, 1321, 293, 2464, 760, 11, 291, 458, 11, 4195, 390, 17774, 8729, 337, 18223, 281, 30305, 257, 5308, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485834421205126, "compression_ratio": 1.5966666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457198680053017e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 37828, "start": 389.9, "end": 390.53999999999996, "text": " No, they don't.", "tokens": [50946, 883, 11, 436, 500, 380, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485834421205126, "compression_ratio": 1.5966666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457198680053017e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 37828, "start": 390.61999999999995, "end": 391.58, "text": " They just ignore you.", "tokens": [50982, 814, 445, 11200, 291, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485834421205126, "compression_ratio": 1.5966666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457198680053017e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 37828, "start": 391.79999999999995, "end": 394.47999999999996, "text": " They don't log your presence in the club's permanent archives.", "tokens": [51041, 814, 500, 380, 3565, 428, 6814, 294, 264, 6482, 311, 10996, 25607, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485834421205126, "compression_ratio": 1.5966666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457198680053017e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 37828, "start": 394.85999999999996, "end": 396.82, "text": " You aren't even a recognized applicant yet.", "tokens": [51194, 509, 3212, 380, 754, 257, 9823, 30915, 1939, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485834421205126, "compression_ratio": 1.5966666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457198680053017e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 37828, "start": 397.03999999999996, "end": 399.71999999999997, "text": " You never crossed the ingress boundary to become a proposal.", "tokens": [51303, 509, 1128, 14622, 264, 3957, 735, 12866, 281, 1813, 257, 11494, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485834421205126, "compression_ratio": 1.5966666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457198680053017e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 37828, "start": 400.32, "end": 402.85999999999996, "text": " That analogy holds, but I would actually push it further.", "tokens": [51467, 663, 21663, 9190, 11, 457, 286, 576, 767, 2944, 309, 3052, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485834421205126, "compression_ratio": 1.5966666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.3457198680053017e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 40286, "start": 402.86, "end": 412.82, "text": " It's not just that the bouncer ignores you, it's that the club's entire architectural layout is designed so that the security cameras don't even point at the sidewalk.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 406, 445, 300, 264, 272, 14296, 5335, 2706, 291, 11, 309, 311, 300, 264, 6482, 311, 2302, 26621, 13333, 307, 4761, 370, 300, 264, 3825, 8622, 500, 380, 754, 935, 412, 264, 25360, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1759516398111979, "compression_ratio": 1.6026058631921825, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491476374265845e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 40286, "start": 412.96000000000004, "end": 413.5, "text": " Oh, man.", "tokens": [50870, 876, 11, 587, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1759516398111979, "compression_ratio": 1.6026058631921825, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491476374265845e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 40286, "start": 413.68, "end": 413.86, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50906, 3153, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1759516398111979, "compression_ratio": 1.6026058631921825, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491476374265845e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 40286, "start": 413.90000000000003, "end": 414.08000000000004, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50917, 1779, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1759516398111979, "compression_ratio": 1.6026058631921825, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491476374265845e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 40286, "start": 414.22, "end": 418.62, "text": " The system is structurally blind to anything outside the ingress boundary.", "tokens": [50933, 440, 1185, 307, 6594, 6512, 6865, 281, 1340, 2380, 264, 3957, 735, 12866, 13, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1759516398111979, "compression_ratio": 1.6026058631921825, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491476374265845e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 40286, "start": 419.12, "end": 423.04, "text": " And this brings in the sociological dimensions of Fliction's argument.", "tokens": [51178, 400, 341, 5607, 294, 264, 3075, 4383, 12819, 295, 3235, 4105, 311, 6770, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1759516398111979, "compression_ratio": 1.6026058631921825, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491476374265845e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 40286, "start": 423.7, "end": 431.24, "text": " The paper heavily references Adrian McKenzie's concept of code as sociality and Mark C. Marino's work in critical code studies.", "tokens": [51407, 440, 3035, 10950, 15400, 31746, 21765, 32203, 311, 3410, 295, 3089, 382, 2093, 507, 293, 3934, 383, 13, 2039, 2982, 311, 589, 294, 4924, 3089, 5313, 13, 51784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1759516398111979, "compression_ratio": 1.6026058631921825, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491476374265845e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 40286, "start": 431.24, "end": 432.5, "text": " I remember reading that part.", "tokens": [51784, 286, 1604, 3760, 300, 644, 13, 51847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1759516398111979, "compression_ratio": 1.6026058631921825, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491476374265845e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 43250, "start": 432.5, "end": 437.3, "text": " Marino basically argues that source code isn't just a set of functional instructions.", "tokens": [50365, 2039, 2982, 1936, 38218, 300, 4009, 3089, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 992, 295, 11745, 9415, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11771195906179922, "compression_ratio": 1.7395833333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324504240385675e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 43250, "start": 437.92, "end": 442.52, "text": " It is a text that is overflowing with cultural, political, and rhetorical commitments.", "tokens": [50636, 467, 307, 257, 2487, 300, 307, 670, 43955, 365, 6988, 11, 3905, 11, 293, 24182, 284, 804, 26230, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11771195906179922, "compression_ratio": 1.7395833333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324504240385675e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 43250, "start": 442.72, "end": 453.06, "text": " Because the very act of defining the parameters of the ingress operator deciding what constitutes a quote-unquote well-formed proposal is an act of extreme editorial power.", "tokens": [50876, 1436, 264, 588, 605, 295, 17827, 264, 9834, 295, 264, 3957, 735, 12973, 17990, 437, 44204, 257, 6513, 12, 409, 25016, 731, 12, 22892, 11494, 307, 364, 605, 295, 8084, 33412, 1347, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11771195906179922, "compression_ratio": 1.7395833333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324504240385675e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 43250, "start": 453.14, "end": 454.9, "text": " It is the ultimate editorial power.", "tokens": [51397, 467, 307, 264, 9705, 33412, 1347, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11771195906179922, "compression_ratio": 1.7395833333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324504240385675e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 43250, "start": 454.9, "end": 461.86, "text": " What the system recognizes as a proposal defines the entirety of what the system is willing to acknowledge even exists.", "tokens": [51485, 708, 264, 1185, 26564, 382, 257, 11494, 23122, 264, 31557, 295, 437, 264, 1185, 307, 4950, 281, 10692, 754, 8198, 13, 51833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11771195906179922, "compression_ratio": 1.7395833333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.8324504240385675e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 46186, "start": 461.86, "end": 462.56, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 50400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093511036464147, "compression_ratio": 1.4426229508196722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751745390147788e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 46186, "start": 463.12, "end": 467.54, "text": " The boundary of ingress is an institutional boundary disguised as a technical one.", "tokens": [50428, 440, 12866, 295, 3957, 735, 307, 364, 18391, 12866, 23333, 2640, 382, 257, 6191, 472, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093511036464147, "compression_ratio": 1.4426229508196722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751745390147788e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 46186, "start": 467.94, "end": 470.62, "text": " Which brings us to the concept of audit completeness.", "tokens": [50669, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 3410, 295, 17748, 1557, 15264, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093511036464147, "compression_ratio": 1.4426229508196722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751745390147788e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 46186, "start": 470.82, "end": 471.18, "text": " Oh, yeah.", "tokens": [50813, 876, 11, 1338, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093511036464147, "compression_ratio": 1.4426229508196722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751745390147788e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 46186, "start": 471.26, "end": 472.04, "text": " This was fascinating.", "tokens": [50835, 639, 390, 10343, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093511036464147, "compression_ratio": 1.4426229508196722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751745390147788e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 46186, "start": 472.38, "end": 475.86, "text": " Because we always hear that robust systems have to have perfect audit logs.", "tokens": [50891, 1436, 321, 1009, 1568, 300, 13956, 3652, 362, 281, 362, 2176, 17748, 20820, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093511036464147, "compression_ratio": 1.4426229508196722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751745390147788e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 46186, "start": 476.1, "end": 476.58000000000004, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51077, 7587, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18093511036464147, "compression_ratio": 1.4426229508196722, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751745390147788e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 47658, "start": 476.58, "end": 484.74, "text": " But Fliction argues that recording only becomes a structural mandate after a proposal crosses that explicit ingress boundary.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3235, 4105, 38218, 300, 6613, 787, 3643, 257, 15067, 23885, 934, 257, 11494, 28467, 300, 13691, 3957, 735, 12866, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293348165658805, "compression_ratio": 1.4948979591836735, "no_speech_prob": 1.7888726524389886e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 47658, "start": 485.53999999999996, "end": 491.3, "text": " A server isn't obligated to permanently archive every random ping it receives from a botnet.", "tokens": [50813, 316, 7154, 1943, 380, 9270, 770, 281, 24042, 23507, 633, 4974, 26151, 309, 20717, 490, 257, 10592, 7129, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293348165658805, "compression_ratio": 1.4948979591836735, "no_speech_prob": 1.7888726524389886e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 47658, "start": 491.38, "end": 493.5, "text": " That would just fill up the hard drives instantly.", "tokens": [51105, 663, 576, 445, 2836, 493, 264, 1152, 11754, 13518, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293348165658805, "compression_ratio": 1.4948979591836735, "no_speech_prob": 1.7888726524389886e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 47658, "start": 493.65999999999997, "end": 494.52, "text": " It would be impossible.", "tokens": [51219, 467, 576, 312, 6243, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16293348165658805, "compression_ratio": 1.4948979591836735, "no_speech_prob": 1.7888726524389886e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 49452, "start": 494.52, "end": 506.18, "text": " But once the ingress operator validates the syntax and authenticates the user, once it recognizes the signal as a formal proposal within space, I-audit completeness becomes unconditional.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1564, 264, 3957, 735, 12973, 7363, 1024, 264, 28431, 293, 12466, 1024, 264, 4195, 11, 1564, 309, 26564, 264, 6358, 382, 257, 9860, 11494, 1951, 1901, 11, 286, 12, 3751, 270, 1557, 15264, 3643, 47916, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14476940155029297, "compression_ratio": 1.5849056603773586, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845673277813948e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 49452, "start": 506.62, "end": 511.06, "text": " So if the proposal is subsequently denied, that denial must be permanently recorded.", "tokens": [50970, 407, 498, 264, 11494, 307, 26514, 17774, 11, 300, 28754, 1633, 312, 24042, 8287, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14476940155029297, "compression_ratio": 1.5849056603773586, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845673277813948e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 49452, "start": 511.21999999999997, "end": 511.65999999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51200, 7587, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14476940155029297, "compression_ratio": 1.5849056603773586, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845673277813948e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 49452, "start": 512.14, "end": 514.72, "text": " The ingress boundary dictates the threshold of memory.", "tokens": [51246, 440, 3957, 735, 12866, 12569, 1024, 264, 14678, 295, 4675, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14476940155029297, "compression_ratio": 1.5849056603773586, "no_speech_prob": 2.0845673277813948e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 51472, "start": 514.72, "end": 519.4200000000001, "text": " And that threshold of memory forces a system to commit to an event.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 14678, 295, 4675, 5874, 257, 1185, 281, 5599, 281, 364, 2280, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566044035412017, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051708995132532e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 51472, "start": 519.94, "end": 526.1, "text": " And once a signal becomes a recognized proposal, we arrive at the first true layer of the architecture, operational validity.", "tokens": [50626, 400, 1564, 257, 6358, 3643, 257, 9823, 11494, 11, 321, 8881, 412, 264, 700, 2074, 4583, 295, 264, 9482, 11, 16607, 40943, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566044035412017, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051708995132532e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 51472, "start": 526.4, "end": 527.46, "text": " Denoted by the letter V.", "tokens": [50949, 6458, 23325, 538, 264, 5063, 691, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566044035412017, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051708995132532e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 51472, "start": 527.6600000000001, "end": 528.24, "text": " Right, V.", "tokens": [51012, 1779, 11, 691, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566044035412017, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051708995132532e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 51472, "start": 528.86, "end": 535.5400000000001, "text": " And this is where Fliction introduces the first of the executable witnesses, a tiny program written in Go called HelloTool.", "tokens": [51072, 400, 341, 307, 689, 3235, 4105, 31472, 264, 700, 295, 264, 7568, 712, 20217, 11, 257, 5870, 1461, 3720, 294, 1037, 1219, 2425, 51, 1092, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566044035412017, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051708995132532e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 51472, "start": 535.6800000000001, "end": 538.6800000000001, "text": " And Go is the perfect rhetorical choice for this specific layer.", "tokens": [51413, 400, 1037, 307, 264, 2176, 24182, 284, 804, 3922, 337, 341, 2685, 4583, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566044035412017, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051708995132532e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 51472, "start": 539.0600000000001, "end": 541.6, "text": " Fliction notes that Go supplies austere utility.", "tokens": [51582, 3235, 4105, 5570, 300, 1037, 11768, 34916, 323, 14877, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566044035412017, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051708995132532e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 51472, "start": 541.9, "end": 542.82, "text": " Austere utility.", "tokens": [51724, 4126, 323, 14877, 13, 51770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566044035412017, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051708995132532e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 51472, "start": 542.98, "end": 543.4, "text": " I like that.", "tokens": [51778, 286, 411, 300, 13, 51799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11566044035412017, "compression_ratio": 1.6813559322033897, "no_speech_prob": 1.9051708995132532e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 54340, "start": 543.4, "end": 548.42, "text": " It is not a language built for poetic abstraction or, like, magical metaprogramming.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 406, 257, 2856, 3094, 337, 41080, 37765, 420, 11, 411, 11, 12066, 1131, 569, 340, 1342, 2810, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11800169944763184, "compression_ratio": 1.6677966101694914, "no_speech_prob": 2.343935809334674e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 54340, "start": 548.66, "end": 554.78, "text": " It is built for explicit error handling, rigorous standard library parsing, and conventional metadata.", "tokens": [50628, 467, 307, 3094, 337, 13691, 6713, 13175, 11, 29882, 3832, 6405, 21156, 278, 11, 293, 16011, 26603, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11800169944763184, "compression_ratio": 1.6677966101694914, "no_speech_prob": 2.343935809334674e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 54340, "start": 555.12, "end": 558.1, "text": " And the HelloTool program itself is almost painfully mundane.", "tokens": [50951, 400, 264, 2425, 51, 1092, 1461, 2564, 307, 1920, 1822, 2277, 43497, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11800169944763184, "compression_ratio": 1.6677966101694914, "no_speech_prob": 2.343935809334674e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 54340, "start": 558.3, "end": 559.28, "text": " It is so boring.", "tokens": [51110, 467, 307, 370, 9989, 13, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11800169944763184, "compression_ratio": 1.6677966101694914, "no_speech_prob": 2.343935809334674e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 54340, "start": 559.38, "end": 562.5, "text": " It's just a secure starter scaffold for a command line application.", "tokens": [51164, 467, 311, 445, 257, 7144, 22465, 44094, 337, 257, 5622, 1622, 3861, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11800169944763184, "compression_ratio": 1.6677966101694914, "no_speech_prob": 2.343935809334674e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 54340, "start": 563.06, "end": 568.42, "text": " It greets a named user, reports its version, and meticulously rejects malformed flags.", "tokens": [51348, 467, 6066, 1385, 257, 4926, 4195, 11, 7122, 1080, 3037, 11, 293, 41566, 25038, 8248, 82, 2806, 22892, 23265, 13, 51616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11800169944763184, "compression_ratio": 1.6677966101694914, "no_speech_prob": 2.343935809334674e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 54340, "start": 568.42, "end": 572.18, "text": " It also includes a management script to build, test, and tag releases.", "tokens": [51616, 467, 611, 5974, 257, 4592, 5755, 281, 1322, 11, 1500, 11, 293, 6162, 16952, 13, 51804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11800169944763184, "compression_ratio": 1.6677966101694914, "no_speech_prob": 2.343935809334674e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 57218, "start": 572.18, "end": 575.2199999999999, "text": " But its mundane nature is the entire point.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1080, 43497, 3687, 307, 264, 2302, 935, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14585208892822266, "compression_ratio": 1.5138888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879079514295348e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 57218, "start": 575.52, "end": 578.3599999999999, "text": " It's not trying to solve some complex business problem.", "tokens": [50532, 467, 311, 406, 1382, 281, 5039, 512, 3997, 1606, 1154, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14585208892822266, "compression_ratio": 1.5138888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879079514295348e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 57218, "start": 578.78, "end": 582.62, "text": " It's trying to establish an absolute text line for operational boundaries.", "tokens": [50695, 467, 311, 1382, 281, 8327, 364, 8236, 2487, 1622, 337, 16607, 13180, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14585208892822266, "compression_ratio": 1.5138888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879079514295348e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 57218, "start": 583.18, "end": 588.8599999999999, "text": " The part of this section that immediately stood out to me was Fliction's mathematical formalization of subtractive security.", "tokens": [50915, 440, 644, 295, 341, 3541, 300, 4258, 9371, 484, 281, 385, 390, 3235, 4105, 311, 18894, 9860, 2144, 295, 16390, 488, 3825, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14585208892822266, "compression_ratio": 1.5138888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879079514295348e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 57218, "start": 589.28, "end": 590.92, "text": " Oh, the math here is great.", "tokens": [51220, 876, 11, 264, 5221, 510, 307, 869, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14585208892822266, "compression_ratio": 1.5138888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 1.6879079514295348e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 59092, "start": 590.92, "end": 598.9599999999999, "text": " Because we constantly talk about the principle of least privilege in software engineering, but the paper actually maps it out with a strict monotonic relation.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 321, 6460, 751, 466, 264, 8665, 295, 1935, 12122, 294, 4722, 7043, 11, 457, 264, 3035, 767, 11317, 309, 484, 365, 257, 10910, 1108, 310, 11630, 9721, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10450370745225386, "compression_ratio": 1.436241610738255, "no_speech_prob": 1.957036963040615e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 59092, "start": 599.26, "end": 602.14, "text": " It gives that principle a rigorous mathematical proof.", "tokens": [50782, 467, 2709, 300, 8665, 257, 29882, 18894, 8177, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10450370745225386, "compression_ratio": 1.436241610738255, "no_speech_prob": 1.957036963040615e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 60214, "start": 602.14, "end": 612.52, "text": " So, Fliction uses the Greek letter gamma to represent the set of capabilities available to a program, and E to denote the reachable external effects of those capabilities.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 3235, 4105, 4960, 264, 10281, 5063, 15546, 281, 2906, 264, 992, 295, 10862, 2435, 281, 257, 1461, 11, 293, 462, 281, 45708, 264, 2524, 712, 8320, 5065, 295, 729, 10862, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13847047906172902, "compression_ratio": 1.9617224880382775, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310954544142663e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 60214, "start": 612.66, "end": 612.8199999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50891, 1779, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13847047906172902, "compression_ratio": 1.9617224880382775, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310954544142663e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 60214, "start": 612.98, "end": 613.6, "text": " Gamma and E.", "tokens": [50907, 24723, 1696, 293, 462, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13847047906172902, "compression_ratio": 1.9617224880382775, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310954544142663e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 60214, "start": 613.9, "end": 625.88, "text": " And the relation states that if the capabilities of program P' are a subset of the capabilities of program P, then the reachable effects of P' are mathematically guaranteed to be a subset of the reachable effects of P.", "tokens": [50953, 400, 264, 9721, 4368, 300, 498, 264, 10862, 295, 1461, 430, 6, 366, 257, 25993, 295, 264, 10862, 295, 1461, 430, 11, 550, 264, 2524, 712, 5065, 295, 430, 6, 366, 44003, 18031, 281, 312, 257, 25993, 295, 264, 2524, 712, 5065, 295, 430, 13, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13847047906172902, "compression_ratio": 1.9617224880382775, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310954544142663e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 62588, "start": 625.88, "end": 628.3, "text": " I mean, it seems obvious on its face, right?", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 309, 2544, 6322, 322, 1080, 1851, 11, 558, 30, 50486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630944617000627, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609844367283187e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 62588, "start": 628.58, "end": 633.46, "text": " If a program doesn't have network access, it obviously can't leak data over the Internet.", "tokens": [50500, 759, 257, 1461, 1177, 380, 362, 3209, 2105, 11, 309, 2745, 393, 380, 17143, 1412, 670, 264, 7703, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630944617000627, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609844367283187e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 62588, "start": 633.58, "end": 633.8, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [50750, 4894, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630944617000627, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609844367283187e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 62588, "start": 633.92, "end": 634.68, "text": " It sounds simple.", "tokens": [50767, 467, 3263, 2199, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630944617000627, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609844367283187e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 62588, "start": 635.1, "end": 639.4399999999999, "text": " But Fliction is making a much sharper critique of modern software development here.", "tokens": [50826, 583, 3235, 4105, 307, 1455, 257, 709, 44670, 25673, 295, 4363, 4722, 3250, 510, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630944617000627, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609844367283187e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 62588, "start": 639.82, "end": 645.06, "text": " The paper is really pushing back against the whole era of massive dependency accumulation.", "tokens": [51062, 440, 3035, 307, 534, 7380, 646, 1970, 264, 1379, 4249, 295, 5994, 33621, 35647, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1630944617000627, "compression_ratio": 1.4734513274336283, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609844367283187e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 64506, "start": 645.06, "end": 646.3199999999999, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 50428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528301887141848, "compression_ratio": 1.6022304832713754, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389617086056465e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 64506, "start": 646.52, "end": 656.0799999999999, "text": " Think about the NPM ecosystem, or the constant parade of supply chain attacks, where some tiny package deep, deep in a dependency tree gets compromised.", "tokens": [50438, 6557, 466, 264, 426, 18819, 11311, 11, 420, 264, 5754, 26128, 295, 5847, 5021, 8122, 11, 689, 512, 5870, 7372, 2452, 11, 2452, 294, 257, 33621, 4230, 2170, 32463, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528301887141848, "compression_ratio": 1.6022304832713754, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389617086056465e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 64506, "start": 656.4, "end": 657.88, "text": " And suddenly everything is vulnerable.", "tokens": [50932, 400, 5800, 1203, 307, 10955, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528301887141848, "compression_ratio": 1.6022304832713754, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389617086056465e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 64506, "start": 658.1999999999999, "end": 658.4599999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51022, 1779, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528301887141848, "compression_ratio": 1.6022304832713754, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389617086056465e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 64506, "start": 659.04, "end": 665.9399999999999, "text": " Subtractive security argues that a patch dependency is never as safe as actively removing the dependency entirely.", "tokens": [51064, 8511, 83, 1897, 488, 3825, 38218, 300, 257, 9972, 33621, 307, 1128, 382, 3273, 382, 13022, 12720, 264, 33621, 7696, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528301887141848, "compression_ratio": 1.6022304832713754, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389617086056465e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 64506, "start": 666.3199999999999, "end": 666.56, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51428, 1779, 13, 51440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528301887141848, "compression_ratio": 1.6022304832713754, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389617086056465e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 64506, "start": 666.66, "end": 667.5, "text": " Just starve it out.", "tokens": [51445, 1449, 46755, 309, 484, 13, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528301887141848, "compression_ratio": 1.6022304832713754, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389617086056465e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 64506, "start": 667.9599999999999, "end": 672.06, "text": " And HelloTool achieves its security posture through that exact starvation.", "tokens": [51510, 400, 2425, 51, 1092, 3538, 977, 1080, 3825, 18502, 807, 300, 1900, 3543, 11116, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1528301887141848, "compression_ratio": 1.6022304832713754, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389617086056465e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 67206, "start": 672.06, "end": 676.0999999999999, "text": " It relies exclusively on the GoStandard library.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 30910, 20638, 322, 264, 1037, 4520, 474, 515, 6405, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12868524065204695, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 2.687057390829417e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 67206, "start": 676.7399999999999, "end": 679.14, "text": " Zero third-party runtime dependencies.", "tokens": [50599, 17182, 2636, 12, 23409, 34474, 36606, 13, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12868524065204695, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 2.687057390829417e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 67206, "start": 679.8399999999999, "end": 682.56, "text": " It is an architectural refusal of external complexity.", "tokens": [50754, 467, 307, 364, 26621, 48948, 295, 8320, 14024, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12868524065204695, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 2.687057390829417e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 67206, "start": 683.18, "end": 691.0799999999999, "text": " By aggressively stripping away capabilities, it reduces the surface area of reachable effects to a manageable, auditable domain.", "tokens": [50921, 3146, 32024, 3575, 3759, 1314, 10862, 11, 309, 18081, 264, 3753, 1859, 295, 2524, 712, 5065, 281, 257, 38798, 11, 2379, 16772, 9274, 13, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12868524065204695, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 2.687057390829417e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 67206, "start": 691.38, "end": 693.5799999999999, "text": " But Fliction is careful to bound this claim, aren't they?", "tokens": [51331, 583, 3235, 4105, 307, 5026, 281, 5472, 341, 3932, 11, 3212, 380, 436, 30, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12868524065204695, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 2.687057390829417e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 67206, "start": 693.5999999999999, "end": 694.16, "text": " Yeah, they are.", "tokens": [51442, 865, 11, 436, 366, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12868524065204695, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 2.687057390829417e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 67206, "start": 694.54, "end": 698.76, "text": " The paper explicitly states that this capability removal is a reduction in reachable effect.", "tokens": [51489, 440, 3035, 20803, 4368, 300, 341, 13759, 17933, 307, 257, 11004, 294, 2524, 712, 1802, 13, 51700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12868524065204695, "compression_ratio": 1.6043956043956045, "no_speech_prob": 2.687057390829417e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 69876, "start": 698.76, "end": 702.26, "text": " It's not a universal proof that everything remaining inside the boundary is safe.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 406, 257, 11455, 8177, 300, 1203, 8877, 1854, 264, 12866, 307, 3273, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649357375278267, "compression_ratio": 1.5564853556485356, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083389362633545e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 69876, "start": 702.36, "end": 702.46, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50545, 1779, 13, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649357375278267, "compression_ratio": 1.5564853556485356, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083389362633545e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 69876, "start": 702.5, "end": 703.58, "text": " It's a localized discipline.", "tokens": [50552, 467, 311, 257, 44574, 13635, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649357375278267, "compression_ratio": 1.5564853556485356, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083389362633545e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 69876, "start": 703.84, "end": 704.22, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50619, 7587, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649357375278267, "compression_ratio": 1.5564853556485356, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083389362633545e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 69876, "start": 704.7, "end": 709.26, "text": " It doesn't mean the code is flawless, just that its potential blast radius is strictly contained.", "tokens": [50662, 467, 1177, 380, 914, 264, 3089, 307, 45693, 11, 445, 300, 1080, 3995, 12035, 15845, 307, 20792, 16212, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649357375278267, "compression_ratio": 1.5564853556485356, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083389362633545e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 69876, "start": 709.68, "end": 713.6, "text": " And we see this containment most vividly at the program's release boundary.", "tokens": [50911, 400, 321, 536, 341, 44058, 881, 23603, 356, 412, 264, 1461, 311, 4374, 12866, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649357375278267, "compression_ratio": 1.5564853556485356, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083389362633545e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 69876, "start": 714.46, "end": 717.34, "text": " This is where HelloTool really proves its point.", "tokens": [51150, 639, 307, 689, 2425, 51, 1092, 534, 25019, 1080, 935, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649357375278267, "compression_ratio": 1.5564853556485356, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083389362633545e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 69876, "start": 717.4399999999999, "end": 718.36, "text": " At the release script.", "tokens": [51299, 1711, 264, 4374, 5755, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11649357375278267, "compression_ratio": 1.5564853556485356, "no_speech_prob": 2.4083389362633545e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 71836, "start": 718.36, "end": 723.04, "text": " So the management script will vet the code, run the tests, and compile the binary.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 4592, 5755, 486, 12423, 264, 3089, 11, 1190, 264, 6921, 11, 293, 31413, 264, 17434, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17885598049888127, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039822665879337e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 71836, "start": 723.5600000000001, "end": 728.52, "text": " It will even create a cryptographically signed local git tag to verify the release.", "tokens": [50625, 467, 486, 754, 1884, 257, 9844, 3108, 984, 8175, 2654, 18331, 6162, 281, 16888, 264, 4374, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17885598049888127, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039822665879337e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 71836, "start": 729.46, "end": 730.98, "text": " But then it hits a hard stop.", "tokens": [50920, 583, 550, 309, 8664, 257, 1152, 1590, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17885598049888127, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039822665879337e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 71836, "start": 731.72, "end": 736.86, "text": " It absolutely refuses to automatically push that tag to a remote server.", "tokens": [51033, 467, 3122, 33222, 281, 6772, 2944, 300, 6162, 281, 257, 8607, 7154, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17885598049888127, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039822665879337e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 71836, "start": 737.0600000000001, "end": 740.42, "text": " And that hard stop is the manifestation of operational validity.", "tokens": [51300, 400, 300, 1152, 1590, 307, 264, 29550, 295, 16607, 40943, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17885598049888127, "compression_ratio": 1.6057692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 2.0039822665879337e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 74042, "start": 740.42, "end": 748.3399999999999, "text": " To explain the theoretical weight of this stopping point, Fliction brings in Helen Nissenbaum's concept of contextual integrity.", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 2903, 264, 20864, 3364, 295, 341, 12767, 935, 11, 3235, 4105, 5607, 294, 26294, 426, 10987, 46641, 311, 3410, 295, 35526, 16000, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11271898235593523, "compression_ratio": 1.6918032786885246, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549643820819692e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 74042, "start": 748.74, "end": 750.78, "text": " Okay, remind me how Nissenbaum frames that.", "tokens": [50781, 1033, 11, 4160, 385, 577, 426, 10987, 46641, 12083, 300, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11271898235593523, "compression_ratio": 1.6918032786885246, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549643820819692e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 74042, "start": 750.9599999999999, "end": 755.92, "text": " So Nissenbaum's framework argues that privacy and security aren't about absolute secrecy.", "tokens": [50892, 407, 426, 10987, 46641, 311, 8388, 38218, 300, 11427, 293, 3825, 3212, 380, 466, 8236, 34432, 1344, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11271898235593523, "compression_ratio": 1.6918032786885246, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549643820819692e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 74042, "start": 756.0799999999999, "end": 760.5799999999999, "text": " They're about ensuring that information flows appropriately within strictly defined contexts.", "tokens": [51148, 814, 434, 466, 16882, 300, 1589, 12867, 23505, 1951, 20792, 7642, 30628, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11271898235593523, "compression_ratio": 1.6918032786885246, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549643820819692e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 74042, "start": 760.8, "end": 761.9599999999999, "text": " Right, context is everything.", "tokens": [51384, 1779, 11, 4319, 307, 1203, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11271898235593523, "compression_ratio": 1.6918032786885246, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549643820819692e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 74042, "start": 762.04, "end": 762.4, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51446, 7587, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11271898235593523, "compression_ratio": 1.6918032786885246, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549643820819692e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 74042, "start": 762.56, "end": 768.54, "text": " A flow that is perfectly appropriate in one context becomes a violation the very moment it crosses into a different one.", "tokens": [51472, 316, 3095, 300, 307, 6239, 6854, 294, 472, 4319, 3643, 257, 22840, 264, 588, 1623, 309, 28467, 666, 257, 819, 472, 13, 51771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11271898235593523, "compression_ratio": 1.6918032786885246, "no_speech_prob": 1.5549643820819692e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 76854, "start": 768.54, "end": 778.26, "text": " Okay, so creating a signed local git tag is an action that is entirely acceptable, and in fact necessary, within the local informational boundary of the developer's machine.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 4084, 257, 8175, 2654, 18331, 6162, 307, 364, 3069, 300, 307, 7696, 15513, 11, 293, 294, 1186, 4818, 11, 1951, 264, 2654, 49391, 12866, 295, 264, 10754, 311, 3479, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747755175051482, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551318471503707e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 76854, "start": 778.52, "end": 780.24, "text": " Right, it executes flawlessly there.", "tokens": [50864, 1779, 11, 309, 4454, 1819, 13717, 12048, 456, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747755175051482, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551318471503707e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 76854, "start": 780.36, "end": 791.3399999999999, "text": " But HelloTool recognizes that local validity does not automatically grant the authority to transmit that information across a network boundary to a public repository.", "tokens": [50956, 583, 2425, 51, 1092, 26564, 300, 2654, 40943, 775, 406, 6772, 6386, 264, 8281, 281, 17831, 300, 1589, 2108, 257, 3209, 12866, 281, 257, 1908, 25841, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747755175051482, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551318471503707e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 76854, "start": 791.42, "end": 791.9, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51509, 7587, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747755175051482, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551318471503707e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 76854, "start": 792.3, "end": 795.54, "text": " It isolates local preparation from global effect.", "tokens": [51553, 467, 7381, 1024, 2654, 13081, 490, 4338, 1802, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11747755175051482, "compression_ratio": 1.5970695970695972, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551318471503707e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 79554, "start": 795.54, "end": 802.52, "text": " It forces the system to require an explicit, separate authorization to bridge those contexts.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 5874, 264, 1185, 281, 3651, 364, 13691, 11, 4994, 33697, 281, 7283, 729, 30628, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1544043024381002, "compression_ratio": 1.518987341772152, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118225661780453e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 79554, "start": 802.8, "end": 804.4, "text": " Think about when you write an angry email.", "tokens": [50728, 6557, 466, 562, 291, 2464, 364, 6884, 3796, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1544043024381002, "compression_ratio": 1.518987341772152, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118225661780453e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 79554, "start": 805.0999999999999, "end": 807.16, "text": " The save-as-draft function is a boundary.", "tokens": [50843, 440, 3155, 12, 296, 12, 67, 4469, 2445, 307, 257, 12866, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1544043024381002, "compression_ratio": 1.518987341772152, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118225661780453e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 79554, "start": 807.52, "end": 808.8199999999999, "text": " Oh, that's a perfect analogy.", "tokens": [50964, 876, 11, 300, 311, 257, 2176, 21663, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1544043024381002, "compression_ratio": 1.518987341772152, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118225661780453e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 79554, "start": 809.24, "end": 809.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51050, 1779, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1544043024381002, "compression_ratio": 1.518987341772152, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118225661780453e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 79554, "start": 809.98, "end": 812.88, "text": " Clicking send crosses into a totally new context.", "tokens": [51087, 8230, 278, 2845, 28467, 666, 257, 3879, 777, 4319, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1544043024381002, "compression_ratio": 1.518987341772152, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118225661780453e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 79554, "start": 813.4599999999999, "end": 817.3199999999999, "text": " So HelloTool is basically forcing a system to take a breath before hitting send.", "tokens": [51261, 407, 2425, 51, 1092, 307, 1936, 19030, 257, 1185, 281, 747, 257, 6045, 949, 8850, 2845, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1544043024381002, "compression_ratio": 1.518987341772152, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118225661780453e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 79554, "start": 817.5799999999999, "end": 818.38, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51467, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1544043024381002, "compression_ratio": 1.518987341772152, "no_speech_prob": 2.0118225661780453e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 81838, "start": 818.38, "end": 827.5, "text": " It proves that a system can validly execute a complex sequence of operations, record them locally, and still fundamentally lack the mandate to alter the external world.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 25019, 300, 257, 1185, 393, 7363, 356, 14483, 257, 3997, 8310, 295, 7705, 11, 2136, 552, 16143, 11, 293, 920, 17879, 5011, 264, 23885, 281, 11337, 264, 8320, 1002, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14750590435294217, "compression_ratio": 1.6775510204081632, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246519746523138e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 81838, "start": 828.02, "end": 832.72, "text": " Operational validity simply determines if an action can execute safely within its defined limits.", "tokens": [50847, 12480, 1478, 40943, 2935, 24799, 498, 364, 3069, 393, 14483, 11750, 1951, 1080, 7642, 10406, 13, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14750590435294217, "compression_ratio": 1.6775510204081632, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246519746523138e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 81838, "start": 832.98, "end": 834.54, "text": " Independent of whether it should be broadcast.", "tokens": [51095, 40310, 295, 1968, 309, 820, 312, 9975, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14750590435294217, "compression_ratio": 1.6775510204081632, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246519746523138e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 81838, "start": 834.76, "end": 835.2, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51184, 7587, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14750590435294217, "compression_ratio": 1.6775510204081632, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246519746523138e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 81838, "start": 835.48, "end": 836.72, "text": " Independent of the should.", "tokens": [51220, 40310, 295, 264, 820, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14750590435294217, "compression_ratio": 1.6775510204081632, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246519746523138e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 81838, "start": 836.98, "end": 839.92, "text": " Which exposes the massive limitation of operational validity.", "tokens": [51295, 3013, 1278, 4201, 264, 5994, 27432, 295, 16607, 40943, 13, 51442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14750590435294217, "compression_ratio": 1.6775510204081632, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246519746523138e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 83992, "start": 839.92, "end": 843.3, "text": " Because Go just executes the math perfectly and then it stops.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 1037, 445, 4454, 1819, 264, 5221, 6239, 293, 550, 309, 10094, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21829620567527977, "compression_ratio": 1.6475095785440612, "no_speech_prob": 2.167270703179458e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 83992, "start": 843.8199999999999, "end": 844.86, "text": " But execution is blind.", "tokens": [50560, 583, 15058, 307, 6865, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21829620567527977, "compression_ratio": 1.6475095785440612, "no_speech_prob": 2.167270703179458e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 83992, "start": 845.0799999999999, "end": 845.64, "text": " Totally blind.", "tokens": [50623, 22837, 6865, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21829620567527977, "compression_ratio": 1.6475095785440612, "no_speech_prob": 2.167270703179458e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 83992, "start": 845.7199999999999, "end": 849.8199999999999, "text": " A perfectly executed rule can still be a terrible, unjust rule.", "tokens": [50655, 316, 6239, 17577, 4978, 393, 920, 312, 257, 6237, 11, 37046, 4978, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21829620567527977, "compression_ratio": 1.6475095785440612, "no_speech_prob": 2.167270703179458e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 83992, "start": 850.9399999999999, "end": 853.18, "text": " How does the system actually weigh the context?", "tokens": [50916, 1012, 775, 264, 1185, 767, 13843, 264, 4319, 30, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21829620567527977, "compression_ratio": 1.6475095785440612, "no_speech_prob": 2.167270703179458e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 83992, "start": 853.86, "end": 858.5799999999999, "text": " How does it decide if a validly executed proposal actually deserves to become reality?", "tokens": [51062, 1012, 775, 309, 4536, 498, 257, 7363, 356, 17577, 11494, 767, 17037, 281, 1813, 4103, 30, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21829620567527977, "compression_ratio": 1.6475095785440612, "no_speech_prob": 2.167270703179458e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 83992, "start": 859.14, "end": 863.8, "text": " And that gap transitions us directly into the second layer of Fliction's architecture.", "tokens": [51326, 400, 300, 7417, 23767, 505, 3838, 666, 264, 1150, 4583, 295, 3235, 4105, 311, 9482, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21829620567527977, "compression_ratio": 1.6475095785440612, "no_speech_prob": 2.167270703179458e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 83992, "start": 864.28, "end": 864.78, "text": " Judgment.", "tokens": [51583, 7661, 10433, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21829620567527977, "compression_ratio": 1.6475095785440612, "no_speech_prob": 2.167270703179458e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 83992, "start": 864.9599999999999, "end": 866.04, "text": " Denoted by the letter J.", "tokens": [51617, 6458, 23325, 538, 264, 5063, 508, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21829620567527977, "compression_ratio": 1.6475095785440612, "no_speech_prob": 2.167270703179458e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 83992, "start": 866.26, "end": 867.0, "text": " Yes, J.", "tokens": [51682, 1079, 11, 508, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21829620567527977, "compression_ratio": 1.6475095785440612, "no_speech_prob": 2.167270703179458e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 86700, "start": 867.0, "end": 870.18, "text": " And to explore this, the paper shifts entirely.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 281, 6839, 341, 11, 264, 3035, 19201, 7696, 13, 50524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15721839365333018, "compression_ratio": 1.538812785388128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736393509078853e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 86700, "start": 870.6, "end": 874.62, "text": " Introducing the second program, Reality Permit, written in Perl.", "tokens": [50545, 27193, 2175, 264, 1150, 1461, 11, 33822, 41006, 270, 11, 3720, 294, 3026, 75, 13, 50746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15721839365333018, "compression_ratio": 1.538812785388128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736393509078853e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 86700, "start": 874.94, "end": 879.46, "text": " And the linguistic shift from Go to Perl is, like, conceptually load-bearing here.", "tokens": [50762, 400, 264, 43002, 5513, 490, 1037, 281, 3026, 75, 307, 11, 411, 11, 3410, 671, 3677, 12, 650, 1921, 510, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15721839365333018, "compression_ratio": 1.538812785388128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736393509078853e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 86700, "start": 879.5, "end": 880.54, "text": " Oh, it absolutely is.", "tokens": [50990, 876, 11, 309, 3122, 307, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15721839365333018, "compression_ratio": 1.538812785388128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736393509078853e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 86700, "start": 880.68, "end": 883.24, "text": " Go was chosen for its austere, strict utility.", "tokens": [51049, 1037, 390, 8614, 337, 1080, 34916, 323, 11, 10910, 14877, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15721839365333018, "compression_ratio": 1.538812785388128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736393509078853e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 86700, "start": 883.82, "end": 886.82, "text": " Perl, as Fliction describes it, is a textual machine.", "tokens": [51206, 3026, 75, 11, 382, 3235, 4105, 15626, 309, 11, 307, 257, 2487, 901, 3479, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15721839365333018, "compression_ratio": 1.538812785388128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736393509078853e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 86700, "start": 887.02, "end": 887.98, "text": " A textual machine.", "tokens": [51366, 316, 2487, 901, 3479, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15721839365333018, "compression_ratio": 1.538812785388128, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736393509078853e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 88798, "start": 887.98, "end": 893.1, "text": " It's a language historically built for aggressive string manipulation, for interpolating variables", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 2856, 16180, 3094, 337, 10762, 6798, 26475, 11, 337, 44902, 990, 9102, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10698563539529149, "compression_ratio": 1.5545454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758199424844356e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 88798, "start": 893.1, "end": 897.0, "text": " into massive blocks of text, and for assembling complex documents on the fly.", "tokens": [50621, 666, 5994, 8474, 295, 2487, 11, 293, 337, 43867, 3997, 8512, 322, 264, 3603, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10698563539529149, "compression_ratio": 1.5545454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758199424844356e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 88798, "start": 897.2, "end": 901.28, "text": " So if you want to generate administrative proclamations and official-sounding edicts and bureaucratic", "tokens": [50826, 407, 498, 291, 528, 281, 8460, 17900, 447, 3474, 335, 763, 293, 4783, 12, 82, 24625, 1257, 985, 82, 293, 26360, 25198, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10698563539529149, "compression_ratio": 1.5545454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758199424844356e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 88798, "start": 901.28, "end": 901.86, "text": " paperwork...", "tokens": [51030, 27953, 485, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10698563539529149, "compression_ratio": 1.5545454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758199424844356e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 88798, "start": 901.86, "end": 903.98, "text": " Perl is rhetorically the perfect tool for the job.", "tokens": [51059, 3026, 75, 307, 24182, 284, 984, 264, 2176, 2290, 337, 264, 1691, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10698563539529149, "compression_ratio": 1.5545454545454545, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758199424844356e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 90398, "start": 903.98, "end": 907.94, "text": " And the program Fliction builds with it is an incredible piece of technical satire.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 1461, 3235, 4105, 15182, 365, 309, 307, 364, 4651, 2522, 295, 6191, 3227, 621, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13643511603860295, "compression_ratio": 1.5338983050847457, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070486493415032e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 90398, "start": 907.94, "end": 913.4200000000001, "text": " I mean, Reality Permit instantiates a fictional bureaucracy called the Ministry of Possible Affairs.", "tokens": [50563, 286, 914, 11, 33822, 41006, 270, 9836, 72, 1024, 257, 28911, 44671, 1219, 264, 19720, 295, 430, 5785, 21721, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13643511603860295, "compression_ratio": 1.5338983050847457, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070486493415032e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 90398, "start": 913.76, "end": 914.54, "text": " It's so good.", "tokens": [50854, 467, 311, 370, 665, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13643511603860295, "compression_ratio": 1.5338983050847457, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070486493415032e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 90398, "start": 914.66, "end": 920.04, "text": " The program's entire function is to ingest a procedurally generated quote-unquote universe", "tokens": [50899, 440, 1461, 311, 2302, 2445, 307, 281, 3957, 377, 257, 6682, 6512, 10833, 6513, 12, 409, 25016, 6445, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13643511603860295, "compression_ratio": 1.5338983050847457, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070486493415032e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 90398, "start": 920.04, "end": 924.98, "text": " and compute whether that universe is approved or denied by the ministry.", "tokens": [51168, 293, 14722, 1968, 300, 6445, 307, 10826, 420, 17774, 538, 264, 15024, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13643511603860295, "compression_ratio": 1.5338983050847457, "no_speech_prob": 2.3070486493415032e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 92498, "start": 924.98, "end": 929.54, "text": " And the satire allows Fliction to isolate the mechanics of bureaucratic judgment without", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 3227, 621, 4045, 3235, 4105, 281, 25660, 264, 12939, 295, 26360, 25198, 12216, 1553, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973068237304688, "compression_ratio": 1.589171974522293, "no_speech_prob": 1.383020325866624e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 92498, "start": 929.54, "end": 932.8000000000001, "text": " getting bogged down in the specifics of real-world policy.", "tokens": [50593, 1242, 26132, 3004, 760, 294, 264, 28454, 295, 957, 12, 13217, 3897, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973068237304688, "compression_ratio": 1.589171974522293, "no_speech_prob": 1.383020325866624e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 92498, "start": 933.4200000000001, "end": 939.22, "text": " The script evaluates each proposed universe using this highly specific, hard-coded formula.", "tokens": [50787, 440, 5755, 6133, 1024, 1184, 10348, 6445, 1228, 341, 5405, 2685, 11, 1152, 12, 66, 12340, 8513, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973068237304688, "compression_ratio": 1.589171974522293, "no_speech_prob": 1.383020325866624e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 92498, "start": 939.5, "end": 941.76, "text": " Okay, walk me through the formula again, because it's hilarious.", "tokens": [51091, 1033, 11, 1792, 385, 807, 264, 8513, 797, 11, 570, 309, 311, 19796, 13, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973068237304688, "compression_ratio": 1.589171974522293, "no_speech_prob": 1.383020325866624e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 92498, "start": 941.94, "end": 945.1800000000001, "text": " So it assigns a score based on three numerical measurements.", "tokens": [51213, 407, 309, 6269, 82, 257, 6175, 2361, 322, 1045, 29054, 15383, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973068237304688, "compression_ratio": 1.589171974522293, "no_speech_prob": 1.383020325866624e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 92498, "start": 945.6800000000001, "end": 948.26, "text": " Coherence, majesty, and paperwork.", "tokens": [51400, 3066, 511, 655, 11, 32146, 11, 293, 27953, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973068237304688, "compression_ratio": 1.589171974522293, "no_speech_prob": 1.383020325866624e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 92498, "start": 948.58, "end": 953.9, "text": " I cannot emphasize enough how much I love that majesty and paperwork are treated as mathematically", "tokens": [51545, 286, 2644, 16078, 1547, 577, 709, 286, 959, 300, 32146, 293, 27953, 366, 8668, 382, 44003, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14973068237304688, "compression_ratio": 1.589171974522293, "no_speech_prob": 1.383020325866624e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 95390, "start": 953.9, "end": 957.36, "text": " equivalent vectors for determining the validity of a universe.", "tokens": [50365, 10344, 18875, 337, 23751, 264, 40943, 295, 257, 6445, 13, 50538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 95390, "start": 957.62, "end": 958.12, "text": " It's amazing.", "tokens": [50551, 467, 311, 2243, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 95390, "start": 958.26, "end": 963.5, "text": " So it takes the floor of the sum of coherence, majesty, and paperwork and divides it by three", "tokens": [50583, 407, 309, 2516, 264, 4123, 295, 264, 2408, 295, 26528, 655, 11, 32146, 11, 293, 27953, 293, 41347, 309, 538, 1045, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 95390, "start": 963.5, "end": 964.4399999999999, "text": " to find the average.", "tokens": [50845, 281, 915, 264, 4274, 13, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 95390, "start": 964.62, "end": 964.8, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50901, 1033, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 95390, "start": 965.1, "end": 969.26, "text": " But then it adds a flat seven points to the score if an appeal has been lodged, regardless", "tokens": [50925, 583, 550, 309, 10860, 257, 4962, 3407, 2793, 281, 264, 6175, 498, 364, 13668, 575, 668, 33311, 3004, 11, 10060, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 95390, "start": 969.26, "end": 971.6999999999999, "text": " of the actual content or merit of the appeal.", "tokens": [51133, 295, 264, 3539, 2701, 420, 24527, 295, 264, 13668, 13, 51255], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 95390, "start": 971.6999999999999, "end": 974.4399999999999, "text": " Just a flat seven points for the existence of an appeal.", "tokens": [51255, 1449, 257, 4962, 3407, 2793, 337, 264, 9123, 295, 364, 13668, 13, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 95390, "start": 974.86, "end": 975.3, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51413, 7587, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 95390, "start": 975.72, "end": 980.24, "text": " And if the final tabulated score is 55 or greater, the universe is granted a permit.", "tokens": [51456, 400, 498, 264, 2572, 4421, 6987, 6175, 307, 12330, 420, 5044, 11, 264, 6445, 307, 12344, 257, 13423, 13, 51682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 95390, "start": 980.68, "end": 983.74, "text": " If it falls below 55, the universe is denied.", "tokens": [51704, 759, 309, 8804, 2507, 12330, 11, 264, 6445, 307, 17774, 13, 51857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14631949225775628, "compression_ratio": 1.729641693811075, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077976402837813e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 98390, "start": 983.9, "end": 987.52, "text": " And the script issues a procedurally generated remedial measure.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 5755, 2663, 257, 6682, 6512, 10833, 28718, 831, 3481, 13, 50546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20165361404418947, "compression_ratio": 1.5546558704453441, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423720022862298e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 98390, "start": 988.24, "end": 993.24, "text": " And to ensure the system operates consistently, the Pearl script uses a linear congruential", "tokens": [50582, 400, 281, 5586, 264, 1185, 22577, 14961, 11, 264, 24639, 5755, 4960, 257, 8213, 8882, 84, 2549, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20165361404418947, "compression_ratio": 1.5546558704453441, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423720022862298e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 98390, "start": 993.24, "end": 997.34, "text": " generator, an LCG, initialized by a highly specific seed.", "tokens": [50832, 19265, 11, 364, 42198, 38, 11, 5883, 1602, 538, 257, 5405, 2685, 8871, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20165361404418947, "compression_ratio": 1.5546558704453441, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423720022862298e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 98390, "start": 997.5, "end": 998.48, "text": " Seed 1982.", "tokens": [51045, 1100, 292, 31352, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20165361404418947, "compression_ratio": 1.5546558704453441, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423720022862298e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 98390, "start": 998.9599999999999, "end": 1000.0, "text": " Seed 1982.", "tokens": [51118, 1100, 292, 31352, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20165361404418947, "compression_ratio": 1.5546558704453441, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423720022862298e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 98390, "start": 1000.48, "end": 1000.62, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51194, 1779, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20165361404418947, "compression_ratio": 1.5546558704453441, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423720022862298e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 98390, "start": 1000.74, "end": 1005.1999999999999, "text": " Because of how the LCG works, a given permit number and appeal state will guarantee the", "tokens": [51207, 1436, 295, 577, 264, 42198, 38, 1985, 11, 257, 2212, 13423, 1230, 293, 13668, 1785, 486, 10815, 264, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20165361404418947, "compression_ratio": 1.5546558704453441, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423720022862298e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 98390, "start": 1005.1999999999999, "end": 1007.16, "text": " exact same procedural generation.", "tokens": [51430, 1900, 912, 43951, 5125, 13, 51528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20165361404418947, "compression_ratio": 1.5546558704453441, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423720022862298e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 98390, "start": 1007.3, "end": 1008.24, "text": " Every single time.", "tokens": [51535, 2048, 2167, 565, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20165361404418947, "compression_ratio": 1.5546558704453441, "no_speech_prob": 1.6423720022862298e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 100824, "start": 1008.24, "end": 1013.58, "text": " It will yield the exact same values for majesty and paperwork and culminate in the exact same", "tokens": [50365, 467, 486, 11257, 264, 1900, 912, 4190, 337, 32146, 293, 27953, 293, 28583, 473, 294, 264, 1900, 912, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13413800363955292, "compression_ratio": 1.626086956521739, "no_speech_prob": 1.8504505653466063e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 100824, "start": 1013.58, "end": 1014.4, "text": " final ruling.", "tokens": [50632, 2572, 21437, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13413800363955292, "compression_ratio": 1.626086956521739, "no_speech_prob": 1.8504505653466063e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 100824, "start": 1014.76, "end": 1017.7, "text": " It is the ultimate manifestation of procedural regularity.", "tokens": [50691, 467, 307, 264, 9705, 29550, 295, 43951, 3890, 507, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13413800363955292, "compression_ratio": 1.626086956521739, "no_speech_prob": 1.8504505653466063e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 100824, "start": 1018.16, "end": 1023.38, "text": " Equivalent inputs will, without fail, yield equivalent outputs stretching into infinity.", "tokens": [50861, 15624, 3576, 317, 15743, 486, 11, 1553, 3061, 11, 11257, 10344, 23930, 19632, 666, 13202, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13413800363955292, "compression_ratio": 1.626086956521739, "no_speech_prob": 1.8504505653466063e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 100824, "start": 1023.6, "end": 1023.76, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51133, 1033, 13, 51141], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13413800363955292, "compression_ratio": 1.626086956521739, "no_speech_prob": 1.8504505653466063e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 100824, "start": 1023.78, "end": 1024.9, "text": " Here's where it gets really interesting.", "tokens": [51142, 1692, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13413800363955292, "compression_ratio": 1.626086956521739, "no_speech_prob": 1.8504505653466063e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 100824, "start": 1025.02, "end": 1026.74, "text": " Let me challenge the premise of the paper here for a moment.", "tokens": [51204, 961, 385, 3430, 264, 22045, 295, 264, 3035, 510, 337, 257, 1623, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13413800363955292, "compression_ratio": 1.626086956521739, "no_speech_prob": 1.8504505653466063e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 100824, "start": 1026.74, "end": 1027.16, "text": " Go for it.", "tokens": [51290, 1037, 337, 309, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13413800363955292, "compression_ratio": 1.626086956521739, "no_speech_prob": 1.8504505653466063e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 102716, "start": 1027.16, "end": 1032.88, "text": " We spend so much time in technology circles criticizing human bias, like judges who give harsher sentences", "tokens": [50365, 492, 3496, 370, 709, 565, 294, 2899, 13040, 45474, 1952, 12577, 11, 411, 14449, 567, 976, 276, 685, 511, 16579, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17199187583111702, "compression_ratio": 1.492063492063492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310989238612183e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 102716, "start": 1032.88, "end": 1036.16, "text": " before lunch, or loan officers who hold implicit prejudices.", "tokens": [50651, 949, 6349, 11, 420, 10529, 9199, 567, 1797, 26947, 23121, 1473, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17199187583111702, "compression_ratio": 1.492063492063492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310989238612183e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 102716, "start": 1036.3400000000001, "end": 1036.46, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50824, 1779, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17199187583111702, "compression_ratio": 1.492063492063492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310989238612183e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 102716, "start": 1036.5400000000002, "end": 1037.76, "text": " The noise in human judgment.", "tokens": [50834, 440, 5658, 294, 1952, 12216, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17199187583111702, "compression_ratio": 1.492063492063492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310989238612183e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 102716, "start": 1038.1200000000001, "end": 1038.6200000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50913, 7587, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17199187583111702, "compression_ratio": 1.492063492063492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310989238612183e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 102716, "start": 1039.2, "end": 1045.1000000000001, "text": " So the Pearl script's formula, driven by Seed 1982, always yields the exact same result", "tokens": [50967, 407, 264, 24639, 5755, 311, 8513, 11, 9555, 538, 1100, 292, 31352, 11, 1009, 32168, 264, 1900, 912, 1874, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17199187583111702, "compression_ratio": 1.492063492063492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310989238612183e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 102716, "start": 1045.1000000000001, "end": 1046.6000000000001, "text": " for the exact same input.", "tokens": [51262, 337, 264, 1900, 912, 4846, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17199187583111702, "compression_ratio": 1.492063492063492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310989238612183e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 102716, "start": 1047.3200000000002, "end": 1049.44, "text": " Isn't that the definition of procedural fairness?", "tokens": [51373, 6998, 380, 300, 264, 7123, 295, 43951, 29765, 30, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17199187583111702, "compression_ratio": 1.492063492063492, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310989238612183e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 104944, "start": 1049.44, "end": 1053.5800000000002, "text": " We rely on algorithms specifically to enforce determinism.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 10687, 322, 14642, 4682, 281, 24825, 15957, 1434, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20383494609111064, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.883438283806216e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 104944, "start": 1053.78, "end": 1058.54, "text": " If two people submit the exact same universe to the ministry, they get the exact same ruling.", "tokens": [50582, 759, 732, 561, 10315, 264, 1900, 912, 6445, 281, 264, 15024, 11, 436, 483, 264, 1900, 912, 21437, 13, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20383494609111064, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.883438283806216e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 104944, "start": 1059.0, "end": 1063.18, "text": " Isn't that consistency the very foundation of legitimate administration?", "tokens": [50843, 6998, 380, 300, 14416, 264, 588, 7030, 295, 17956, 7236, 30, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20383494609111064, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.883438283806216e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 104944, "start": 1063.8600000000001, "end": 1066.64, "text": " That is precisely the trap that Flixin is highlighting.", "tokens": [51086, 663, 307, 13402, 264, 11487, 300, 3235, 970, 259, 307, 26551, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20383494609111064, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.883438283806216e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 104944, "start": 1066.88, "end": 1071.16, "text": " You are observing flawless procedural determinism and mistaking it for legitimacy.", "tokens": [51237, 509, 366, 22107, 45693, 43951, 15957, 1434, 293, 3544, 2456, 309, 337, 41339, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20383494609111064, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.883438283806216e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 104944, "start": 1071.5800000000002, "end": 1075.22, "text": " And the paper draws a hard, formal line to break that illusion.", "tokens": [51472, 400, 264, 3035, 20045, 257, 1152, 11, 9860, 1622, 281, 1821, 300, 18854, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20383494609111064, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.883438283806216e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 104944, "start": 1075.8, "end": 1078.52, "text": " Let's look at the mechanism of the math Flixin uses here.", "tokens": [51683, 961, 311, 574, 412, 264, 7513, 295, 264, 5221, 3235, 970, 259, 4960, 510, 13, 51819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20383494609111064, "compression_ratio": 1.6643835616438356, "no_speech_prob": 1.883438283806216e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 107852, "start": 1079.28, "end": 1083.68, "text": " Determinism of F equals 1 does not imply legitimacy of F equals 1.", "tokens": [50403, 4237, 966, 259, 1434, 295, 479, 6915, 502, 775, 406, 33616, 41339, 295, 479, 6915, 502, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16202394104003906, "compression_ratio": 1.7700348432055748, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759069818352625e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 107852, "start": 1083.92, "end": 1086.52, "text": " D-day equals 1 does not imply leg F equals 1.", "tokens": [50635, 413, 12, 810, 6915, 502, 775, 406, 33616, 1676, 479, 6915, 502, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16202394104003906, "compression_ratio": 1.7700348432055748, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759069818352625e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 107852, "start": 1086.58, "end": 1087.06, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50768, 7587, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16202394104003906, "compression_ratio": 1.7700348432055748, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759069818352625e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 107852, "start": 1087.26, "end": 1091.22, "text": " A function can be perfectly deterministic, repeating its output with crystalline perfection", "tokens": [50802, 316, 2445, 393, 312, 6239, 15957, 3142, 11, 18617, 1080, 5598, 365, 31924, 533, 19708, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16202394104003906, "compression_ratio": 1.7700348432055748, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759069818352625e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 107852, "start": 1091.22, "end": 1094.0, "text": " while lacking any inherent legitimacy whatsoever.", "tokens": [51000, 1339, 20889, 604, 26387, 41339, 17076, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16202394104003906, "compression_ratio": 1.7700348432055748, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759069818352625e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 107852, "start": 1094.28, "end": 1097.52, "text": " Because the code itself has no awareness of justice or context.", "tokens": [51153, 1436, 264, 3089, 2564, 575, 572, 8888, 295, 6118, 420, 4319, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16202394104003906, "compression_ratio": 1.7700348432055748, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759069818352625e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 107852, "start": 1097.82, "end": 1100.92, "text": " It only knows that its arbitrariness is perfectly repeatable.", "tokens": [51330, 467, 787, 3255, 300, 1080, 14931, 5352, 1324, 307, 6239, 7149, 712, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16202394104003906, "compression_ratio": 1.7700348432055748, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759069818352625e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 107852, "start": 1101.06, "end": 1101.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51492, 7587, 13, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16202394104003906, "compression_ratio": 1.7700348432055748, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759069818352625e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 107852, "start": 1101.7, "end": 1103.56, "text": " Look at the internal logic of the ministry's formula.", "tokens": [51524, 2053, 412, 264, 6920, 9952, 295, 264, 15024, 311, 8513, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16202394104003906, "compression_ratio": 1.7700348432055748, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759069818352625e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 107852, "start": 1103.98, "end": 1107.32, "text": " Why is majesty a valid metric for evaluating a reality?", "tokens": [51638, 1545, 307, 32146, 257, 7363, 20678, 337, 27479, 257, 4103, 30, 51805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16202394104003906, "compression_ratio": 1.7700348432055748, "no_speech_prob": 1.8759069818352625e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 110732, "start": 1107.32, "end": 1113.84, "text": " Why does an appeal mechanically grant exactly seven points, completely ignoring the textual", "tokens": [50365, 1545, 775, 364, 13668, 4236, 984, 6386, 2293, 3407, 2793, 11, 2584, 26258, 264, 2487, 901, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1560677319038205, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903433506023415e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 110732, "start": 1113.84, "end": 1115.1399999999999, "text": " argument of the appeal itself?", "tokens": [50691, 6770, 295, 264, 13668, 2564, 30, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1560677319038205, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903433506023415e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 110732, "start": 1115.6799999999998, "end": 1118.4399999999998, "text": " Why is the threshold for existence exactly 55?", "tokens": [50783, 1545, 307, 264, 14678, 337, 9123, 2293, 12330, 30, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1560677319038205, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903433506023415e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 110732, "start": 1118.76, "end": 1119.96, "text": " It's completely arbitrary.", "tokens": [50937, 467, 311, 2584, 23211, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1560677319038205, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903433506023415e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 110732, "start": 1120.58, "end": 1126.26, "text": " The determinism of the LCG simply masks the fact that the foundational criteria are entirely", "tokens": [51028, 440, 15957, 1434, 295, 264, 42198, 38, 2935, 11830, 264, 1186, 300, 264, 32195, 11101, 366, 7696, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1560677319038205, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903433506023415e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 110732, "start": 1126.26, "end": 1127.06, "text": " fabricated.", "tokens": [51312, 7253, 770, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1560677319038205, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903433506023415e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 110732, "start": 1127.1599999999999, "end": 1130.0, "text": " It's a mathematical execution of pure absurdity.", "tokens": [51357, 467, 311, 257, 18894, 15058, 295, 6075, 19774, 507, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1560677319038205, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.8903433506023415e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 113000, "start": 1130.0, "end": 1133.96, "text": " But it doesn't feel absurd when it's codified into a script.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 309, 1177, 380, 841, 19774, 562, 309, 311, 17656, 2587, 666, 257, 5755, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208862266155205, "compression_ratio": 1.5756457564575646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279280220203197e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 113000, "start": 1134.28, "end": 1139.88, "text": " And that is where Flixin brings in the sociological framework of Jeffrey C. Boker and Susan Lee Starr,", "tokens": [50579, 400, 300, 307, 689, 3235, 970, 259, 5607, 294, 264, 3075, 4383, 8388, 295, 28721, 383, 13, 363, 16722, 293, 15160, 6957, 745, 2284, 11, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208862266155205, "compression_ratio": 1.5756457564575646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279280220203197e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 113000, "start": 1140.5, "end": 1143.86, "text": " specifically referencing their foundational book, Sorting Things Out.", "tokens": [50890, 4682, 40582, 641, 32195, 1446, 11, 26149, 278, 9514, 5925, 13, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208862266155205, "compression_ratio": 1.5756457564575646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279280220203197e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 113000, "start": 1144.24, "end": 1144.68, "text": " Right book.", "tokens": [51077, 1779, 1446, 13, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208862266155205, "compression_ratio": 1.5756457564575646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279280220203197e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 113000, "start": 1144.82, "end": 1150.32, "text": " Boker and Starr analyze how infrastructure works, and their central thesis is that classifications", "tokens": [51106, 363, 16722, 293, 745, 2284, 12477, 577, 6896, 1985, 11, 293, 641, 5777, 22288, 307, 300, 1508, 7833, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208862266155205, "compression_ratio": 1.5756457564575646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279280220203197e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 113000, "start": 1150.32, "end": 1154.6, "text": " and categories only acquire force when an infrastructure makes them consequential.", "tokens": [51381, 293, 10479, 787, 20001, 3464, 562, 364, 6896, 1669, 552, 7242, 2549, 13, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13208862266155205, "compression_ratio": 1.5756457564575646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279280220203197e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 115460, "start": 1154.6, "end": 1160.2199999999998, "text": " So a category like majesty is just a whimsical thought experiment until a computational infrastructure", "tokens": [50365, 407, 257, 7719, 411, 32146, 307, 445, 257, 315, 49945, 1194, 5120, 1826, 257, 28270, 6896, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577460007234053, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 2.7615260338870184e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 115460, "start": 1160.2199999999998, "end": 1162.8, "text": " uses it to approve or deny a permit.", "tokens": [50646, 4960, 309, 281, 18827, 420, 15744, 257, 13423, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577460007234053, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 2.7615260338870184e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 115460, "start": 1163.02, "end": 1163.4199999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50786, 7587, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577460007234053, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 2.7615260338870184e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 115460, "start": 1163.8999999999999, "end": 1166.08, "text": " The Perl script is a miniature infrastructure.", "tokens": [50830, 440, 3026, 75, 5755, 307, 257, 34674, 6896, 13, 50939], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577460007234053, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 2.7615260338870184e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 115460, "start": 1166.52, "end": 1170.8, "text": " It takes whimsical, arbitrary categories, cements them in code, and converts them into", "tokens": [50961, 467, 2516, 315, 49945, 11, 23211, 10479, 11, 269, 6400, 552, 294, 3089, 11, 293, 38874, 552, 666, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577460007234053, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 2.7615260338870184e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 115460, "start": 1170.8, "end": 1173.32, "text": " an official ruling with a binding remedial act.", "tokens": [51175, 364, 4783, 21437, 365, 257, 17359, 28718, 831, 605, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577460007234053, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 2.7615260338870184e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 115460, "start": 1173.6, "end": 1175.82, "text": " Infrastructure makes the invisible consequential.", "tokens": [51315, 38425, 2885, 1669, 264, 14603, 7242, 2549, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1577460007234053, "compression_ratio": 1.6170212765957446, "no_speech_prob": 2.7615260338870184e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 117582, "start": 1175.82, "end": 1180.62, "text": " The fact that the Perl script evaluates paperwork isn't just a joke about bureaucracy.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1186, 300, 264, 3026, 75, 5755, 6133, 1024, 27953, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 7647, 466, 44671, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515084463974525, "compression_ratio": 1.685512367491166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014009558863341e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 117582, "start": 1181.32, "end": 1185.78, "text": " It exposes how computation doesn't inherently dismantle bureaucratic absurdity.", "tokens": [50640, 467, 1278, 4201, 577, 24903, 1177, 380, 27993, 30506, 306, 26360, 25198, 19774, 507, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515084463974525, "compression_ratio": 1.685512367491166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014009558863341e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 117582, "start": 1186.6, "end": 1188.74, "text": " In many ways, computation perfects it.", "tokens": [50904, 682, 867, 2098, 11, 24903, 2176, 82, 309, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515084463974525, "compression_ratio": 1.685512367491166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014009558863341e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 117582, "start": 1188.9399999999998, "end": 1189.6599999999999, "text": " It automates it.", "tokens": [51021, 467, 3553, 1024, 309, 13, 51057], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515084463974525, "compression_ratio": 1.685512367491166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014009558863341e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 117582, "start": 1189.8799999999999, "end": 1195.06, "text": " It strips away the human elements of fatigue or discretion and replaces them with an inescapable,", "tokens": [51068, 467, 19842, 1314, 264, 1952, 4959, 295, 20574, 420, 30140, 293, 46734, 552, 365, 364, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 11, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515084463974525, "compression_ratio": 1.685512367491166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014009558863341e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 117582, "start": 1195.3, "end": 1197.7, "text": " flawless execution of arbitrary rules.", "tokens": [51339, 45693, 15058, 295, 23211, 4474, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515084463974525, "compression_ratio": 1.685512367491166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014009558863341e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 117582, "start": 1198.32, "end": 1202.4399999999998, "text": " Flixin points out that there is a unit test in the Perl source code literally named", "tokens": [51490, 3235, 970, 259, 2793, 484, 300, 456, 307, 257, 4985, 1500, 294, 264, 3026, 75, 4009, 3089, 3736, 4926, 51696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515084463974525, "compression_ratio": 1.685512367491166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014009558863341e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 117582, "start": 1202.4399999999998, "end": 1204.9199999999998, "text": " the bureaucracy is deterministic.", "tokens": [51696, 264, 44671, 307, 15957, 3142, 13, 51820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1515084463974525, "compression_ratio": 1.685512367491166, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014009558863341e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 120492, "start": 1204.92, "end": 1205.88, "text": " That's so good.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 370, 665, 13, 50413], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420776533043903, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582861807837526e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 120492, "start": 1206.26, "end": 1209.98, "text": " That single test condenses the entire philosophical argument of this layer.", "tokens": [50432, 663, 2167, 1500, 2224, 9085, 264, 2302, 25066, 6770, 295, 341, 4583, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420776533043903, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582861807837526e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 120492, "start": 1210.48, "end": 1214.9, "text": " The ministry cannot defend its ruling by claiming human discretion, changing circumstances,", "tokens": [50643, 440, 15024, 2644, 8602, 1080, 21437, 538, 19232, 1952, 30140, 11, 4473, 9121, 11, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420776533043903, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582861807837526e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 120492, "start": 1215.16, "end": 1216.14, "text": " or moral nuance.", "tokens": [50877, 420, 9723, 42625, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420776533043903, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582861807837526e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 120492, "start": 1216.5800000000002, "end": 1219.24, "text": " Its absurdity is flawlessly repeatable.", "tokens": [50948, 6953, 19774, 507, 307, 13717, 12048, 7149, 712, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420776533043903, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582861807837526e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 120492, "start": 1219.74, "end": 1223.46, "text": " Determinism without context is just a machine repeating a mistake forever.", "tokens": [51106, 4237, 966, 259, 1434, 1553, 4319, 307, 445, 257, 3479, 18617, 257, 6146, 5680, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420776533043903, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582861807837526e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 120492, "start": 1223.6000000000001, "end": 1224.16, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51299, 7587, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420776533043903, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582861807837526e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 120492, "start": 1224.54, "end": 1229.0600000000002, "text": " So if determinism isn't the bedrock of legitimacy, what actually bridges that gap?", "tokens": [51346, 407, 498, 15957, 1434, 1943, 380, 264, 2901, 17799, 295, 41339, 11, 437, 767, 21114, 300, 7417, 30, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420776533043903, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582861807837526e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 120492, "start": 1229.64, "end": 1234.74, "text": " How does a system prove that its judgments are mathematically consistent and institutionally valid?", "tokens": [51601, 1012, 775, 257, 1185, 7081, 300, 1080, 40337, 366, 44003, 8398, 293, 7818, 379, 7363, 30, 51856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420776533043903, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582861807837526e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 123492, "start": 1234.92, "end": 1240.38, "text": " To solve this, Flixin introduces the formal concept of the policy bundle, represented mathematically", "tokens": [50365, 1407, 5039, 341, 11, 3235, 970, 259, 31472, 264, 9860, 3410, 295, 264, 3897, 24438, 11, 10379, 44003, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13923754475333475, "compression_ratio": 1.1111111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 3.5591605617585342e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 124038, "start": 1240.38, "end": 1241.88, "text": " by the Greek letter pi.", "tokens": [50365, 538, 264, 10281, 5063, 3895, 13, 50440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2312019151799819, "compression_ratio": 1.453551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 3.0923308618618917e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 124038, "start": 1242.1200000000001, "end": 1242.42, "text": " Pi.", "tokens": [50452, 17741, 13, 50467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2312019151799819, "compression_ratio": 1.453551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 3.0923308618618917e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 124038, "start": 1242.6000000000001, "end": 1248.24, "text": " The paper argues that for a decision system to possess actual legitimacy, it must make its", "tokens": [50476, 440, 3035, 38218, 300, 337, 257, 3537, 1185, 281, 17490, 3539, 41339, 11, 309, 1633, 652, 1080, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2312019151799819, "compression_ratio": 1.453551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 3.0923308618618917e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 124038, "start": 1248.24, "end": 1251.5200000000002, "text": " surrounding policy context explicit and machine readable.", "tokens": [50758, 11498, 3897, 4319, 13691, 293, 3479, 49857, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2312019151799819, "compression_ratio": 1.453551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 3.0923308618618917e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 124038, "start": 1252.2800000000002, "end": 1257.0600000000002, "text": " A policy bundle is not just the executable predicate, the code of the rule itself.", "tokens": [50960, 316, 3897, 24438, 307, 406, 445, 264, 7568, 712, 3852, 8700, 11, 264, 3089, 295, 264, 4978, 2564, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2312019151799819, "compression_ratio": 1.453551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 3.0923308618618917e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 124038, "start": 1257.2, "end": 1257.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51206, 1779, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2312019151799819, "compression_ratio": 1.453551912568306, "no_speech_prob": 3.0923308618618917e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 125740, "start": 1257.4, "end": 1258.94, "text": " It's not just the if-them statement.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 406, 445, 264, 498, 12, 47959, 5629, 13, 50442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13844722356551734, "compression_ratio": 1.5485436893203883, "no_speech_prob": 2.64544072411943e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 125740, "start": 1258.94, "end": 1259.42, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50442, 7587, 13, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13844722356551734, "compression_ratio": 1.5485436893203883, "no_speech_prob": 2.64544072411943e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 125740, "start": 1259.42, "end": 1264.48, "text": " The bundle must contain the plain text of the rule, the version history of that rule, the", "tokens": [50466, 440, 24438, 1633, 5304, 264, 11121, 2487, 295, 264, 4978, 11, 264, 3037, 2503, 295, 300, 4978, 11, 264, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13844722356551734, "compression_ratio": 1.5485436893203883, "no_speech_prob": 2.64544072411943e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 125740, "start": 1264.48, "end": 1270.52, "text": " asserted authority enforcing it, the specific jurisdiction it applies to, the temporal interval", "tokens": [50719, 19810, 292, 8281, 25495, 2175, 309, 11, 264, 2685, 27285, 309, 13165, 281, 11, 264, 30881, 15035, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13844722356551734, "compression_ratio": 1.5485436893203883, "no_speech_prob": 2.64544072411943e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 125740, "start": 1270.52, "end": 1275.88, "text": " during which it is effective, and most crucially, a defined procedure for contestation.", "tokens": [51021, 1830, 597, 309, 307, 4942, 11, 293, 881, 5140, 1909, 11, 257, 7642, 10747, 337, 10287, 399, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13844722356551734, "compression_ratio": 1.5485436893203883, "no_speech_prob": 2.64544072411943e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 127588, "start": 1275.88, "end": 1278.46, "text": " It has to encode the right to fight back.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 575, 281, 2058, 1429, 264, 558, 281, 2092, 646, 13, 50494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14240210646883064, "compression_ratio": 1.6879699248120301, "no_speech_prob": 2.163595257814732e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 127588, "start": 1278.7, "end": 1283.44, "text": " It has to acknowledge that the rule is situated in a political reality, not just a mathematical", "tokens": [50506, 467, 575, 281, 10692, 300, 264, 4978, 307, 30143, 294, 257, 3905, 4103, 11, 406, 445, 257, 18894, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14240210646883064, "compression_ratio": 1.6879699248120301, "no_speech_prob": 2.163595257814732e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 127588, "start": 1283.44, "end": 1283.94, "text": " vacuum.", "tokens": [50743, 14224, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14240210646883064, "compression_ratio": 1.6879699248120301, "no_speech_prob": 2.163595257814732e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 127588, "start": 1284.1000000000001, "end": 1284.3600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50776, 1079, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14240210646883064, "compression_ratio": 1.6879699248120301, "no_speech_prob": 2.163595257814732e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 127588, "start": 1285.0400000000002, "end": 1289.98, "text": " Real, robust architectures must define all these parameters because legitimacy is fundamentally", "tokens": [50823, 8467, 11, 13956, 6331, 1303, 1633, 6964, 439, 613, 9834, 570, 41339, 307, 17879, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14240210646883064, "compression_ratio": 1.6879699248120301, "no_speech_prob": 2.163595257814732e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 127588, "start": 1289.98, "end": 1290.88, "text": " a relational property.", "tokens": [51070, 257, 38444, 4707, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14240210646883064, "compression_ratio": 1.6879699248120301, "no_speech_prob": 2.163595257814732e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 127588, "start": 1291.5600000000002, "end": 1292.5400000000002, "text": " A relational property.", "tokens": [51149, 316, 38444, 4707, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14240210646883064, "compression_ratio": 1.6879699248120301, "no_speech_prob": 2.163595257814732e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 127588, "start": 1292.66, "end": 1293.1000000000001, "text": " I like that.", "tokens": [51204, 286, 411, 300, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14240210646883064, "compression_ratio": 1.6879699248120301, "no_speech_prob": 2.163595257814732e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 127588, "start": 1293.2800000000002, "end": 1297.7800000000002, "text": " It is the relationship between a rule, the authority asserting that rule, the subjects affected", "tokens": [51235, 467, 307, 264, 2480, 1296, 257, 4978, 11, 264, 8281, 1256, 27187, 300, 4978, 11, 264, 13066, 8028, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14240210646883064, "compression_ratio": 1.6879699248120301, "no_speech_prob": 2.163595257814732e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 127588, "start": 1297.7800000000002, "end": 1300.3000000000002, "text": " by it, and the procedures available for review.", "tokens": [51460, 538, 309, 11, 293, 264, 13846, 2435, 337, 3131, 13, 51586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14240210646883064, "compression_ratio": 1.6879699248120301, "no_speech_prob": 2.163595257814732e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 130030, "start": 1300.3, "end": 1305.78, "text": " So a computational system can mathematically verify that the parameters of a policy bundle", "tokens": [50365, 407, 257, 28270, 1185, 393, 44003, 16888, 300, 264, 9834, 295, 257, 3897, 24438, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10952849917941623, "compression_ratio": 1.6793893129770991, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506429891485988e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 130030, "start": 1305.78, "end": 1311.1399999999999, "text": " were applied correctly to a specific input, but computation alone can never answer the", "tokens": [50639, 645, 6456, 8944, 281, 257, 2685, 4846, 11, 457, 24903, 3312, 393, 1128, 1867, 264, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10952849917941623, "compression_ratio": 1.6793893129770991, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506429891485988e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 130030, "start": 1311.1399999999999, "end": 1315.94, "text": " prior, deeply political question of whether the authority itself is legitimate.", "tokens": [50907, 4059, 11, 8760, 3905, 1168, 295, 1968, 264, 8281, 2564, 307, 17956, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10952849917941623, "compression_ratio": 1.6793893129770991, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506429891485988e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 130030, "start": 1316.08, "end": 1316.46, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51154, 7587, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10952849917941623, "compression_ratio": 1.6793893129770991, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506429891485988e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 130030, "start": 1316.84, "end": 1323.1, "text": " And the PERL program, reality permit, deliberately omits the policy bundle to mathematically prove", "tokens": [51192, 400, 264, 26825, 43, 1461, 11, 4103, 13423, 11, 23506, 3406, 1208, 264, 3897, 24438, 281, 44003, 7081, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10952849917941623, "compression_ratio": 1.6793893129770991, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506429891485988e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 130030, "start": 1323.1, "end": 1326.8799999999999, "text": " that without that relational context, all you have is repeatable nonsense.", "tokens": [51505, 300, 1553, 300, 38444, 4319, 11, 439, 291, 362, 307, 7149, 712, 14925, 13, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10952849917941623, "compression_ratio": 1.6793893129770991, "no_speech_prob": 1.9506429891485988e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 132688, "start": 1326.88, "end": 1331.3200000000002, "text": " This completely reframes how we should look at algorithmic decision-making.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 2584, 13334, 1632, 577, 321, 820, 574, 412, 9284, 299, 3537, 12, 12402, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10028546590071458, "compression_ratio": 1.6054421768707483, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906321820610916e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 132688, "start": 1331.8400000000001, "end": 1336.68, "text": " When we look at automated credit scoring models, resume filtering algorithms, or content", "tokens": [50613, 1133, 321, 574, 412, 18473, 5397, 22358, 5245, 11, 15358, 30822, 14642, 11, 420, 2701, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10028546590071458, "compression_ratio": 1.6054421768707483, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906321820610916e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 132688, "start": 1336.68, "end": 1341.2600000000002, "text": " moderation systems, they are all just hyperscaled ministries of possible affairs.", "tokens": [50855, 49471, 3652, 11, 436, 366, 439, 445, 7420, 433, 66, 5573, 16182, 2244, 295, 1944, 17478, 13, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10028546590071458, "compression_ratio": 1.6054421768707483, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906321820610916e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 132688, "start": 1341.38, "end": 1342.0200000000002, "text": " They really are?", "tokens": [51090, 814, 534, 366, 30, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10028546590071458, "compression_ratio": 1.6054421768707483, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906321820610916e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 132688, "start": 1342.2, "end": 1347.5, "text": " They are generating highly consequential rulings based on arbitrary internal metrics, some hidden", "tokens": [51131, 814, 366, 17746, 5405, 7242, 2549, 8551, 1109, 2361, 322, 23211, 6920, 16367, 11, 512, 7633, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10028546590071458, "compression_ratio": 1.6054421768707483, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906321820610916e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 132688, "start": 1347.5, "end": 1352.7800000000002, "text": " seed 1982, often without exposing the policy bundle or the mechanisms for contestation.", "tokens": [51396, 8871, 31352, 11, 2049, 1553, 33178, 264, 3897, 24438, 420, 264, 15902, 337, 10287, 399, 13, 51660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10028546590071458, "compression_ratio": 1.6054421768707483, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906321820610916e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 132688, "start": 1352.98, "end": 1354.1000000000001, "text": " And that's terrifying.", "tokens": [51670, 400, 300, 311, 18106, 13, 51726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10028546590071458, "compression_ratio": 1.6054421768707483, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906321820610916e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 135410, "start": 1354.1, "end": 1358.4199999999998, "text": " Okay, so a proposal has crossed the ingress boundary, established its operational validity", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 257, 11494, 575, 14622, 264, 3957, 735, 12866, 11, 7545, 1080, 16607, 40943, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746524117209695, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.3901711772994494e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 135410, "start": 1358.4199999999998, "end": 1361.6799999999998, "text": " in GO, and received a judgment, however arbitrary in PERL.", "tokens": [50581, 294, 10365, 11, 293, 4613, 257, 12216, 11, 4461, 23211, 294, 26825, 43, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746524117209695, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.3901711772994494e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 135410, "start": 1362.2199999999998, "end": 1364.1999999999998, "text": " But what happens after the judgment is rendered?", "tokens": [50771, 583, 437, 2314, 934, 264, 12216, 307, 28748, 30, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746524117209695, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.3901711772994494e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 135410, "start": 1364.52, "end": 1368.06, "text": " Where does the record of that decision go, especially if the proposal is denied?", "tokens": [50886, 2305, 775, 264, 2136, 295, 300, 3537, 352, 11, 2318, 498, 264, 11494, 307, 17774, 30, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746524117209695, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.3901711772994494e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 135410, "start": 1368.4199999999998, "end": 1374.1599999999999, "text": " This is where we reach the final, and in many ways the most profound, layer of Flakassian's", "tokens": [51081, 639, 307, 689, 321, 2524, 264, 2572, 11, 293, 294, 867, 2098, 264, 881, 14382, 11, 4583, 295, 3235, 514, 640, 952, 311, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746524117209695, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.3901711772994494e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 135410, "start": 1374.1599999999999, "end": 1376.54, "text": " architecture, historical continuation.", "tokens": [51368, 9482, 11, 8584, 29357, 13, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746524117209695, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.3901711772994494e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 135410, "start": 1376.8799999999999, "end": 1378.06, "text": " Denoted by the letter A.", "tokens": [51504, 6458, 23325, 538, 264, 5063, 316, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746524117209695, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.3901711772994494e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 135410, "start": 1378.1799999999998, "end": 1378.4199999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51569, 1779, 13, 51581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15746524117209695, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.3901711772994494e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 137842, "start": 1378.42, "end": 1383.88, "text": " And to model this, the paper shifts languages one final time, introducing the third program,", "tokens": [50365, 400, 281, 2316, 341, 11, 264, 3035, 19201, 8650, 472, 2572, 565, 11, 15424, 264, 2636, 1461, 11, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15765143663455278, "compression_ratio": 1.4953271028037383, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549085235864625e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 137842, "start": 1384.3400000000001, "end": 1386.52, "text": " Counterfactual Git, written in Rust.", "tokens": [50661, 35607, 44919, 901, 16939, 11, 3720, 294, 34952, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15765143663455278, "compression_ratio": 1.4953271028037383, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549085235864625e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 137842, "start": 1386.74, "end": 1389.22, "text": " The choice of Rust here is incredibly deliberate.", "tokens": [50781, 440, 3922, 295, 34952, 510, 307, 6252, 30515, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15765143663455278, "compression_ratio": 1.4953271028037383, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549085235864625e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 137842, "start": 1389.96, "end": 1394.46, "text": " Rust is famous or infamous, depending on who you ask for, its obsessively strict memory safety,", "tokens": [50942, 34952, 307, 4618, 420, 30769, 11, 5413, 322, 567, 291, 1029, 337, 11, 1080, 35803, 3413, 10910, 4675, 4514, 11, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15765143663455278, "compression_ratio": 1.4953271028037383, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549085235864625e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 137842, "start": 1394.98, "end": 1397.14, "text": " its ownership model, and its borrow checker.", "tokens": [51193, 1080, 15279, 2316, 11, 293, 1080, 11172, 1520, 260, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15765143663455278, "compression_ratio": 1.4953271028037383, "no_speech_prob": 1.6549085235864625e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 139714, "start": 1397.14, "end": 1404.3000000000002, "text": " It forces the developer to be explicitly, rigidly aware of what data is mutating, who owns that", "tokens": [50365, 467, 5874, 264, 10754, 281, 312, 20803, 11, 22195, 356, 3650, 295, 437, 1412, 307, 5839, 990, 11, 567, 19143, 300, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238659900167714, "compression_ratio": 1.6291390728476822, "no_speech_prob": 2.465457742475974e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 139714, "start": 1404.3000000000002, "end": 1406.44, "text": " data, and how state transitions occur.", "tokens": [50723, 1412, 11, 293, 577, 1785, 23767, 5160, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238659900167714, "compression_ratio": 1.6291390728476822, "no_speech_prob": 2.465457742475974e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 139714, "start": 1406.5400000000002, "end": 1410.4, "text": " Which maps perfectly onto the architectural requirements for managing an immutable historical", "tokens": [50835, 3013, 11317, 6239, 3911, 264, 26621, 7728, 337, 11642, 364, 3397, 32148, 8584, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238659900167714, "compression_ratio": 1.6291390728476822, "no_speech_prob": 2.465457742475974e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 139714, "start": 1410.4, "end": 1410.9, "text": " timeline.", "tokens": [51028, 12933, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238659900167714, "compression_ratio": 1.6291390728476822, "no_speech_prob": 2.465457742475974e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 139714, "start": 1411.5600000000002, "end": 1416.94, "text": " You need a language that treats state transition as a deeply protected, tightly regulated event.", "tokens": [51086, 509, 643, 257, 2856, 300, 19566, 1785, 6034, 382, 257, 8760, 10594, 11, 21952, 26243, 2280, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238659900167714, "compression_ratio": 1.6291390728476822, "no_speech_prob": 2.465457742475974e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 139714, "start": 1417.0200000000002, "end": 1417.3400000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51359, 7587, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238659900167714, "compression_ratio": 1.6291390728476822, "no_speech_prob": 2.465457742475974e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 139714, "start": 1417.6200000000001, "end": 1420.88, "text": " So in Counterfactual Git, the system processes proposed events.", "tokens": [51389, 407, 294, 35607, 44919, 901, 16939, 11, 264, 1185, 7555, 10348, 3931, 13, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238659900167714, "compression_ratio": 1.6291390728476822, "no_speech_prob": 2.465457742475974e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 139714, "start": 1421.0600000000002, "end": 1425.7800000000002, "text": " Each event contains a year, a subject, a verb, an object, and a cryptographic hash.", "tokens": [51561, 6947, 2280, 8306, 257, 1064, 11, 257, 3983, 11, 257, 9595, 11, 364, 2657, 11, 293, 257, 9844, 12295, 22019, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10238659900167714, "compression_ratio": 1.6291390728476822, "no_speech_prob": 2.465457742475974e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 142578, "start": 1425.78, "end": 1430.18, "text": " When a user submits an event, the system attempts to create a commit to the timeline.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 257, 4195, 8286, 1208, 364, 2280, 11, 264, 1185, 15257, 281, 1884, 257, 5599, 281, 264, 12933, 13, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14280160268147787, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351809651263485e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 142578, "start": 1430.58, "end": 1435.08, "text": " But the program enforces strict boundaries on what is allowed to enter the operative reality.", "tokens": [50605, 583, 264, 1461, 25495, 887, 10910, 13180, 322, 437, 307, 4350, 281, 3242, 264, 2208, 1166, 4103, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14280160268147787, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351809651263485e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 142578, "start": 1435.44, "end": 1440.6, "text": " And the rules for what Flakassian calls causal inadmissibility are fantastic.", "tokens": [50848, 400, 264, 4474, 337, 437, 3235, 514, 640, 952, 5498, 38755, 42148, 76, 891, 2841, 366, 5456, 13, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14280160268147787, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351809651263485e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 142578, "start": 1441.12, "end": 1444.5, "text": " They read like the laws of physics for a bureaucratic time travel agency.", "tokens": [51132, 814, 1401, 411, 264, 6064, 295, 10649, 337, 257, 26360, 25198, 565, 3147, 7934, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14280160268147787, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351809651263485e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 142578, "start": 1444.58, "end": 1444.92, "text": " They do.", "tokens": [51305, 814, 360, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14280160268147787, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351809651263485e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 142578, "start": 1445.3, "end": 1446.76, "text": " Let's look at the mechanics of these rules.", "tokens": [51341, 961, 311, 574, 412, 264, 12939, 295, 613, 4474, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14280160268147787, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351809651263485e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 142578, "start": 1447.1399999999999, "end": 1449.92, "text": " Rule one, a year cannot be occupied twice.", "tokens": [51433, 27533, 472, 11, 257, 1064, 2644, 312, 19629, 6091, 13, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14280160268147787, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351809651263485e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 142578, "start": 1450.46, "end": 1453.86, "text": " So if the timeline already has an accepted event for the year 2026,", "tokens": [51599, 407, 498, 264, 12933, 1217, 575, 364, 9035, 2280, 337, 264, 1064, 945, 10880, 11, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14280160268147787, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351809651263485e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 145386, "start": 1453.86, "end": 1458.1, "text": " you cannot submit a new contradictory event for 2026.", "tokens": [50365, 291, 2644, 10315, 257, 777, 49555, 2280, 337, 945, 10880, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16086233655611673, "compression_ratio": 1.6312056737588652, "no_speech_prob": 1.81084823785288e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 145386, "start": 1458.6599999999999, "end": 1459.9599999999998, "text": " The temporal space is claimed.", "tokens": [50605, 440, 30881, 1901, 307, 12941, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16086233655611673, "compression_ratio": 1.6312056737588652, "no_speech_prob": 1.81084823785288e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 145386, "start": 1460.28, "end": 1460.6999999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50686, 7587, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16086233655611673, "compression_ratio": 1.6312056737588652, "no_speech_prob": 1.81084823785288e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 145386, "start": 1461.12, "end": 1465.1799999999998, "text": " Rule two, history cannot quietly replace the committee reviewing the history.", "tokens": [50728, 27533, 732, 11, 2503, 2644, 19141, 7406, 264, 7482, 19576, 264, 2503, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16086233655611673, "compression_ratio": 1.6312056737588652, "no_speech_prob": 1.81084823785288e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 145386, "start": 1465.78, "end": 1471.28, "text": " That specific rule is a brilliant safeguard against temporal paradoxes and institutional erasure.", "tokens": [50961, 663, 2685, 4978, 307, 257, 10248, 40153, 1970, 30881, 26221, 279, 293, 18391, 1189, 2508, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16086233655611673, "compression_ratio": 1.6312056737588652, "no_speech_prob": 1.81084823785288e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 145386, "start": 1471.9599999999998, "end": 1476.32, "text": " The system mathematically forbids the admission of any event that would retroactively dissolve", "tokens": [51270, 440, 1185, 44003, 16603, 3742, 264, 24668, 295, 604, 2280, 300, 576, 18820, 45679, 30150, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16086233655611673, "compression_ratio": 1.6312056737588652, "no_speech_prob": 1.81084823785288e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 145386, "start": 1476.32, "end": 1479.62, "text": " or replace the very authority currently evaluating the timeline.", "tokens": [51488, 420, 7406, 264, 588, 8281, 4362, 27479, 264, 12933, 13, 51653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16086233655611673, "compression_ratio": 1.6312056737588652, "no_speech_prob": 1.81084823785288e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 145386, "start": 1479.6799999999998, "end": 1481.28, "text": " It requires causal continuity.", "tokens": [51656, 467, 7029, 38755, 23807, 13, 51736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16086233655611673, "compression_ratio": 1.6312056737588652, "no_speech_prob": 1.81084823785288e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 148128, "start": 1481.28, "end": 1486.46, "text": " And rule three, which is genuinely poetic, an apocalypse requires an accepted alibi.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 4978, 1045, 11, 597, 307, 17839, 41080, 11, 364, 42600, 7029, 364, 9035, 419, 25515, 13, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1507469850427964, "compression_ratio": 1.6531531531531531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736428203548373e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 148128, "start": 1486.62, "end": 1487.32, "text": " I love that one.", "tokens": [50632, 286, 959, 300, 472, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1507469850427964, "compression_ratio": 1.6531531531531531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736428203548373e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 148128, "start": 1487.42, "end": 1490.7, "text": " If a proposed event constitutes an apocalyptic state transition,", "tokens": [50672, 759, 257, 10348, 2280, 44204, 364, 1882, 47407, 1785, 6034, 11, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1507469850427964, "compression_ratio": 1.6531531531531531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736428203548373e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 148128, "start": 1491.3, "end": 1494.94, "text": " the system must scan the preceding history to verify that an earlier,", "tokens": [50866, 264, 1185, 1633, 11049, 264, 16969, 278, 2503, 281, 16888, 300, 364, 3071, 11, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1507469850427964, "compression_ratio": 1.6531531531531531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736428203548373e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 148128, "start": 1495.36, "end": 1498.44, "text": " legally distinct event established a valid alibi for the participants.", "tokens": [51069, 21106, 10644, 2280, 7545, 257, 7363, 419, 25515, 337, 264, 10503, 13, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1507469850427964, "compression_ratio": 1.6531531531531531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736428203548373e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 148128, "start": 1499.2, "end": 1502.36, "text": " If no causal prerequisite exists, the apocalypse is denied.", "tokens": [51261, 759, 572, 38755, 38333, 34152, 8198, 11, 264, 42600, 307, 17774, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1507469850427964, "compression_ratio": 1.6531531531531531, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736428203548373e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 150236, "start": 1502.36, "end": 1507.58, "text": " And while the rules are framed comedically, they demonstrate the strict mechanics of path dependence.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1339, 264, 4474, 366, 30420, 18418, 984, 11, 436, 11698, 264, 10910, 12939, 295, 3100, 31704, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15751532012341068, "compression_ratio": 1.6267123287671232, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970376705797597e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 150236, "start": 1508.3999999999999, "end": 1513.52, "text": " The admissibility of any proposed event is entirely contingent upon the specific sequence of events", "tokens": [50667, 440, 5910, 891, 2841, 295, 604, 10348, 2280, 307, 7696, 27820, 317, 3564, 264, 2685, 8310, 295, 3931, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15751532012341068, "compression_ratio": 1.6267123287671232, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970376705797597e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 150236, "start": 1513.52, "end": 1515.36, "text": " that have already been accepted into the history.", "tokens": [50923, 300, 362, 1217, 668, 9035, 666, 264, 2503, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15751532012341068, "compression_ratio": 1.6267123287671232, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970376705797597e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 150236, "start": 1515.6799999999998, "end": 1515.7199999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51031, 1779, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15751532012341068, "compression_ratio": 1.6267123287671232, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970376705797597e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 150236, "start": 1515.8999999999999, "end": 1520.78, "text": " But the true conceptual breakthrough in this section of the paper isn't just the rules themselves.", "tokens": [51042, 583, 264, 2074, 24106, 22397, 294, 341, 3541, 295, 264, 3035, 1943, 380, 445, 264, 4474, 2969, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15751532012341068, "compression_ratio": 1.6267123287671232, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970376705797597e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 150236, "start": 1521.04, "end": 1526.6, "text": " It is how Flitchian mathematically formalizes the divergence between the documentary history", "tokens": [51299, 467, 307, 577, 3235, 1549, 952, 44003, 9860, 5660, 264, 47387, 1296, 264, 15674, 2503, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15751532012341068, "compression_ratio": 1.6267123287671232, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970376705797597e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 150236, "start": 1526.6, "end": 1528.26, "text": " and the operative state.", "tokens": [51577, 293, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 13, 51660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15751532012341068, "compression_ratio": 1.6267123287671232, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970376705797597e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 152826, "start": 1528.26, "end": 1531.84, "text": " Yes, this is the core mechanic we need to dissect.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 341, 307, 264, 4965, 23860, 321, 643, 281, 48332, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1775951385498047, "compression_ratio": 1.6135458167330676, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450226557617196e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 152826, "start": 1532.26, "end": 1534.44, "text": " The paper defines two distinct tracks.", "tokens": [50565, 440, 3035, 23122, 732, 10644, 10218, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1775951385498047, "compression_ratio": 1.6135458167330676, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450226557617196e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 152826, "start": 1534.8799999999999, "end": 1538.96, "text": " We have H, which represents the monotonically increasing documentary history,", "tokens": [50696, 492, 362, 389, 11, 597, 8855, 264, 1108, 27794, 984, 5662, 15674, 2503, 11, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1775951385498047, "compression_ratio": 1.6135458167330676, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450226557617196e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 152826, "start": 1539.12, "end": 1543.24, "text": " and we have sigma, which represents the current operative state of reality.", "tokens": [50908, 293, 321, 362, 12771, 11, 597, 8855, 264, 2190, 2208, 1166, 1785, 295, 4103, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1775951385498047, "compression_ratio": 1.6135458167330676, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450226557617196e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 152826, "start": 1543.44, "end": 1544.98, "text": " Let's walk through the state transition logic.", "tokens": [51124, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 264, 1785, 6034, 9952, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1775951385498047, "compression_ratio": 1.6135458167330676, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450226557617196e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 152826, "start": 1545.28, "end": 1548.18, "text": " When a proposal is recognized by the ingress operator and evaluated,", "tokens": [51216, 1133, 257, 11494, 307, 9823, 538, 264, 3957, 735, 12973, 293, 25509, 11, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1775951385498047, "compression_ratio": 1.6135458167330676, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450226557617196e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 152826, "start": 1548.54, "end": 1550.52, "text": " it receives a recorded disposition.", "tokens": [51379, 309, 20717, 257, 8287, 40293, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1775951385498047, "compression_ratio": 1.6135458167330676, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450226557617196e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 152826, "start": 1550.78, "end": 1551.2, "text": " A ruling.", "tokens": [51491, 316, 21437, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1775951385498047, "compression_ratio": 1.6135458167330676, "no_speech_prob": 2.6450226557617196e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 155120, "start": 1551.2, "end": 1558.0, "text": " At this moment, the documentary history sequence H sub N plus 1 is defined as the previous history,", "tokens": [50365, 1711, 341, 1623, 11, 264, 15674, 2503, 8310, 389, 1422, 426, 1804, 502, 307, 7642, 382, 264, 3894, 2503, 11, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13377512494723, "compression_ratio": 1.701195219123506, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 155120, "start": 1558.22, "end": 1562.06, "text": " H sub N, appended with the new commit and its disposition.", "tokens": [50716, 389, 1422, 426, 11, 724, 3502, 365, 264, 777, 5599, 293, 1080, 40293, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13377512494723, "compression_ratio": 1.701195219123506, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 155120, "start": 1562.22, "end": 1563.24, "text": " Okay, so it gets added.", "tokens": [50916, 1033, 11, 370, 309, 2170, 3869, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13377512494723, "compression_ratio": 1.701195219123506, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 155120, "start": 1563.4, "end": 1566.24, "text": " And this append operation happens unconditionally.", "tokens": [50975, 400, 341, 34116, 6916, 2314, 34959, 15899, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13377512494723, "compression_ratio": 1.701195219123506, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 155120, "start": 1567.22, "end": 1572.48, "text": " Every recognized proposal, whether approved or denied, permanently grows the documentary history.", "tokens": [51166, 2048, 9823, 11494, 11, 1968, 10826, 420, 17774, 11, 24042, 13156, 264, 15674, 2503, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13377512494723, "compression_ratio": 1.701195219123506, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 155120, "start": 1572.64, "end": 1577.54, "text": " But the operative state sigma sub N plus 1 operates on an entirely different conditional logic.", "tokens": [51437, 583, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 12771, 1422, 426, 1804, 502, 22577, 322, 364, 7696, 819, 27708, 9952, 13, 51682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13377512494723, "compression_ratio": 1.701195219123506, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796968767800568e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 157754, "start": 1577.54, "end": 1578.1599999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16933719390029206, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013985706415546e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 157754, "start": 1578.58, "end": 1582.5, "text": " The operative state only advances if the admissibility predicate returns true.", "tokens": [50417, 440, 2208, 1166, 1785, 787, 25297, 498, 264, 5910, 891, 2841, 3852, 8700, 11247, 2074, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16933719390029206, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013985706415546e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 157754, "start": 1583.46, "end": 1589.24, "text": " If the event violates the rules, say, trying to occupy a year twice, the proposal is rejected.", "tokens": [50661, 759, 264, 2280, 3448, 1024, 264, 4474, 11, 584, 11, 1382, 281, 30645, 257, 1064, 6091, 11, 264, 11494, 307, 15749, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16933719390029206, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013985706415546e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 157754, "start": 1589.8, "end": 1592.6, "text": " The operative state remains entirely unchanged.", "tokens": [50978, 440, 2208, 1166, 1785, 7023, 7696, 44553, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16933719390029206, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013985706415546e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 157754, "start": 1593.46, "end": 1596.78, "text": " Sigma sub N plus 1 simply equals sigma sub N.", "tokens": [51161, 36595, 1422, 426, 1804, 502, 2935, 6915, 12771, 1422, 426, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16933719390029206, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013985706415546e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 157754, "start": 1597.2, "end": 1602.78, "text": " So when an event is rejected, the actual functioning reality of the system, the operative state, doesn't budge.", "tokens": [51348, 407, 562, 364, 2280, 307, 15749, 11, 264, 3539, 18483, 4103, 295, 264, 1185, 11, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 11, 1177, 380, 3265, 432, 13, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16933719390029206, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013985706415546e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 157754, "start": 1603.42, "end": 1606.1, "text": " But the failure itself is still perfectly preserved.", "tokens": [51659, 583, 264, 7763, 2564, 307, 920, 6239, 22242, 13, 51793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16933719390029206, "compression_ratio": 1.6896551724137931, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013985706415546e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 160610, "start": 1606.1, "end": 1609.1999999999998, "text": " It is appended to the documentary history track.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 724, 3502, 281, 264, 15674, 2503, 2837, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485470414161682, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.446644015857702e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 160610, "start": 1609.52, "end": 1613.34, "text": " Let me ground this in a real world infrastructure we all use, the financial system.", "tokens": [50536, 961, 385, 2727, 341, 294, 257, 957, 1002, 6896, 321, 439, 764, 11, 264, 4669, 1185, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485470414161682, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.446644015857702e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 160610, "start": 1613.4199999999998, "end": 1613.84, "text": " That's a good example.", "tokens": [50731, 663, 311, 257, 665, 1365, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485470414161682, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.446644015857702e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 160610, "start": 1613.9599999999998, "end": 1617.8799999999999, "text": " If I apply for a mortgage or a new credit card, that application is a formal proposal.", "tokens": [50758, 759, 286, 3079, 337, 257, 20236, 420, 257, 777, 5397, 2920, 11, 300, 3861, 307, 257, 9860, 11494, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485470414161682, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.446644015857702e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 160610, "start": 1618.2199999999998, "end": 1624.9399999999998, "text": " If the bank's algorithm evaluates my request and denies it, my actual bank account balance, my operative state doesn't change.", "tokens": [50971, 759, 264, 3765, 311, 9284, 6133, 1024, 452, 5308, 293, 1441, 530, 309, 11, 452, 3539, 3765, 2696, 4772, 11, 452, 2208, 1166, 1785, 1177, 380, 1319, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485470414161682, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.446644015857702e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 160610, "start": 1625.1399999999999, "end": 1627.3799999999999, "text": " Right, you don't magically lose money just for applying.", "tokens": [51317, 1779, 11, 291, 500, 380, 39763, 3624, 1460, 445, 337, 9275, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485470414161682, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.446644015857702e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 160610, "start": 1627.76, "end": 1628.1399999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51448, 7587, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485470414161682, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.446644015857702e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 160610, "start": 1628.3999999999999, "end": 1630.6399999999999, "text": " I don't get the house, I don't get the line of credit.", "tokens": [51480, 286, 500, 380, 483, 264, 1782, 11, 286, 500, 380, 483, 264, 1622, 295, 5397, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13485470414161682, "compression_ratio": 1.627906976744186, "no_speech_prob": 2.446644015857702e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 163064, "start": 1630.64, "end": 1640.76, "text": " The operative reality remains static, but the record of that denial, the hard inquiry on my credit report, is permanently etched into my documentary history.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2208, 1166, 4103, 7023, 13437, 11, 457, 264, 2136, 295, 300, 28754, 11, 264, 1152, 25736, 322, 452, 5397, 2275, 11, 307, 24042, 1030, 19318, 666, 452, 15674, 2503, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513189998673803, "compression_ratio": 1.6211453744493391, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724366474358486e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 163064, "start": 1640.8400000000001, "end": 1641.96, "text": " Oh, that's exactly it.", "tokens": [50875, 876, 11, 300, 311, 2293, 309, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513189998673803, "compression_ratio": 1.6211453744493391, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724366474358486e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 163064, "start": 1642.2, "end": 1651.4, "text": " The refusal is recorded in tract, and that recorded refusal will actually influence future evaluations, even though the original transaction never executed.", "tokens": [50943, 440, 48948, 307, 8287, 294, 24207, 11, 293, 300, 8287, 48948, 486, 767, 6503, 2027, 43085, 11, 754, 1673, 264, 3380, 14425, 1128, 17577, 13, 51403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513189998673803, "compression_ratio": 1.6211453744493391, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724366474358486e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 163064, "start": 1652.0200000000002, "end": 1653.7800000000002, "text": " Refusal does not mean erasure.", "tokens": [51434, 16957, 11765, 775, 406, 914, 1189, 2508, 13, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14513189998673803, "compression_ratio": 1.6211453744493391, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724366474358486e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 165378, "start": 1653.78, "end": 1656.44, "text": " That is an excellent grounding of the concept.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 364, 7103, 46727, 295, 264, 3410, 13, 50498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318614257009406, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610252228157265e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 165378, "start": 1656.8799999999999, "end": 1663.06, "text": " The hard inquiry is a perfect example of a recorded disposition in H-A-B-N that failed to alter sigma.", "tokens": [50520, 440, 1152, 25736, 307, 257, 2176, 1365, 295, 257, 8287, 40293, 294, 389, 12, 32, 12, 33, 12, 45, 300, 7612, 281, 11337, 12771, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318614257009406, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610252228157265e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 165378, "start": 1663.66, "end": 1669.78, "text": " And Fliction argues that understanding this separation is revolutionary for how we design and audit systems.", "tokens": [50859, 400, 3235, 4105, 38218, 300, 3701, 341, 14634, 307, 22687, 337, 577, 321, 1715, 293, 17748, 3652, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318614257009406, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610252228157265e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 165378, "start": 1670.06, "end": 1678.1399999999999, "text": " Because we are conditioned to think of history as a unified ledger of everything that is true, we view it as a simple list of the things that successfully happened.", "tokens": [51179, 1436, 321, 366, 35833, 281, 519, 295, 2503, 382, 257, 26787, 4684, 1321, 295, 1203, 300, 307, 2074, 11, 321, 1910, 309, 382, 257, 2199, 1329, 295, 264, 721, 300, 10727, 2011, 13, 51583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318614257009406, "compression_ratio": 1.6145038167938932, "no_speech_prob": 1.8610252228157265e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 167814, "start": 1678.14, "end": 1683.24, "text": " But Fliction mathematically demonstrates that operative history is actually a highly selective projection.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3235, 4105, 44003, 31034, 300, 2208, 1166, 2503, 307, 767, 257, 5405, 33930, 22743, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144798065852193, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 2.271251763052984e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 167814, "start": 1683.74, "end": 1689.3600000000001, "text": " It is a narrowly chosen path carved through a vastly larger, more comprehensive field of recorded proposals.", "tokens": [50645, 467, 307, 257, 9432, 356, 8614, 3100, 28613, 807, 257, 41426, 4833, 11, 544, 13914, 2519, 295, 8287, 20198, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144798065852193, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 2.271251763052984e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 167814, "start": 1689.5600000000002, "end": 1691.5200000000002, "text": " The documentary record is the full universe.", "tokens": [50936, 440, 15674, 2136, 307, 264, 1577, 6445, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144798065852193, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 2.271251763052984e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 167814, "start": 1691.94, "end": 1697.0400000000002, "text": " It contains all the triumphant yeses, but it also contains every single structurally sound no.", "tokens": [51055, 467, 8306, 439, 264, 1376, 449, 15071, 2086, 279, 11, 457, 309, 611, 8306, 633, 2167, 6594, 6512, 1626, 572, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144798065852193, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 2.271251763052984e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 167814, "start": 1697.3600000000001, "end": 1697.76, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51326, 1079, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144798065852193, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 2.271251763052984e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 167814, "start": 1698.18, "end": 1700.8400000000001, "text": " And the Rust program maintains this dichotomy perfectly.", "tokens": [51367, 400, 264, 34952, 1461, 33385, 341, 10390, 310, 8488, 6239, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144798065852193, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 2.271251763052984e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 167814, "start": 1701.48, "end": 1704.8400000000001, "text": " It maintains a strictly linear, accepted timeline.", "tokens": [51532, 467, 33385, 257, 20792, 8213, 11, 9035, 12933, 13, 51700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.144798065852193, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 2.271251763052984e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 170484, "start": 1704.84, "end": 1715.4399999999998, "text": " The operative reality the system inhabits running parallel to a monotonically increasing audit spine containing every single proposal ever submitted.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2208, 1166, 4103, 264, 1185, 16934, 1208, 2614, 8952, 281, 257, 1108, 27794, 984, 5662, 17748, 15395, 19273, 633, 2167, 11494, 1562, 14405, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11088144402754935, "compression_ratio": 1.6801470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414801154955195e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 170484, "start": 1715.4399999999998, "end": 1720.3, "text": " So a rejected proposal isn't just transient garbage data or a fleeting error message.", "tokens": [50895, 407, 257, 15749, 11494, 1943, 380, 445, 41998, 14150, 1412, 420, 257, 7025, 9880, 6713, 3636, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11088144402754935, "compression_ratio": 1.6801470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414801154955195e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 170484, "start": 1720.78, "end": 1722.1999999999998, "text": " It is retained evidence.", "tokens": [51162, 467, 307, 33438, 4467, 13, 51233], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11088144402754935, "compression_ratio": 1.6801470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414801154955195e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 170484, "start": 1722.6399999999999, "end": 1730.08, "text": " It acts as a permanent cryptographic marker showing exactly where the boundaries of acceptable reality were drawn at that specific moment in time.", "tokens": [51255, 467, 10672, 382, 257, 10996, 9844, 12295, 15247, 4099, 2293, 689, 264, 13180, 295, 15513, 4103, 645, 10117, 412, 300, 2685, 1623, 294, 565, 13, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11088144402754935, "compression_ratio": 1.6801470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414801154955195e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 170484, "start": 1730.22, "end": 1732.78, "text": " It maps the negative space of the system's logic.", "tokens": [51634, 467, 11317, 264, 3671, 1901, 295, 264, 1185, 311, 9952, 13, 51762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11088144402754935, "compression_ratio": 1.6801470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.7414801154955195e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 173278, "start": 1732.78, "end": 1737.7, "text": " But exploring this theoretically immediately brings up a massive physical limitation.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 12736, 341, 29400, 4258, 5607, 493, 257, 5994, 4001, 27432, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867840730691258, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204452260558226e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 173278, "start": 1738.0, "end": 1738.8, "text": " The storage problem.", "tokens": [50626, 440, 6725, 1154, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867840730691258, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204452260558226e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 173278, "start": 1738.94, "end": 1739.1399999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50673, 1779, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867840730691258, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204452260558226e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 173278, "start": 1739.62, "end": 1753.62, "text": " If a system's architecture mandates that we unconditionally record every single recognized proposal, including all the billions of rejections, denied access attempts, and failed validations, wouldn't our storage infrastructure eventually collapse under its own weight?", "tokens": [50707, 759, 257, 1185, 311, 9482, 48662, 300, 321, 34959, 15899, 2136, 633, 2167, 9823, 11494, 11, 3009, 439, 264, 17375, 295, 8248, 626, 11, 17774, 2105, 15257, 11, 293, 7612, 7363, 763, 11, 2759, 380, 527, 6725, 6896, 4728, 15584, 833, 1080, 1065, 3364, 30, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867840730691258, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204452260558226e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 173278, "start": 1753.74, "end": 1754.7, "text": " It absolutely would.", "tokens": [51413, 467, 3122, 576, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867840730691258, "compression_ratio": 1.55, "no_speech_prob": 2.0204452260558226e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 175470, "start": 1754.7, "end": 1763.18, "text": " How does the physical reality of silicon and magnetic storage handle the theoretical demand of an infinitely expanding append-only documentary history?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 775, 264, 4001, 4103, 295, 22848, 293, 12688, 6725, 4813, 264, 20864, 4733, 295, 364, 36227, 14702, 34116, 12, 25202, 15674, 2503, 30, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13405350276402064, "compression_ratio": 1.3017241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 2.083812289388476e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 176318, "start": 1763.18, "end": 1767.0600000000002, "text": " So, Fliction anticipates this exact operational critique.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 3235, 4105, 10416, 1024, 341, 1900, 16607, 25673, 13, 50559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2024350438799177, "compression_ratio": 1.5446428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201314579471052e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 176318, "start": 1767.0600000000002, "end": 1772.3, "text": " The paper explicitly unvests the tension between logical invariants and physical bounds.", "tokens": [50559, 440, 3035, 20803, 517, 85, 4409, 264, 8980, 1296, 14978, 33270, 1719, 293, 4001, 29905, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2024350438799177, "compression_ratio": 1.5446428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201314579471052e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 176318, "start": 1773.2, "end": 1785.98, "text": " The logical mathematical property of an append-only history does not enforce a requirement that every single byte of payload data must remain forever resident in expensive, high-speed primary memory.", "tokens": [50866, 440, 14978, 18894, 4707, 295, 364, 34116, 12, 25202, 2503, 775, 406, 24825, 257, 11695, 300, 633, 2167, 40846, 295, 30918, 1412, 1633, 6222, 5680, 10832, 294, 5124, 11, 1090, 12, 22746, 6194, 4675, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2024350438799177, "compression_ratio": 1.5446428571428572, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201314579471052e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 178598, "start": 1785.98, "end": 1788.3, "text": " The paper defines hard physical limits.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 23122, 1152, 4001, 10406, 13, 50481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13981778725333835, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554022471721886e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 178598, "start": 1788.78, "end": 1795.42, "text": " It sets a bound for ingress capacity, labeled as B-sub-Q, and a bound for online storage, labeled as B-sub-8.", "tokens": [50505, 467, 6352, 257, 5472, 337, 3957, 735, 6042, 11, 21335, 382, 363, 12, 30131, 12, 48, 11, 293, 257, 5472, 337, 2950, 6725, 11, 21335, 382, 363, 12, 30131, 12, 23, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13981778725333835, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554022471721886e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 178598, "start": 1795.46, "end": 1795.6, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50839, 1779, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13981778725333835, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554022471721886e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 178598, "start": 1795.82, "end": 1800.28, "text": " It acknowledges that when a system hits those physical bounds, it can't just magically expand.", "tokens": [50857, 467, 15195, 2880, 300, 562, 257, 1185, 8664, 729, 4001, 29905, 11, 309, 393, 380, 445, 39763, 5268, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13981778725333835, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554022471721886e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 178598, "start": 1800.44, "end": 1801.74, "text": " It has to manage the state.", "tokens": [51088, 467, 575, 281, 3067, 264, 1785, 13, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13981778725333835, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554022471721886e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 178598, "start": 1801.9, "end": 1804.76, "text": " And this introduces the cryptographic mechanism of compaction.", "tokens": [51161, 400, 341, 31472, 264, 9844, 12295, 7513, 295, 715, 2894, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13981778725333835, "compression_ratio": 1.5616438356164384, "no_speech_prob": 1.7554022471721886e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 180476, "start": 1804.76, "end": 1805.28, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16382505455795598, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.7081665902872754e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 180476, "start": 1805.78, "end": 1812.62, "text": " When a system needs to verify a new proposal, it doesn't need to read the entire infinite history from the Genesis block every single time.", "tokens": [50416, 1133, 257, 1185, 2203, 281, 16888, 257, 777, 11494, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 643, 281, 1401, 264, 2302, 13785, 2503, 490, 264, 20587, 3461, 633, 2167, 565, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16382505455795598, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.7081665902872754e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 180476, "start": 1813.06, "end": 1819.82, "text": " The system can take an older prefix of the documentary history, for example, every record from year 1 to year 1000, and seal it.", "tokens": [50780, 440, 1185, 393, 747, 364, 4906, 46969, 295, 264, 15674, 2503, 11, 337, 1365, 11, 633, 2136, 490, 1064, 502, 281, 1064, 9714, 11, 293, 12185, 309, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16382505455795598, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.7081665902872754e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 180476, "start": 1819.96, "end": 1821.74, "text": " It archives the bulk data to make room.", "tokens": [51125, 467, 25607, 264, 16139, 1412, 281, 652, 1808, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16382505455795598, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.7081665902872754e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 180476, "start": 1822.08, "end": 1822.44, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51231, 1079, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16382505455795598, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.7081665902872754e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 180476, "start": 1822.7, "end": 1826.82, "text": " But it does so in a way that preserves perfect cryptographic continuity.", "tokens": [51262, 583, 309, 775, 370, 294, 257, 636, 300, 1183, 9054, 2176, 9844, 12295, 23807, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16382505455795598, "compression_ratio": 1.5454545454545454, "no_speech_prob": 2.7081665902872754e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 182682, "start": 1826.82, "end": 1839.74, "text": " It moves the heavy bulk data to cold storage, but it leaves behind an authenticated commitment, typically a Merkle root hash, along with the operative state checkpoint at that exact moment, and an observation summary.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 6067, 264, 4676, 16139, 1412, 281, 3554, 6725, 11, 457, 309, 5510, 2261, 364, 9214, 3587, 8371, 11, 5850, 257, 6124, 14677, 5593, 22019, 11, 2051, 365, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 42269, 412, 300, 1900, 1623, 11, 293, 364, 14816, 12691, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10389992531309737, "compression_ratio": 1.6162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250414200726706e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 182682, "start": 1840.34, "end": 1842.3999999999999, "text": " Blysian formalizes this in equation 19.", "tokens": [51041, 363, 44193, 952, 9860, 5660, 341, 294, 5367, 1294, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10389992531309737, "compression_ratio": 1.6162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250414200726706e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 182682, "start": 1843.1799999999998, "end": 1851.6399999999999, "text": " The archive representation retains the root, the state, the summary, and the specific identifiers for the policy bundles that were in effect during that epoch.", "tokens": [51183, 440, 23507, 10290, 1533, 2315, 264, 5593, 11, 264, 1785, 11, 264, 12691, 11, 293, 264, 2685, 2473, 23463, 337, 264, 3897, 13882, 904, 300, 645, 294, 1802, 1830, 300, 30992, 339, 13, 51606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10389992531309737, "compression_ratio": 1.6162790697674418, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250414200726706e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 185164, "start": 1851.64, "end": 1857.4, "text": " So you drastically reduce the physical memory footprint, but you never break the logical chain of custody.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 291, 29673, 5407, 264, 4001, 4675, 24222, 11, 457, 291, 1128, 1821, 264, 14978, 5021, 295, 26976, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09535195909697435, "compression_ratio": 1.6636085626911314, "no_speech_prob": 2.2719090064099445e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 185164, "start": 1857.4, "end": 1865.42, "text": " If a dispute arises 50 years later, you can retrieve the cold storage data, hash it, and prove that it perfectly matches the root left in active memory.", "tokens": [50653, 759, 257, 25379, 27388, 2625, 924, 1780, 11, 291, 393, 30254, 264, 3554, 6725, 1412, 11, 22019, 309, 11, 293, 7081, 300, 309, 6239, 10676, 264, 5593, 1411, 294, 4967, 4675, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09535195909697435, "compression_ratio": 1.6636085626911314, "no_speech_prob": 2.2719090064099445e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 185164, "start": 1865.5800000000002, "end": 1869.76, "text": " You maintain the absolute integrity of the audit trail without melting the active servers.", "tokens": [51062, 509, 6909, 264, 8236, 16000, 295, 264, 17748, 9924, 1553, 20493, 264, 4967, 15909, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09535195909697435, "compression_ratio": 1.6636085626911314, "no_speech_prob": 2.2719090064099445e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 185164, "start": 1869.96, "end": 1870.48, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51281, 48746, 736, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09535195909697435, "compression_ratio": 1.6636085626911314, "no_speech_prob": 2.2719090064099445e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 185164, "start": 1870.9, "end": 1874.2800000000002, "text": " The logic remains unbroken even as the physical medium shifts.", "tokens": [51328, 440, 9952, 7023, 517, 37947, 754, 382, 264, 4001, 6399, 19201, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09535195909697435, "compression_ratio": 1.6636085626911314, "no_speech_prob": 2.2719090064099445e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 185164, "start": 1875.0200000000002, "end": 1881.48, "text": " And this robust historical tracking leads to one of the most conceptually dense and important ideas in the entire text.", "tokens": [51534, 400, 341, 13956, 8584, 11603, 6689, 281, 472, 295, 264, 881, 3410, 671, 18011, 293, 1021, 3487, 294, 264, 2302, 2487, 13, 51857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09535195909697435, "compression_ratio": 1.6636085626911314, "no_speech_prob": 2.2719090064099445e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 188164, "start": 1881.64, "end": 1883.3200000000002, "text": " The continuation space.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 29357, 1901, 13, 50449], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14664946964808873, "compression_ratio": 1.6015037593984962, "no_speech_prob": 1.860643800491446e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 188164, "start": 1883.3200000000002, "end": 1889.76, "text": " Which, flexion denotes mathematically as C, parameterized by H, sigma, and pi.", "tokens": [50449, 3013, 11, 5896, 313, 1441, 17251, 44003, 382, 383, 11, 13075, 1602, 538, 389, 11, 12771, 11, 293, 3895, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14664946964808873, "compression_ratio": 1.6015037593984962, "no_speech_prob": 1.860643800491446e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 188164, "start": 1890.3400000000001, "end": 1896.96, "text": " The continuation space is the theoretical domain of all presently admissible future events.", "tokens": [50800, 440, 29357, 1901, 307, 264, 20864, 9274, 295, 439, 1974, 356, 5910, 41073, 2027, 3931, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14664946964808873, "compression_ratio": 1.6015037593984962, "no_speech_prob": 1.860643800491446e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 188164, "start": 1897.5400000000002, "end": 1903.0400000000002, "text": " Now, to be clear, the paper emphasizes that this isn't a literal pre-calculated list, right?", "tokens": [51160, 823, 11, 281, 312, 1850, 11, 264, 3035, 48856, 300, 341, 1943, 380, 257, 20411, 659, 12, 9895, 2444, 770, 1329, 11, 558, 30, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14664946964808873, "compression_ratio": 1.6015037593984962, "no_speech_prob": 1.860643800491446e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 188164, "start": 1903.0800000000002, "end": 1909.0400000000002, "text": " The system isn't sitting there generating a database of every single thing that could possibly happen in the next 10 minutes.", "tokens": [51437, 440, 1185, 1943, 380, 3798, 456, 17746, 257, 8149, 295, 633, 2167, 551, 300, 727, 6264, 1051, 294, 264, 958, 1266, 2077, 13, 51735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14664946964808873, "compression_ratio": 1.6015037593984962, "no_speech_prob": 1.860643800491446e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 188164, "start": 1909.0800000000002, "end": 1909.76, "text": " It couldn't.", "tokens": [51737, 467, 2809, 380, 13, 51771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14664946964808873, "compression_ratio": 1.6015037593984962, "no_speech_prob": 1.860643800491446e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 190976, "start": 1909.76, "end": 1919.74, "text": " If a system attempted to pre-calculate and lift all possible valid future states based on current variables, the combinatorial explosion would render the list practically infinite.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 1185, 18997, 281, 659, 12, 9895, 2444, 473, 293, 5533, 439, 1944, 7363, 2027, 4368, 2361, 322, 2190, 9102, 11, 264, 2512, 31927, 831, 15673, 576, 15529, 264, 1329, 15667, 13785, 13, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334724667706067, "compression_ratio": 1.5418502202643172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417423840010438e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 190976, "start": 1920.24, "end": 1924.6, "text": " Instead, flexion defines the continuation space as an extensional specification.", "tokens": [50889, 7156, 11, 5896, 313, 23122, 264, 29357, 1901, 382, 364, 1279, 11075, 31256, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334724667706067, "compression_ratio": 1.5418502202643172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417423840010438e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 190976, "start": 1925.44, "end": 1927.8, "text": " The system does not generate proposals in advance.", "tokens": [51149, 440, 1185, 775, 406, 8460, 20198, 294, 7295, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334724667706067, "compression_ratio": 1.5418502202643172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417423840010438e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 190976, "start": 1928.16, "end": 1929.28, "text": " Rather, it waits.", "tokens": [51285, 16571, 11, 309, 40597, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334724667706067, "compression_ratio": 1.5418502202643172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417423840010438e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 190976, "start": 1929.4, "end": 1930.16, "text": " It just sits there.", "tokens": [51347, 467, 445, 12696, 456, 13, 51385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11334724667706067, "compression_ratio": 1.5418502202643172, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417423840010438e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 193016, "start": 1930.16, "end": 1930.88, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13730527999553274, "compression_ratio": 1.6541353383458646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970236843717347e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 193016, "start": 1931.38, "end": 1938.16, "text": " When a specific proposal crosses the ingress boundary and forms in space I, the system subjects it to the admissibility predicate.", "tokens": [50426, 1133, 257, 2685, 11494, 28467, 264, 3957, 735, 12866, 293, 6422, 294, 1901, 286, 11, 264, 1185, 13066, 309, 281, 264, 5910, 891, 2841, 3852, 8700, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13730527999553274, "compression_ratio": 1.6541353383458646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970236843717347e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 193016, "start": 1938.5600000000002, "end": 1941.5600000000002, "text": " The system is essentially answering a precise membership question.", "tokens": [50785, 440, 1185, 307, 4476, 13430, 257, 13600, 16560, 1168, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13730527999553274, "compression_ratio": 1.6541353383458646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970236843717347e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 193016, "start": 1941.76, "end": 1952.24, "text": " Does this specific submitted proposal mathematically belong within the continuation space right now give the exact state of our documentary history, our operative state, and the current policy bundle?", "tokens": [50945, 4402, 341, 2685, 14405, 11494, 44003, 5784, 1951, 264, 29357, 1901, 558, 586, 976, 264, 1900, 1785, 295, 527, 15674, 2503, 11, 527, 2208, 1166, 1785, 11, 293, 264, 2190, 3897, 24438, 30, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13730527999553274, "compression_ratio": 1.6541353383458646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970236843717347e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 193016, "start": 1952.3600000000001, "end": 1952.78, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51475, 7587, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13730527999553274, "compression_ratio": 1.6541353383458646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970236843717347e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 193016, "start": 1952.94, "end": 1953.8600000000001, "text": " It's a membership test.", "tokens": [51504, 467, 311, 257, 16560, 1500, 13, 51550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13730527999553274, "compression_ratio": 1.6541353383458646, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970236843717347e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 195386, "start": 1953.86, "end": 1959.84, "text": " Let me ask a clarifying question about the mechanics of this because this touches on how systems evolve over time.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 385, 1029, 257, 6093, 5489, 1168, 466, 264, 12939, 295, 341, 570, 341, 17431, 322, 577, 3652, 16693, 670, 565, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09169954913003105, "compression_ratio": 1.4261363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179299211829036e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 195386, "start": 1960.06, "end": 1960.1799999999998, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [50675, 4894, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09169954913003105, "compression_ratio": 1.4261363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179299211829036e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 195386, "start": 1960.52, "end": 1967.4599999999998, "text": " If the boundaries of the continuation space are heavily dictated by the current policy bundle, what happens when the rules change?", "tokens": [50698, 759, 264, 13180, 295, 264, 29357, 1901, 366, 10950, 12569, 770, 538, 264, 2190, 3897, 24438, 11, 437, 2314, 562, 264, 4474, 1319, 30, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09169954913003105, "compression_ratio": 1.4261363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179299211829036e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 196746, "start": 1967.46, "end": 1973.24, "text": " Let's say a new administration takes over the Ministry of Possible Affairs and they update the policy bundle.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 584, 257, 777, 7236, 2516, 670, 264, 19720, 295, 430, 5785, 21721, 293, 436, 5623, 264, 3897, 24438, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14705145011827783, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883083472918337e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 196746, "start": 1973.64, "end": 1977.4, "text": " They add a strict new rule that invalidates certain types of proposals.", "tokens": [50674, 814, 909, 257, 10910, 777, 4978, 300, 34702, 1024, 1629, 3467, 295, 20198, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14705145011827783, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883083472918337e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 196746, "start": 1977.4, "end": 1986.14, "text": " Does the system have to go back in time and scrub the documentary history to delete all the old records that violate the new rule?", "tokens": [50862, 4402, 264, 1185, 362, 281, 352, 646, 294, 565, 293, 24163, 264, 15674, 2503, 281, 12097, 439, 264, 1331, 7724, 300, 37478, 264, 777, 4978, 30, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14705145011827783, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883083472918337e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 196746, "start": 1986.24, "end": 1986.88, "text": " Absolutely not.", "tokens": [51304, 7021, 406, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14705145011827783, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883083472918337e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 196746, "start": 1987.28, "end": 1993.76, "text": " Altering the past to conform to present policy would categorically violate the immutability of the documentary history track.", "tokens": [51356, 32608, 278, 264, 1791, 281, 18975, 281, 1974, 3897, 576, 19250, 984, 37478, 264, 3397, 325, 2310, 295, 264, 15674, 2503, 2837, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14705145011827783, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883083472918337e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 196746, "start": 1993.96, "end": 1994.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51690, 1779, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14705145011827783, "compression_ratio": 1.7011070110701108, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883083472918337e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 199406, "start": 1994.06, "end": 1999.3, "text": " Flickstun addresses this temporal shift through the concept of narrowing interventions.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 618, 372, 409, 16862, 341, 30881, 5513, 807, 264, 3410, 295, 9432, 278, 20924, 13, 50627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11374457195551708, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858775881047449e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 199406, "start": 2000.2, "end": 2007.5, "text": " When an authority updates a policy bundle or adds a new restrictive rule, that intervention does not reach backward to alter the past.", "tokens": [50672, 1133, 364, 8281, 9205, 257, 3897, 24438, 420, 10860, 257, 777, 43220, 4978, 11, 300, 13176, 775, 406, 2524, 23897, 281, 11337, 264, 1791, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11374457195551708, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858775881047449e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 199406, "start": 2007.82, "end": 2011.44, "text": " It simply shrinks the geometry of the continuation space going forward.", "tokens": [51053, 467, 2935, 9884, 16431, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 29357, 1901, 516, 2128, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11374457195551708, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858775881047449e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 199406, "start": 2011.54, "end": 2013.72, "text": " The text is extremely precise on this point.", "tokens": [51239, 440, 2487, 307, 4664, 13600, 322, 341, 935, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11374457195551708, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858775881047449e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 199406, "start": 2013.98, "end": 2020.8799999999999, "text": " It states mathematically that an event being absent from the operative history does not imply it is absent from the recorded history.", "tokens": [51361, 467, 4368, 44003, 300, 364, 2280, 885, 25185, 490, 264, 2208, 1166, 2503, 775, 406, 33616, 309, 307, 25185, 490, 264, 8287, 2503, 13, 51706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11374457195551708, "compression_ratio": 1.72, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858775881047449e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 202088, "start": 2020.88, "end": 2024.42, "text": " So an event can be rendered entirely obsolete by a new policy.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 364, 2280, 393, 312, 28748, 7696, 46333, 538, 257, 777, 3897, 13, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18006329536437987, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042200762916072e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 202088, "start": 2025.0200000000002, "end": 2032.8200000000002, "text": " It can become mathematically impossible to execute in the current operative reality, but its historical record remains perfectly intact in the archive.", "tokens": [50572, 467, 393, 1813, 44003, 6243, 281, 14483, 294, 264, 2190, 2208, 1166, 4103, 11, 457, 1080, 8584, 2136, 7023, 6239, 23493, 294, 264, 23507, 13, 50962], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18006329536437987, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042200762916072e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 202088, "start": 2033.2, "end": 2033.48, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50981, 1079, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18006329536437987, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042200762916072e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 202088, "start": 2034.0400000000002, "end": 2037.5600000000002, "text": " Persistence fundamentally precedes operative truth.", "tokens": [51023, 14006, 468, 655, 17879, 16969, 279, 2208, 1166, 3494, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18006329536437987, "compression_ratio": 1.5055555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.8042200762916072e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 203756, "start": 2037.56, "end": 2051.02, "text": " A distinction, a rejected proposal, or a rule that was valid for a brief window can survive as structural information long before or even without ever being selected to become part of the operative reality.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 16844, 11, 257, 15749, 11494, 11, 420, 257, 4978, 300, 390, 7363, 337, 257, 5353, 4910, 393, 7867, 382, 15067, 1589, 938, 949, 420, 754, 1553, 1562, 885, 8209, 281, 1813, 644, 295, 264, 2208, 1166, 4103, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10184300223062205, "compression_ratio": 1.4206896551724137, "no_speech_prob": 2.0562776741755995e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 205102, "start": 2051.02, "end": 2068.54, "text": " It's like analyzing the discarded drafts of a constitutional document or the transcripts of a failed legislative session.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 411, 23663, 264, 45469, 11206, 82, 295, 257, 20176, 4166, 420, 264, 24444, 82, 295, 257, 7612, 21331, 5481, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24235072502723107, "compression_ratio": 1.2222222222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582822776559317e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 206854, "start": 2068.54, "end": 2077.84, "text": " Those drafts aren't the operative law, but they tell you exactly what the architects of the system were afraid of, what they debated, and where they drew the lines at that specific moment in history.", "tokens": [50365, 3950, 11206, 82, 3212, 380, 264, 2208, 1166, 2101, 11, 457, 436, 980, 291, 2293, 437, 264, 30491, 295, 264, 1185, 645, 4638, 295, 11, 437, 436, 42212, 11, 293, 689, 436, 12804, 264, 3876, 412, 300, 2685, 1623, 294, 2503, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10121631622314453, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555658532800167e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 206854, "start": 2077.96, "end": 2078.44, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50836, 7587, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10121631622314453, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555658532800167e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 206854, "start": 2078.74, "end": 2081.24, "text": " The refusals define the shape of the resulting law.", "tokens": [50875, 440, 1895, 301, 1124, 6964, 264, 3909, 295, 264, 16505, 2101, 13, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10121631622314453, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555658532800167e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 206854, "start": 2081.48, "end": 2084.14, "text": " Okay, we've journeyed deep into the mechanics of these three layers.", "tokens": [51012, 1033, 11, 321, 600, 4671, 292, 2452, 666, 264, 12939, 295, 613, 1045, 7914, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10121631622314453, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555658532800167e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 208414, "start": 2084.14, "end": 2098.22, "text": " When we pull back and look at the progression from Go to Pearl to Rust, Fliction seems to be making a much larger, cohesive argument that the fundamental architecture of a system inescapably dictates its relationship with power.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 321, 2235, 646, 293, 574, 412, 264, 18733, 490, 1037, 281, 24639, 281, 34952, 11, 3235, 4105, 2544, 281, 312, 1455, 257, 709, 4833, 11, 43025, 6770, 300, 264, 8088, 9482, 295, 257, 1185, 294, 279, 9485, 1188, 12569, 1024, 1080, 2480, 365, 1347, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11743165006731997, "compression_ratio": 1.5964285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.897336454614873e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 208414, "start": 2098.48, "end": 2101.24, "text": " That is the ultimate synthesis of Fliction's work.", "tokens": [51082, 663, 307, 264, 9705, 30252, 295, 3235, 4105, 311, 589, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11743165006731997, "compression_ratio": 1.5964285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.897336454614873e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 208414, "start": 2101.66, "end": 2110.72, "text": " The paper argues that the choice of language for each of the three executable witnesses wasn't merely a technical convenience, it was a profound rhetorical fit.", "tokens": [51241, 440, 3035, 38218, 300, 264, 3922, 295, 2856, 337, 1184, 295, 264, 1045, 7568, 712, 20217, 2067, 380, 17003, 257, 6191, 19283, 11, 309, 390, 257, 14382, 24182, 284, 804, 3318, 13, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11743165006731997, "compression_ratio": 1.5964285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.897336454614873e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 208414, "start": 2110.8399999999997, "end": 2111.06, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51700, 1779, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11743165006731997, "compression_ratio": 1.5964285714285715, "no_speech_prob": 1.897336454614873e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 211106, "start": 2111.06, "end": 2115.68, "text": " Go was chosen for its operational legibility and capability reduction.", "tokens": [50365, 1037, 390, 8614, 337, 1080, 16607, 1676, 2841, 293, 13759, 11004, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460834371632543, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310920933875316e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 211106, "start": 2116.68, "end": 2121.52, "text": " Pearl was chosen for its generative, textural ability to mock bureaucratic absurdity.", "tokens": [50646, 24639, 390, 8614, 337, 1080, 1337, 1166, 11, 2487, 1807, 3485, 281, 17362, 26360, 25198, 19774, 507, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460834371632543, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310920933875316e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 211106, "start": 2122.42, "end": 2127.06, "text": " Rust was chosen for its obsessive, structural enforcement of historical state transitions.", "tokens": [50933, 34952, 390, 8614, 337, 1080, 35803, 488, 11, 15067, 11475, 295, 8584, 1785, 23767, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460834371632543, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310920933875316e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 211106, "start": 2127.06, "end": 2131.52, "text": " The programming languages themselves actively participate in the philosophical argument.", "tokens": [51165, 440, 9410, 8650, 2969, 13022, 8197, 294, 264, 25066, 6770, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460834371632543, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310920933875316e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 211106, "start": 2131.82, "end": 2138.08, "text": " And a crucial architectural decision that binds all three programs together is their absolute rejection of dependency accumulation.", "tokens": [51403, 400, 257, 11462, 26621, 3537, 300, 41515, 439, 1045, 4268, 1214, 307, 641, 8236, 26044, 295, 33621, 35647, 13, 51716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1460834371632543, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310920933875316e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 213808, "start": 2138.08, "end": 2142.7, "text": " None of these programs rely on massive, external, third-party libraries.", "tokens": [50365, 14492, 295, 613, 4268, 10687, 322, 5994, 11, 8320, 11, 2636, 12, 23409, 15148, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10951558430989583, "compression_ratio": 1.545045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.973639134067451e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 213808, "start": 2142.7, "end": 2145.14, "text": " Fliction calls this an epistemic choice.", "tokens": [50596, 3235, 4105, 5498, 341, 364, 2388, 468, 3438, 3922, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10951558430989583, "compression_ratio": 1.545045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.973639134067451e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 213808, "start": 2145.86, "end": 2159.08, "text": " By refusing external dependencies, the architecture forces anyone auditing the code to trace the entire logical path from raw input all the way to final ruling, without having the core mechanics obscured by a black box framework.", "tokens": [50754, 3146, 37289, 8320, 36606, 11, 264, 9482, 5874, 2878, 2379, 1748, 264, 3089, 281, 13508, 264, 2302, 14978, 3100, 490, 8936, 4846, 439, 264, 636, 281, 2572, 21437, 11, 1553, 1419, 264, 4965, 12939, 22082, 3831, 538, 257, 2211, 2424, 8388, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10951558430989583, "compression_ratio": 1.545045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.973639134067451e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 215908, "start": 2159.08, "end": 2160.7, "text": " Inspectability is not a byproduct.", "tokens": [50365, 29552, 2310, 307, 406, 257, 538, 33244, 13, 50446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23048625980411563, "compression_ratio": 1.9391304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045779071757749e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 215908, "start": 2160.7, "end": 2161.04, "text": " Inspectability is not a byproduct.", "tokens": [50446, 29552, 2310, 307, 406, 257, 538, 33244, 13, 50463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23048625980411563, "compression_ratio": 1.9391304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045779071757749e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 215908, "start": 2161.46, "end": 2163.54, "text": " It is the intended architectural result.", "tokens": [50484, 467, 307, 264, 10226, 26621, 1874, 13, 50588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23048625980411563, "compression_ratio": 1.9391304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045779071757749e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 215908, "start": 2164.08, "end": 2169.98, "text": " And this deep inspectability culminates in the final grand categorical inequality of the paper.", "tokens": [50615, 400, 341, 2452, 15018, 2310, 28583, 1024, 294, 264, 2572, 2697, 19250, 804, 16970, 295, 264, 3035, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23048625980411563, "compression_ratio": 1.9391304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045779071757749e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 215908, "start": 2170.24, "end": 2170.9, "text": " Equation 55.", "tokens": [50923, 15624, 399, 12330, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23048625980411563, "compression_ratio": 1.9391304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045779071757749e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 215908, "start": 2171.22, "end": 2171.4, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50972, 1079, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23048625980411563, "compression_ratio": 1.9391304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045779071757749e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 215908, "start": 2171.5, "end": 2172.22, "text": " Equation 55.", "tokens": [50986, 15624, 399, 12330, 13, 51022], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23048625980411563, "compression_ratio": 1.9391304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045779071757749e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 215908, "start": 2172.6, "end": 2176.08, "text": " And it acts as the master key for the entire theoretical framework.", "tokens": [51041, 400, 309, 10672, 382, 264, 4505, 2141, 337, 264, 2302, 20864, 8388, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23048625980411563, "compression_ratio": 1.9391304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045779071757749e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 215908, "start": 2177.2, "end": 2184.56, "text": " Existence does not equal recording, which does not equal admission, which does not equal continuation, which does not equal external effect.", "tokens": [51271, 2111, 468, 655, 775, 406, 2681, 6613, 11, 597, 775, 406, 2681, 24668, 11, 597, 775, 406, 2681, 29357, 11, 597, 775, 406, 2681, 8320, 1802, 13, 51639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23048625980411563, "compression_ratio": 1.9391304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045779071757749e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 218456, "start": 2184.56, "end": 2188.34, "text": " That one equation maps the entire hidden bureaucracy we've been talking about.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 472, 5367, 11317, 264, 2302, 7633, 44671, 321, 600, 668, 1417, 466, 13, 50554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1242799273991989, "compression_ratio": 1.9016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2182041359980476e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 218456, "start": 2188.44, "end": 2189.56, "text": " Walk me through it one more time.", "tokens": [50559, 10818, 385, 807, 309, 472, 544, 565, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1242799273991989, "compression_ratio": 1.9016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2182041359980476e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 218456, "start": 2189.88, "end": 2194.2999999999997, "text": " A proposed event can exist in the universe without ever being recorded by the ingress operator.", "tokens": [50631, 316, 10348, 2280, 393, 2514, 294, 264, 6445, 1553, 1562, 885, 8287, 538, 264, 3957, 735, 12973, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1242799273991989, "compression_ratio": 1.9016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2182041359980476e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 218456, "start": 2194.66, "end": 2198.7999999999997, "text": " It can be recorded in the documentary history without ever being admitted into the operative state.", "tokens": [50870, 467, 393, 312, 8287, 294, 264, 15674, 2503, 1553, 1562, 885, 14920, 666, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1242799273991989, "compression_ratio": 1.9016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2182041359980476e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 218456, "start": 2199.06, "end": 2202.88, "text": " It can be admitted into the local operative state without continuing the global timeline.", "tokens": [51090, 467, 393, 312, 14920, 666, 264, 2654, 2208, 1166, 1785, 1553, 9289, 264, 4338, 12933, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1242799273991989, "compression_ratio": 1.9016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2182041359980476e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 218456, "start": 2203.48, "end": 2208.9, "text": " And it can continue the timeline locally without ever having an authorized external effect on the outside world.", "tokens": [51311, 400, 309, 393, 2354, 264, 12933, 16143, 1553, 1562, 1419, 364, 28312, 8320, 1802, 322, 264, 2380, 1002, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1242799273991989, "compression_ratio": 1.9016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2182041359980476e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 218456, "start": 2209.24, "end": 2211.7999999999997, "text": " It dismantles the equivalency illusion perfectly.", "tokens": [51599, 467, 30506, 904, 264, 9052, 3020, 18854, 6239, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1242799273991989, "compression_ratio": 1.9016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2182041359980476e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 221180, "start": 2211.8, "end": 2219.28, "text": " Fliction ties all of these distinct layers together under the unifying concept of safe power through bounded effect.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 14039, 439, 295, 613, 10644, 7914, 1214, 833, 264, 517, 5489, 3410, 295, 3273, 1347, 807, 37498, 1802, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12528014183044434, "compression_ratio": 1.5899581589958158, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827675100057228e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 221180, "start": 2219.92, "end": 2225.5800000000004, "text": " These three small programs demonstrate how software can instantiate profound restraint.", "tokens": [50771, 1981, 1045, 1359, 4268, 11698, 577, 4722, 393, 9836, 13024, 14382, 49281, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12528014183044434, "compression_ratio": 1.5899581589958158, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827675100057228e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 221180, "start": 2226.04, "end": 2230.86, "text": " The Pearl Ministry script can compute universe-altering bureaucratic judgments,", "tokens": [51077, 440, 24639, 19720, 5755, 393, 14722, 6445, 12, 304, 34200, 26360, 25198, 40337, 11, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12528014183044434, "compression_ratio": 1.5899581589958158, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827675100057228e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 221180, "start": 2231.36, "end": 2236.5, "text": " but it structurally lacks the system permissions to actually alter the host machine it runs on.", "tokens": [51343, 457, 309, 6594, 6512, 31132, 264, 1185, 32723, 281, 767, 11337, 264, 3975, 3479, 309, 6676, 322, 13, 51600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12528014183044434, "compression_ratio": 1.5899581589958158, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827675100057228e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 223650, "start": 2236.5, "end": 2241.56, "text": " Right, and the Rust program can simulate complex causal histories and temporal rules,", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 293, 264, 34952, 1461, 393, 27817, 3997, 38755, 30631, 293, 30881, 4474, 11, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14735136836408133, "compression_ratio": 1.5826771653543308, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689002389589814e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 223650, "start": 2241.72, "end": 2245.22, "text": " but it only mutates its own isolated-in-memory state.", "tokens": [50626, 457, 309, 787, 5839, 1024, 1080, 1065, 14621, 12, 259, 12, 17886, 827, 1785, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14735136836408133, "compression_ratio": 1.5826771653543308, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689002389589814e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 223650, "start": 2245.74, "end": 2250.04, "text": " Their restraint is architectural, not merely promised by a terms-of-service agreement.", "tokens": [50827, 6710, 49281, 307, 26621, 11, 406, 17003, 10768, 538, 257, 2115, 12, 2670, 12, 39279, 8106, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14735136836408133, "compression_ratio": 1.5826771653543308, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689002389589814e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 223650, "start": 2250.54, "end": 2255.18, "text": " They grant themselves exactly enough computational power to execute their conceptual claim", "tokens": [51067, 814, 6386, 2969, 2293, 1547, 28270, 1347, 281, 14483, 641, 24106, 3932, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14735136836408133, "compression_ratio": 1.5826771653543308, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689002389589814e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 223650, "start": 2255.18, "end": 2260.08, "text": " while actively mathematically withholding the ability to cause external consequence.", "tokens": [51299, 1339, 13022, 44003, 48867, 278, 264, 3485, 281, 3082, 8320, 18326, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14735136836408133, "compression_ratio": 1.5826771653543308, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689002389589814e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 226008, "start": 2260.08, "end": 2264.52, "text": " So bringing this all the way back down to Earth, why does this matter to you, the listener,", "tokens": [50365, 407, 5062, 341, 439, 264, 636, 646, 760, 281, 4755, 11, 983, 775, 341, 1871, 281, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12828176211466832, "compression_ratio": 1.6351791530944626, "no_speech_prob": 2.289458770135533e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 226008, "start": 2264.7599999999998, "end": 2267.08, "text": " who is just trying to navigate their digital life?", "tokens": [50599, 567, 307, 445, 1382, 281, 12350, 641, 4562, 993, 30, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12828176211466832, "compression_ratio": 1.6351791530944626, "no_speech_prob": 2.289458770135533e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 226008, "start": 2267.36, "end": 2270.9, "text": " It matters because it redefines what we should demand from the technology we use.", "tokens": [50729, 467, 7001, 570, 309, 38818, 1652, 437, 321, 820, 4733, 490, 264, 2899, 321, 764, 13, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12828176211466832, "compression_ratio": 1.6351791530944626, "no_speech_prob": 2.289458770135533e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 226008, "start": 2271.56, "end": 2276.06, "text": " Building trustworthy software, or even just being an informed citizen in a digital world,", "tokens": [50939, 18974, 39714, 4722, 11, 420, 754, 445, 885, 364, 11740, 13326, 294, 257, 4562, 1002, 11, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12828176211466832, "compression_ratio": 1.6351791530944626, "no_speech_prob": 2.289458770135533e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 226008, "start": 2276.4, "end": 2278.94, "text": " isn't just about demanding that a program works correctly.", "tokens": [51181, 1943, 380, 445, 466, 19960, 300, 257, 1461, 1985, 8944, 13, 51308], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12828176211466832, "compression_ratio": 1.6351791530944626, "no_speech_prob": 2.289458770135533e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 226008, "start": 2279.2999999999997, "end": 2281.88, "text": " Correct execution is the absolute bare minimum.", "tokens": [51326, 12753, 15058, 307, 264, 8236, 6949, 7285, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12828176211466832, "compression_ratio": 1.6351791530944626, "no_speech_prob": 2.289458770135533e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 226008, "start": 2282.06, "end": 2283.06, "text": " Right. True.", "tokens": [51464, 1779, 13, 13587, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12828176211466832, "compression_ratio": 1.6351791530944626, "no_speech_prob": 2.289458770135533e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 226008, "start": 2283.54, "end": 2286.96, "text": " Trustworthy architecture is about explicitly programming restraint.", "tokens": [51538, 11580, 23727, 9482, 307, 466, 20803, 9410, 49281, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12828176211466832, "compression_ratio": 1.6351791530944626, "no_speech_prob": 2.289458770135533e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 228696, "start": 2286.96, "end": 2292.54, "text": " It is about demanding to know what the system refuses, how it structures its policy bundles,", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 466, 19960, 281, 458, 437, 264, 1185, 33222, 11, 577, 309, 9227, 1080, 3897, 13882, 904, 11, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11930667543874203, "compression_ratio": 1.6654411764705883, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936951797064014e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 228696, "start": 2292.96, "end": 2297.32, "text": " and demanding that the system keeps the cryptographic receipts when it says no.", "tokens": [50665, 293, 19960, 300, 264, 1185, 5965, 264, 9844, 12295, 2268, 48908, 562, 309, 1619, 572, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11930667543874203, "compression_ratio": 1.6654411764705883, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936951797064014e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 228696, "start": 2297.84, "end": 2302.98, "text": " Because the shape of our digital world isn't just defined by the conveniences computers provide for us,", "tokens": [50909, 1436, 264, 3909, 295, 527, 4562, 1002, 1943, 380, 445, 7642, 538, 264, 7158, 14004, 10807, 2893, 337, 505, 11, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11930667543874203, "compression_ratio": 1.6654411764705883, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936951797064014e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 228696, "start": 2303.1, "end": 2307.6, "text": " it is defined rigorously and silently by the boundaries they enforce against us.", "tokens": [51172, 309, 307, 7642, 42191, 5098, 293, 40087, 538, 264, 13180, 436, 24825, 1970, 505, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11930667543874203, "compression_ratio": 1.6654411764705883, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936951797064014e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 228696, "start": 2307.66, "end": 2309.2400000000002, "text": " It is a profound paradigm shift.", "tokens": [51400, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 24709, 5513, 13, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11930667543874203, "compression_ratio": 1.6654411764705883, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936951797064014e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 228696, "start": 2309.7200000000003, "end": 2313.54, "text": " It moves us from viewing software simply as a utilitarian tool", "tokens": [51503, 467, 6067, 505, 490, 17480, 4722, 2935, 382, 257, 4976, 13707, 2290, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11930667543874203, "compression_ratio": 1.6654411764705883, "no_speech_prob": 2.7936951797064014e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 231354, "start": 2313.54, "end": 2316.96, "text": " to recognizing software as a highly formalized governance structure.", "tokens": [50365, 281, 18538, 4722, 382, 257, 5405, 9860, 1602, 17449, 3877, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13213097795527032, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.4457400080862834e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 231354, "start": 2317.2, "end": 2320.14, "text": " And what a massive journey this paper took us on to prove that point.", "tokens": [50548, 400, 437, 257, 5994, 4671, 341, 3035, 1890, 505, 322, 281, 7081, 300, 935, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13213097795527032, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.4457400080862834e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 231354, "start": 2320.44, "end": 2324.3, "text": " We started by looking at how a tiny Go program sets severe operational boundaries", "tokens": [50710, 492, 1409, 538, 1237, 412, 577, 257, 5870, 1037, 1461, 6352, 8922, 16607, 13180, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13213097795527032, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.4457400080862834e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 231354, "start": 2324.3, "end": 2327.94, "text": " and refuses to hit SIN automatically, enforcing contextual integrity.", "tokens": [50903, 293, 33222, 281, 2045, 318, 1464, 6772, 11, 25495, 2175, 35526, 16000, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13213097795527032, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.4457400080862834e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 231354, "start": 2328.2599999999998, "end": 2333.86, "text": " We watched a Perl script brilliantly satirize the dangerous, highly consequential gap", "tokens": [51101, 492, 6337, 257, 3026, 75, 5755, 8695, 42580, 3227, 347, 1125, 264, 5795, 11, 5405, 7242, 2549, 7417, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13213097795527032, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.4457400080862834e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 231354, "start": 2333.86, "end": 2338.38, "text": " between procedural determinism and actual justified legitimacy.", "tokens": [51381, 1296, 43951, 15957, 1434, 293, 3539, 27808, 41339, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13213097795527032, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.4457400080862834e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 233838, "start": 2338.38, "end": 2343.52, "text": " And we explored how a Rust program separates an immutable, append-only documentary history", "tokens": [50365, 400, 321, 24016, 577, 257, 34952, 1461, 34149, 364, 3397, 32148, 11, 34116, 12, 25202, 15674, 2503, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11196041929310765, "compression_ratio": 1.628930817610063, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086943377354952e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 233838, "start": 2343.52, "end": 2348.48, "text": " from the highly selective, narrowly defined, operative reality we actually experience.", "tokens": [50622, 490, 264, 5405, 33930, 11, 9432, 356, 7642, 11, 2208, 1166, 4103, 321, 767, 1752, 13, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11196041929310765, "compression_ratio": 1.628930817610063, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086943377354952e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 233838, "start": 2348.82, "end": 2352.4, "text": " It provides us with a totally new, highly rigorous vocabulary", "tokens": [50887, 467, 6417, 505, 365, 257, 3879, 777, 11, 5405, 29882, 19864, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11196041929310765, "compression_ratio": 1.628930817610063, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086943377354952e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 233838, "start": 2352.4, "end": 2355.62, "text": " for analyzing the digital infrastructure around us.", "tokens": [51066, 337, 23663, 264, 4562, 6896, 926, 505, 13, 51227], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11196041929310765, "compression_ratio": 1.628930817610063, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086943377354952e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 233838, "start": 2356.12, "end": 2359.6, "text": " The next time you interact with a corporate workflow tool that grays out the submit button,", "tokens": [51252, 440, 958, 565, 291, 4648, 365, 257, 10896, 20993, 2290, 300, 677, 3772, 484, 264, 10315, 2960, 11, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11196041929310765, "compression_ratio": 1.628930817610063, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086943377354952e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 233838, "start": 2360.02, "end": 2361.88, "text": " or a banking app that denies a transfer,", "tokens": [51447, 420, 257, 18261, 724, 300, 1441, 530, 257, 5003, 11, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11196041929310765, "compression_ratio": 1.628930817610063, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086943377354952e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 233838, "start": 2362.2200000000003, "end": 2365.4, "text": " or a social media platform that silently quarantines a post,", "tokens": [51557, 420, 257, 2093, 3021, 3663, 300, 40087, 41240, 1652, 257, 2183, 11, 51716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11196041929310765, "compression_ratio": 1.628930817610063, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086943377354952e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 233838, "start": 2366.02, "end": 2367.6, "text": " you can dissect the interaction.", "tokens": [51747, 291, 393, 48332, 264, 9285, 13, 51826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11196041929310765, "compression_ratio": 1.628930817610063, "no_speech_prob": 2.4086943377354952e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 236760, "start": 2367.6, "end": 2372.14, "text": " You can ask yourself, which specific mathematical boundary did I just hit?", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 1029, 1803, 11, 597, 2685, 18894, 12866, 630, 286, 445, 2045, 30, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179833049922026, "compression_ratio": 1.5823529411764705, "no_speech_prob": 1.804237423526367e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 236760, "start": 2372.48, "end": 2375.56, "text": " Was it an ingress failure where my signal was never even recognized?", "tokens": [50609, 3027, 309, 364, 3957, 735, 7763, 689, 452, 6358, 390, 1128, 754, 9823, 30, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179833049922026, "compression_ratio": 1.5823529411764705, "no_speech_prob": 1.804237423526367e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 236760, "start": 2376.08, "end": 2379.98, "text": " Or was my proposal formally recorded, judged against a hidden policy bundle,", "tokens": [50789, 1610, 390, 452, 11494, 25983, 8287, 11, 27485, 1970, 257, 7633, 3897, 24438, 11, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179833049922026, "compression_ratio": 1.5823529411764705, "no_speech_prob": 1.804237423526367e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 236760, "start": 2380.3399999999997, "end": 2381.4, "text": " and denied continuation?", "tokens": [51002, 293, 17774, 29357, 30, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179833049922026, "compression_ratio": 1.5823529411764705, "no_speech_prob": 1.804237423526367e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 236760, "start": 2381.7599999999998, "end": 2386.2799999999997, "text": " And crucially, where does that system keep the documentary record of that refusal?", "tokens": [51073, 400, 5140, 1909, 11, 689, 775, 300, 1185, 1066, 264, 15674, 2136, 295, 300, 48948, 30, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179833049922026, "compression_ratio": 1.5823529411764705, "no_speech_prob": 1.804237423526367e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 236760, "start": 2386.6, "end": 2390.38, "text": " Exactly. It completely changes how you see the invisible walls of the internet.", "tokens": [51315, 7587, 13, 467, 2584, 2962, 577, 291, 536, 264, 14603, 7920, 295, 264, 4705, 13, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179833049922026, "compression_ratio": 1.5823529411764705, "no_speech_prob": 1.804237423526367e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 236760, "start": 2390.7599999999998, "end": 2392.54, "text": " And before we wrap up this deep dive,", "tokens": [51523, 400, 949, 321, 7019, 493, 341, 2452, 9192, 11, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179833049922026, "compression_ratio": 1.5823529411764705, "no_speech_prob": 1.804237423526367e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 236760, "start": 2392.74, "end": 2396.44, "text": " I want to leave you with one final, slightly chilling thought to mull over.", "tokens": [51622, 286, 528, 281, 1856, 291, 365, 472, 2572, 11, 4748, 31047, 1194, 281, 275, 858, 670, 13, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179833049922026, "compression_ratio": 1.5823529411764705, "no_speech_prob": 1.804237423526367e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 236760, "start": 2396.6, "end": 2397.08, "text": " Oh, here we go.", "tokens": [51815, 876, 11, 510, 321, 352, 13, 51839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12179833049922026, "compression_ratio": 1.5823529411764705, "no_speech_prob": 1.804237423526367e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 239708, "start": 2397.08, "end": 2400.68, "text": " It's an extrapolation that builds directly on Fluxian's architecture,", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 364, 48224, 399, 300, 15182, 3838, 322, 3235, 2449, 952, 311, 9482, 11, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18352563413855147, "compression_ratio": 1.5087719298245614, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540676806344525e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 239708, "start": 2401.02, "end": 2402.72, "text": " but points toward our immediate future.", "tokens": [50562, 457, 2793, 7361, 527, 11629, 2027, 13, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18352563413855147, "compression_ratio": 1.5087719298245614, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540676806344525e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 239708, "start": 2403.58, "end": 2406.42, "text": " We've established today, mathematically and conceptually,", "tokens": [50690, 492, 600, 7545, 965, 11, 44003, 293, 3410, 671, 11, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18352563413855147, "compression_ratio": 1.5087719298245614, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540676806344525e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 239708, "start": 2406.56, "end": 2410.64, "text": " that rejected proposals remain incredibly valuable as structural evidence.", "tokens": [50839, 300, 15749, 20198, 6222, 6252, 8263, 382, 15067, 4467, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18352563413855147, "compression_ratio": 1.5087719298245614, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540676806344525e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 239708, "start": 2411.34, "end": 2417.74, "text": " The graveyard of refusals maps the exact boundaries of what a system considers an acceptable reality.", "tokens": [51078, 440, 42607, 295, 1895, 301, 1124, 11317, 264, 1900, 13180, 295, 437, 257, 1185, 33095, 364, 15513, 4103, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18352563413855147, "compression_ratio": 1.5087719298245614, "no_speech_prob": 1.8540676806344525e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 241774, "start": 2417.74, "end": 2421.3399999999997, "text": " The refusals define the perimeter of the continuation space.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1895, 301, 1124, 6964, 264, 32404, 295, 264, 29357, 1901, 13, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1956282977400155, "compression_ratio": 1.4886363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 1.8793193997529434e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 241774, "start": 2421.3399999999997, "end": 2428.9199999999996, "text": " Right. So, if our modern, hyper-skilled software systems are unconditionally recording every single rejected proposal,", "tokens": [50545, 1779, 13, 407, 11, 498, 527, 4363, 11, 9848, 12, 5161, 6261, 4722, 3652, 366, 34959, 15899, 6613, 633, 2167, 15749, 11494, 11, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1956282977400155, "compression_ratio": 1.4886363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 1.8793193997529434e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 241774, "start": 2429.4599999999996, "end": 2434.02, "text": " every malformed request, every denied loan application, every quarantined message,", "tokens": [50951, 633, 2806, 22892, 5308, 11, 633, 17774, 10529, 3861, 11, 633, 41240, 2001, 3636, 11, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1956282977400155, "compression_ratio": 1.4886363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 1.8793193997529434e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 243402, "start": 2434.02, "end": 2437.46, "text": " every behavioral outlier that the system flagged and stopped.", "tokens": [50365, 633, 19124, 484, 2753, 300, 264, 1185, 7166, 3004, 293, 5936, 13, 50537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2059803307056427, "compression_ratio": 1.2477064220183487, "no_speech_prob": 2.084587927622672e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 243402, "start": 2437.46, "end": 2442.52, "text": " They are building an unimaginably massive archive of failed continuations.", "tokens": [50537, 814, 366, 2390, 364, 517, 44976, 1188, 5994, 23507, 295, 7612, 2993, 763, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2059803307056427, "compression_ratio": 1.2477064220183487, "no_speech_prob": 2.084587927622672e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 244252, "start": 2442.52, "end": 2444.12, "text": " Okay. I see where you're going with this.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 286, 536, 689, 291, 434, 516, 365, 341, 13, 50445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12237391105064979, "compression_ratio": 1.34640522875817, "no_speech_prob": 1.5398661078885878e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 244252, "start": 2444.12, "end": 2448.82, "text": " How long until massive AI systems start looking at that documentary history of refusals,", "tokens": [50445, 1012, 938, 1826, 5994, 7318, 3652, 722, 1237, 412, 300, 15674, 2503, 295, 1895, 301, 1124, 11, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12237391105064979, "compression_ratio": 1.34640522875817, "no_speech_prob": 1.5398661078885878e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 244252, "start": 2449.02, "end": 2453.28, "text": " not just as static audit evidence, but as primary high-value training data?", "tokens": [50690, 406, 445, 382, 13437, 17748, 4467, 11, 457, 382, 6194, 1090, 12, 29155, 3097, 1412, 30, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12237391105064979, "compression_ratio": 1.34640522875817, "no_speech_prob": 1.5398661078885878e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 245328, "start": 2453.28, "end": 2455.6800000000003, "text": " It fundamentally shifts the training paradigm.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 17879, 19201, 264, 3097, 24709, 13, 50485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860693613688151, "compression_ratio": 1.4344827586206896, "no_speech_prob": 2.048260866471807e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 245328, "start": 2456.2400000000002, "end": 2458.38, "text": " Instead of learning how to mimic successful outputs,", "tokens": [50513, 7156, 295, 2539, 577, 281, 31075, 4406, 23930, 11, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860693613688151, "compression_ratio": 1.4344827586206896, "no_speech_prob": 2.048260866471807e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 245328, "start": 2458.46, "end": 2460.82, "text": " a model trained on the documentary history of refusals", "tokens": [50624, 257, 2316, 8895, 322, 264, 15674, 2503, 295, 1895, 301, 1124, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860693613688151, "compression_ratio": 1.4344827586206896, "no_speech_prob": 2.048260866471807e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 245328, "start": 2460.82, "end": 2463.7200000000003, "text": " learns the exact contour of institutional boundaries.", "tokens": [50742, 27152, 264, 1900, 21234, 295, 18391, 13180, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1860693613688151, "compression_ratio": 1.4344827586206896, "no_speech_prob": 2.048260866471807e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 246372, "start": 2463.72, "end": 2469.8799999999997, "text": " It learns exactly what the system fears, what it rejects, and how it defines an invalid reality.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 27152, 2293, 437, 264, 1185, 15649, 11, 437, 309, 8248, 82, 11, 293, 577, 309, 23122, 364, 34702, 4103, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13451391855875652, "compression_ratio": 1.7482758620689656, "no_speech_prob": 2.020628239382538e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 246372, "start": 2469.8999999999996, "end": 2470.2599999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50674, 7587, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13451391855875652, "compression_ratio": 1.7482758620689656, "no_speech_prob": 2.020628239382538e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 246372, "start": 2470.48, "end": 2472.3999999999996, "text": " And what happens when a machine learning model,", "tokens": [50703, 400, 437, 2314, 562, 257, 3479, 2539, 2316, 11, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13451391855875652, "compression_ratio": 1.7482758620689656, "no_speech_prob": 2.020628239382538e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 246372, "start": 2472.7799999999997, "end": 2475.02, "text": " trained on billions of meticulous rejections,", "tokens": [50818, 8895, 322, 17375, 295, 41566, 6893, 8248, 626, 11, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13451391855875652, "compression_ratio": 1.7482758620689656, "no_speech_prob": 2.020628239382538e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 246372, "start": 2475.3599999999997, "end": 2478.3599999999997, "text": " begins to autonomously update the policy bundles?", "tokens": [50947, 7338, 281, 18203, 5098, 5623, 264, 3897, 13882, 904, 30, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13451391855875652, "compression_ratio": 1.7482758620689656, "no_speech_prob": 2.020628239382538e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 246372, "start": 2478.98, "end": 2482.7799999999997, "text": " What happens when it uses that massive graveyard of failed continuations", "tokens": [51128, 708, 2314, 562, 309, 4960, 300, 5994, 42607, 295, 7612, 2993, 763, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13451391855875652, "compression_ratio": 1.7482758620689656, "no_speech_prob": 2.020628239382538e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 246372, "start": 2482.7799999999997, "end": 2486.06, "text": " to redefine the rules of the ingress operator itself?", "tokens": [51318, 281, 38818, 533, 264, 4474, 295, 264, 3957, 735, 12973, 2564, 30, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13451391855875652, "compression_ratio": 1.7482758620689656, "no_speech_prob": 2.020628239382538e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 246372, "start": 2486.24, "end": 2489.54, "text": " When the machine learns more from our refusals than our successes,", "tokens": [51491, 1133, 264, 3479, 27152, 544, 490, 527, 1895, 301, 1124, 813, 527, 26101, 11, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13451391855875652, "compression_ratio": 1.7482758620689656, "no_speech_prob": 2.020628239382538e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 246372, "start": 2490.14, "end": 2493.04, "text": " who is really setting the boundaries of the continuation space?", "tokens": [51686, 567, 307, 534, 3287, 264, 13180, 295, 264, 29357, 1901, 30, 51831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13451391855875652, "compression_ratio": 1.7482758620689656, "no_speech_prob": 2.020628239382538e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 249304, "start": 2493.04, "end": 2496.9, "text": " When the AI decides what even constitutes a well-formed proposal,", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 264, 7318, 14898, 437, 754, 44204, 257, 731, 12, 22892, 11494, 11, 50558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15442609053391676, "compression_ratio": 1.71656050955414, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362760956571524e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 249304, "start": 2497.62, "end": 2500.7, "text": " it gains the power to decide what parts of human behavior", "tokens": [50594, 309, 16823, 264, 1347, 281, 4536, 437, 3166, 295, 1952, 5223, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15442609053391676, "compression_ratio": 1.71656050955414, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362760956571524e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 249304, "start": 2500.7, "end": 2503.0, "text": " are allowed to exist in the digital record at all.", "tokens": [50748, 366, 4350, 281, 2514, 294, 264, 4562, 2136, 412, 439, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15442609053391676, "compression_ratio": 1.71656050955414, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362760956571524e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 249304, "start": 2503.4, "end": 2506.46, "text": " It's the ultimate centralization of the ingress operator.", "tokens": [50883, 467, 311, 264, 9705, 5777, 2144, 295, 264, 3957, 735, 12973, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15442609053391676, "compression_ratio": 1.71656050955414, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362760956571524e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 249304, "start": 2506.96, "end": 2509.52, "text": " The system wouldn't just be governing the operative reality,", "tokens": [51061, 440, 1185, 2759, 380, 445, 312, 30054, 264, 2208, 1166, 4103, 11, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15442609053391676, "compression_ratio": 1.71656050955414, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362760956571524e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 249304, "start": 2509.68, "end": 2512.66, "text": " it would be preemptively defining the limits of existence.", "tokens": [51197, 309, 576, 312, 659, 4543, 3413, 17827, 264, 10406, 295, 9123, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15442609053391676, "compression_ratio": 1.71656050955414, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362760956571524e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 249304, "start": 2512.98, "end": 2514.94, "text": " Think about all those things your computer almost did,", "tokens": [51362, 6557, 466, 439, 729, 721, 428, 3820, 1920, 630, 11, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15442609053391676, "compression_ratio": 1.71656050955414, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362760956571524e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 249304, "start": 2515.04, "end": 2518.94, "text": " those denied requests, those blocked actions, those silent refusals.", "tokens": [51465, 729, 17774, 12475, 11, 729, 15470, 5909, 11, 729, 12784, 1895, 301, 1124, 13, 51660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15442609053391676, "compression_ratio": 1.71656050955414, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362760956571524e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 249304, "start": 2519.06, "end": 2519.86, "text": " They aren't gone.", "tokens": [51666, 814, 3212, 380, 2780, 13, 51706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15442609053391676, "compression_ratio": 1.71656050955414, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362760956571524e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 249304, "start": 2520.32, "end": 2522.04, "text": " They are sitting in the documentary history,", "tokens": [51729, 814, 366, 3798, 294, 264, 15674, 2503, 11, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15442609053391676, "compression_ratio": 1.71656050955414, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362760956571524e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 252204, "start": 2522.04, "end": 2524.06, "text": " mapping the edges of our reality,", "tokens": [50365, 18350, 264, 8819, 295, 527, 4103, 11, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16947588776097153, "compression_ratio": 1.2, "no_speech_prob": 2.0355381876585588e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 252204, "start": 2524.6, "end": 2525.82, "text": " just waiting in the margins.", "tokens": [50493, 445, 3806, 294, 264, 30317, 13, 50554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16947588776097153, "compression_ratio": 1.2, "no_speech_prob": 2.0355381876585588e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 252204, "start": 2526.4, "end": 2528.98, "text": " Until next time, thanks for taking the deep dive with us.", "tokens": [50583, 9088, 958, 565, 11, 3231, 337, 1940, 264, 2452, 9192, 365, 505, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16947588776097153, "compression_ratio": 1.2, "no_speech_prob": 2.0355381876585588e-12}], "language": "en"}
